(window.GAMES = window.GAMES || {})[2004] = [{"t":".hack//Quarantine Part 4","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"January 14"},{"t":".kkrieger","p":["Windows"],"r":"April","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/.kkrieger"},{"t":"2 Fast 2 Furious","p":["Mobile phone"],"g":"Racing, Arcade","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2_Fast_2_Furious_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co5kk8.jpg","s":"2 Fast 2 Furious ups the ante of racing games with total 3D action on your phone. Based on the monster sequel to The Fast and The Furious, you are a tough street racer making your money on the sweltering streets of Miami. In your customized nitro-powered vehicle you have to take out the contenders to your crown and keep winning to make your car unstoppable. Featuring characters from the movie including TEJ, who'll be on hand to help you along the way."},{"t":"2nd Super Robot Wars","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"December 16","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2nd_Super_Robot_Wars"},{"t":"A Sound of Thunder","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"d":"Möbius Entertainment","u":"BAM! Entertainment","g":"Action-adventure","r":"February 28, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A_Sound_of_Thunder_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2zxn.jpg","s":"Based on the Franchise Pictures movie of the same name, A Sound of Thunder takes you to a future where time travel is possible. Things quickly go wrong when someone alters the past, creating a sequence of time ripples that mutate the present-day world. Now you must solve the mystery and sort out a mess that just might mean the end of human existence.\n\nYou'll solve puzzles, manipulate items, interact with other characters, and eliminate mutant creatures and plants. In addition to a single-player mode, the game features both cooperative and competitive multiplayer modes."},{"t":"Ace Combat 5: The Unsung War","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"October 25"},{"t":"Advance Guardian Heroes","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"September 14","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Advance_Guardian_Heroes"},{"t":"Adventure Island","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"May 21","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adventure_Island_(video_game)"},{"t":"Airforce Delta Strike","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Konami Computer Entertainment Studios","u":"Konami","g":"Flight simulator","r":"February 3, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Airforce_Delta_Strike","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co6lyz.jpg","s":"Fly with the 1st, 2nd, and 3rd Element squadrons as you defend country and, eventually, Earth itself from attack. Pilot aircraft that span sixty years of aviation including WWII prop planes, Korean War jets, rare prototypes, and even aircraft from previous Konami games like the Vic Viper and TwinBee.\n\nBetween missions you can explore the base and talk to wingmates, buy new aircraft and special weapons, modify or repaint existing aircraft, and get mission briefings. Missions can have varied objectives, but any enemy crafts shot down will reward money used to buy, modify, and repair aircraft. While Ken Thomas is the main character of the game, other pilots can be used in missions as the game progresses, and using them can open up bonus missions as well as alter the story. The player can only play as Delta Squadron pilots, but the story is told from the perspective of both E.D.A.F.'s Delta Squadron and their O.C.C. Ace counterparts. Medals are awarded to each pilot as they reach milestones, such as number of enemy aces shot down or number of aircraft purchased."},{"t":"Akai Ito","p":["PlayStation 2","Windows"],"d":"Success Corporation","u":"Success Corporation, Hamster","g":"Visual novel, adventure, horror, yuri","r":"October 21, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Akai_Ito_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co6lg6.jpg","s":"A Japan-only adventure-horror game published by Success Corp.\n\nThe story is about a girl named Hatou Kei who, as a result of a dead mother, heads to her father's house in order to claim her inheritance. However, she soon finds herself caught up in supernatural happenings after a dream concerning a huge tree and a mysterious girl..."},{"t":"Alexander","p":["Windows"],"d":"GSC Game World","u":"Ubisoft","g":"Real-time strategy","r":"November 23, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexander_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1ywx.jpg","s":"Alexander is an RTS based on the movie of the same same, and the real-life Alexander the Great. The game follows the same general path as the movie, and includes media straight from the film. Present in the game are Greek, Persian, Indian and Egyptian forces, with a campaign for each. The hybrid 2D/3D engine (2D units, 3D terrain - also used in Cossacks 2: Napoleonic Wars) allows for a very large number of troops on the field. This is used to good effect, as battles can easily contain hundreds of units. Finally, multiplayer and skirmish levels are available, and the soundtrack (of the game and the movie) is by the composer Vangelis."},{"t":"Alias","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"g":"Adventure, Casual, Indie, RPG","r":"April 5","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alias_(video_game)","i":"images/steam-3092710.jpg","s":"Alia’s Chronicles is a puzzle-narrative game where you play as Neniu, a semi-elf on his quest for identity. Every action you take impacts the story! Craft tools, use your powers to solve puzzles, and prove yourself to the inhabitants of this enchanting world."},{"t":"Alida","p":["Windows","macOS"],"d":"Dejavu Worlds","u":"Got Game Entertainment","g":"Adventure","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alida_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co9jby.jpg","s":"Your adventure begins when you’re secretly dropped off on the island of Alida. The story centers around four young men in the band Alida who attained phenomenal success with their first CD release. Loads of money coupled with wild imagination resulted in the band’s construction of a guitar-shaped island theme park. Alida was abandoned when money woes and paranoia set in and the band split up. Now, several years later, the band’s manager suggests a reunion on the island. Soon thereafter band member Arin leaves for the island and is not heard from again. His wife Julia sends you to Alida to find Arin and bring him home."},{"t":"Alien Arena","p":["Windows","macOS","Linux"],"d":"COR Entertainment, LLC","g":"First-person shooter","r":"October 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alien_Arena"},{"t":"Alien Hominid","p":["GameCube"],"r":"November 23","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alien_Hominid"},{"t":"Alien Sky","p":["Windows"],"d":"KraiSoft Entertainment","u":"KraiSoft Entertainment, Oberon Media","g":"Fixed shooter","r":"March 8, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alien_Sky","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4r1t.jpg","s":"It's not easy to survive under the alien sky when there's always someone to burst you with his weaponry or overcome with his tactics. However you have to. Cause you and your ultramodern space-fighter are the only chance to prevent alien invasion which is almost ready to start, turning your homeworld into ruins."},{"t":"All Grown Up!: Express Yourself","p":["PlayStation 2","GameCube","Game Boy Advance"],"r":"October 19"},{"t":"All-Star Baseball 2005","p":["Xbox","PlayStation 2"],"r":"March 23","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/All-Star_Baseball_2005"},{"t":"Alpha Black Zero: Intrepid Protocol","p":["Windows"],"d":"Khaeon","u":"Playlogic","g":"Tactical shooter","r":"July 30, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alpha_Black_Zero:_Intrepid_Protocol","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1yrs.jpg","s":"Alpha Black Zero is a fast-paced mission-based 3rd person tactical shooter with a gripping storyline to test both your fighting abilities and your intelligence. Dozens of different enemies, all possessing strong artificial intelligence will punish your mistakes across huge and challenging levels."},{"t":"Alteil","p":["Browser"],"d":"Dex Entertainment Inc.","u":"Apocoplay LLC, Media Blasters Interactive","g":"Card game","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alteil"},{"t":"Amazing Island","p":["GameCube"],"r":"August 25","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amazing_Island"},{"t":"AMF Xtreme Bowling 3D","p":["Mobile phone"],"d":"Quicksilver Software, Vir2L Studios","u":"Superscape","g":"Sports","r":"June 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AMF_Xtreme_Bowling_3D"},{"t":"Animamundi: Dark Alchemist","p":["Windows"],"d":"Karin Entertainment","u":"Hirameki International","g":"Visual novel","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Animamundi:_Dark_Alchemist","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/coa58j.jpg","s":"A visual novel developed by Karin Entertainment and published by Hirameki in the US."},{"t":"Ao Oni","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ao_Oni"},{"t":"Ape Escape Academy","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"d":"Shift, Alvion","u":"Sony Computer Entertainment","g":"Party","r":"December 30, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ape_Escape_Academy","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co5dym.jpg","s":"Ape Escape Academy sees you taking on the role of one of the cheeky monkeys from the Ape Escape series. Choose your chimp, then prepare to tackle various classes in Academy Mode. Each 'class' is actually a mini-game. Your goal is to complete as many mini-games as possible from the 9x9 grid, and score as many lines as you can (sort of like Noughts and Crosses). Mini-games range from mind-bending quizzes to wacky sports games, to the just plain silly, like protecting a roast banana from oncoming apes, or flying through the sky delivering parachutes to plummeting primates."},{"t":"Ape Escape: Pumped & Primed","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"October 20"},{"t":"Arena Wars","p":["Windows"],"d":"exDream","u":"Ascaron Entertainment, Tri Synergy","g":"Action, real-time strategy","r":"July 16, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arena_Wars","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/xxifyunu3wakc51v0mby.jpg","s":"Arena Wars is a completely new kind of 3D Real Time Strategy game, combining the gameplay principles and interface from RTS games with the fast pace of action-based shooters. Arena Wars is a single and multiplayer game.\n\nMultiplayer supports up to 8 players, who can fight against each other and challenge other players from all around the world via the AW Server, whilst the single player mode is loaded with action-packed single player missions against one or more computer opponents.\n\nThere are 3 different game modes: Capture the Flag, Bombing Run and Double Domination. In AW the goal is not simply to destroy the enemy's base or units. To score points in the various scenarios you must complete objectives that range from stealing the enemy flag, carrying a bomb into your enemy's base or seize and hold Domination zones for a period of time. The winner is the player who satisfies that particular game's objectives. For example, in a Capture the Flag game with a 'capture limit' of 5, the winner is the first player to capture 5 enemy flags."},{"t":"Armies of Exigo","p":["Windows"],"r":"November 30","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Armies_of_Exigo"},{"t":"Armored Core: Nexus","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"September 28"},{"t":"Army Men: Sarge's War","p":["Windows","Xbox","PlayStation 2","GameCube"],"d":"Tactical Development","u":"Global Star Software","g":"Third-person shooter","r":"July 20, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Army_Men:_Sarge's_War","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co45jc.jpg","s":"Army Men: Sarge's War is a 2004 game in the Army Men video game series. It was initially developed by series creator The 3DO Company but after that company's bankruptcy was purchased and completed by Global Star Software. The game is more mature and darker than earlier games in the series. Sarge makes no comical moves, holes are blown into soldiers, and the weapons are also made of metal."},{"t":"Around the World in 80 Days","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"July 5","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Around_the_World_in_80_Days_(video_game)"},{"t":"Ashen","p":["N-Gage"],"d":"Torus Games","u":"Nokia","g":"First-person shooter","r":"May 25, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ashen_(2004_video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3aiw.jpg","s":"Ashen is a supernatural horror-themed FPS developed exclusively for the N-Gage platform. When Seven River City is plunged into chaos, stricken by storms and overcome with supernatural phenomena, Jacob Ward is filled with dread and despair, like most others. Yet Ward knows more about this catastrophe than most, and as its citizens flee, he must return to Seven River City and work to save it. Somewhere in that half-ruined darkness is his sister, a woman Ward believes is responsible for this disaster; a woman who warned him this would happen."},{"t":"Asphalt Urban GT","p":["Nintendo DS"],"r":"November 17","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Asphalt_Urban_GT"},{"t":"Astro Battle","p":["Windows","Linux"],"d":"Lava Lord Games","u":"Self Published","g":"Multidirectional shooter","r":"December 31, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Astro_Battle"},{"t":"Astro Boy","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Sonic Team","u":"Sega","g":"Action","r":"April 18, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Astro_Boy_(2004_video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co6y4r.jpg","s":"An action sandbox game by Sonic Team with emphasis on aerial combat and vertical movement. Do not confuse with the 2009 sidescrolling game based on the movie."},{"t":"Astro Boy: Omega Factor","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"August 18"},{"t":"AstroPop","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox","Browser","Windows","Xbox 360","Mobile phone"],"d":"PopCap Games","u":"PopCap Games, Sorrent","g":"Puzzle","r":"April 6, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AstroPop","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/l0sjfnmvl0cxdp8gnfy6.jpg"},{"t":"Atelier Iris: Eternal Mana","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Gust Co. Ltd.","u":"Gust Co. Ltd., NIS America, Koei, THQ","g":"Role-playing","r":"May 27, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atelier_Iris:_Eternal_Mana","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2vvy.jpg","s":"Atelier Iris: Eternal Mana is a Turn-Based RPG and with alchemy gameplay and story components. It is the 6th core Atelier game and the first game in the Iris series, being the first Ateleir game to be released internationally.\n\nThe game follows the young alchemist Klein Kiesling, who is travelling to learn more about alchemy together with his friend, the Wood Mana, Popo. One day, he is saved from a monster by Lita Blanchimont, a young Galgazit, monster hunter. Lita eventually recruits him to become an Galgazit as well, and they start working together in the town of Kavoc. However, Klein is soon caught in many troubles, and eventually becomes involved in a quest of saving both the world and Lita."},{"t":"Athens 2004","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"July 14","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Athens_2004_(video_game)"},{"t":"Atlantis Evolution","p":["Windows"],"d":"Atlantis Interactive Entertainment","u":"The Adventure Company","g":"Adventure","r":"October 15, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atlantis_Evolution"},{"t":"Attack of the Mutant Artificial Trees","p":["Browser"],"d":"Blockdot","u":"Kewlbox","g":"Action","r":"November 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Attack_of_the_Mutant_Artificial_Trees","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co5wwr.jpg","s":"A free online video game developed as part of a marketing campaign by the National Christmas Tree Association in 2004. The game was meant to support the natural Christmas tree industry and received criticism from artificial tree producers. It has been described as similar to Whac-A-Mole."},{"t":"ATV Offroad Fury 3","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Climax Racing, Climax LA","u":"Sony Computer Entertainment, SouthPeak Interactive","g":"Racing","r":"November 2, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ATV_Offroad_Fury_3","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co22yr.jpg","s":"ATV Offroad Fury 3 gives players intense, free-roaming offroad racing! Playable from both first- and third-person perspectives, with all-new modes of play. Race in more than 30 unique environments with six distinct terrain types including snow, dirt, mud, ice, water and grass, as well as compete in eight exciting mini-games!"},{"t":"Audition Online","p":["Windows"],"d":"T3 Entertainment","u":"YD Online, Hanbitsoft","g":"Music video game and MMOG","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Audition_Online","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3i9w.jpg","s":"Audition Online, is a downloadable multiplayer online casual rhythm game produced by T3 Entertainment. It was originally released in South Korea in 2004, but it has been localized by various publishers around the world. Audition Online is free to play but it earns its revenue by selling virtual items such as clothes for the player's avatar."},{"t":"Aura: Fate of the Ages","p":["Windows"],"d":"Streko-Graphics Inc.","u":"The Adventure Company","g":"Adventure","r":"June 24, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aura:_Fate_of_the_Ages","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1qli.jpg","s":"'In the hallways of the ancients, the Keepers have existed forever.' The legend also claims that whoever unites these rings with the artifacts of the parallel worlds will achieve great power and immortality."},{"t":"Axis & Allies","p":["Windows"],"d":"TimeGate Studios","u":"Atari","g":"Real-time strategy","r":"November 2, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Axis_&_Allies_(2004_video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co8bkr.jpg","s":"A WWII real-time-strategy game based on the popular board game and Timegate Studios previous game series, Kokan."},{"t":"Backyard Wrestling 2: There Goes the Neighborhood","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"Paradox Development","u":"Eidos Interactive","g":"Fighting","r":"November 16, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Backyard_Wrestling_2:_There_Goes_the_Neighborhood","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co9852.jpg","s":"Backyard Wrestling 2: There Goes the Neighborhood is the second installment in the Backyard Wrestling series and was released on Xbox and PlayStation 2. The licensed soundtrack includes music by Andrew W.K., Kool Keith, the Insane Clown Posse, Bad Brains, Body Count, Six and Violence, Mudvayne, Saliva, Fall Out Boy, and Hoobastank. It was developed by Paradox Development, now owned by Midway Games, and was published by Eidos Interactive.\n\nThe television commercial included Insane Clown Posse, Vampiro, New Jack, and Major Gunns. Despite promises of an improved gameplay experience, the game was a critical flop when released in 2004. Its sales numbers remained respectable, however, moving nearly 300,000 copies through 2005."},{"t":"Bad Boys: Miami Takedown","p":["GameCube","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"September 14"},{"t":"Baldur's Gate: Dark Alliance II","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"Black Isle Studios","u":"Interplay Entertainment","g":"Action role-playing, hack and slash","r":"January 20, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baldur's_Gate:_Dark_Alliance_II","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1tb2.jpg","s":"Using the 3rd Edition Dungeons & Dragons rules set, Baldur's Gate: Dark Alliance II features four new acts of hack-and-slash combat and powerful spell casting. Even more monster types will engage in real-time battles using the same overhead perspective as witnessed in the original game. Each selected character can parlay the experience gained from combat into acquiring new feats and enhanced abilities over time. To help in battle, a new item creation system lets players craft magical weapons and armor using raw materials found during their travels.\n\nAs before, two heroes can join the adventure in cooperative play on the same screen, with each character differing in the types of feats and powers under his or her command. Equipment can be found or purchased from local merchants using the gold looted from felled creatures or received as payment for quests. Baldur's Gate: Dark Alliance II also features a number of hidden areas, secret characters, and literally hundreds of items to find and use, including potions, scrolls, and wands. In addition, the game features a new branching storyline that offers players a choice where to go next for fortune and honor."},{"t":"Ballance","p":["Windows"],"d":"Cyparade","u":"Atari Europe, Ziggurat Interactive","g":"Puzzle","r":"April 2, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ballance_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co9trv.jpg","s":"In Ballance, you control a sphere with the simple objective of navigating it to the end of each of the game's 12 linear levels. Expect surreal environments as you transform between three different materials to push boxes, spheres, and other objects to clear a path towards the end. Pre-placed \"Transformers\" will turn your ball into either Paper, Wood, or Stone, each with their own downsides and advantages.\n\nPaper can, for example, use gusts of wind to reach higher elevations, fall slower than the other materials, and get around quickly. Stone may be required to push heavy materials, but, due to its immense weight, will experience different issues when trying to navigate environments. Wood is the neutral material of choice: it rolls reliably and quickly, allowing it to stick to sideways railing while still being able to push objects of a medium density."},{"t":"Balloon Fight","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"May 21","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Balloon_Fight"},{"t":"Bankshot Billiards","p":["Windows"],"d":"pixelStorm entertainment","u":"Oberon Media","r":"October 7, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bankshot_Billiards"},{"t":"Barbie as the Princess and the Pauper","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"September 12","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barbie_as_the_Princess_and_the_Pauper"},{"t":"Baten Kaitos: Eternal Wings and the Lost Ocean","p":["GameCube"],"r":"November 18"},{"t":"Battlefield Vietnam","p":["Windows"],"r":"March 14","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battlefield_Vietnam"},{"t":"Beatmania IIDX 10th Style","p":["Arcade","PlayStation 2"],"d":"Konami Computer Entertainment Tokyo","u":"Konami","g":"Music","r":"February 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beatmania_IIDX_10th_Style","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2hmb.jpg"},{"t":"Beatmania IIDX 7th Style","p":["Arcade","PlayStation 2"],"d":"Konami, Konami Computer Entertainment Studio","u":"Konami, Konami Computer Entertainment Studio","g":"Music","r":"March 13, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beatmania_IIDX_7th_Style"},{"t":"Beatmania IIDX 8th Style","p":["Arcade","PlayStation 2"],"d":"Konami, Konami Computer Entertainment Studio","u":"Konami","g":"Music","r":"November 18, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beatmania_IIDX_8th_Style"},{"t":"Before Crisis: Final Fantasy VII","p":["Mobile phone"],"d":"Square Enix","u":"Square Enix","g":"Action role-playing game","r":"September 24, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Before_Crisis:_Final_Fantasy_VII","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2yuo.jpg","s":"Before Crisis: Final Fantasy VII is a Japanese action role-playing game developed and published by Square Enix in 2004. It is the prequel to Final Fantasy VII, taking place during the six years prior to it. Before Crisis was the first original (i.e. not an enhanced remake) game Square Enix produced for mobile phones."},{"t":"Bejeweled 2","p":["Windows"],"r":"November 5","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bejeweled_2"},{"t":"Ben Jordan: Paranormal Investigator","p":["Windows"],"d":"Grundislav Games","u":"Grundislav Games","g":"Point-and-click adventure","r":"May 27, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ben_Jordan:_Paranormal_Investigator","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2kko.jpg","s":"Ben Jordan: Paranormal Investigator is a freeware episodic point-and-click adventure video game for Microsoft Windows developed by Francisco Gonzalez of Grundislav Games. The game consists of eight individual episodes, or cases, with an overarching plot connecting them together."},{"t":"Ben's Game","p":["Windows","macOS"],"d":"Eric Johnston","u":"Make-A-Wish Foundation","g":"Action","r":"May 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ben's_Game","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co7khs.jpg","s":"This is a game about fighting cancer. In this game, you play the role of a hero on a hovering surfboard with ultra-high-tech weapons. You are the cure!"},{"t":"Berserk: Millennium Falcon Hen Seima Senki no Shō","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Yuke's","u":"Sammy Corporation","g":"Action-adventure","r":"October 7, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Berserk:_Millennium_Falcon_Hen_Seima_Senki_no_Sh%C5%8D"},{"t":"Beyond Divinity","p":["Windows"],"g":"RPG","r":"April 27","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beyond_Divinity","i":"images/steam-219760.jpg","s":"Beyond Divinity is the follow-up to the award-winning Divine Divinity."},{"t":"Bicycle Casino","p":["Xbox"],"d":"Leaping Lizard Software","u":"Activision Value","g":"Gambling","r":"October 26, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bicycle_Casino_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/db3warw9vqwbzd6b5ttd.jpg","s":"Bring the fun, glitz and action of casino gaming into your living room. Step up to the table and place bets or pull the handle of slot machines in 500 different game variations. Put your money down and hope Lady Luck is on your side for fast paced gaming action. Bicycle casino puts you into an authentic casino environment, enables you to create your own customized character and turns you loose out onto the gaming floor. The gameplay options are virtually endless, with table games that include: poker, blackjack, roulette, craps, and more. Play the popular poker variation that is sweeping the nation, \"texas hold'em\", and see if you have the right poker face to win big. If you are more into the one-armed bandits, pull the handle on the three different variations of slot machines and hope you hit the jackpot. Challenge your friends to multiplayer gaming via Xbox Live for even more bicycle casino thrills."},{"t":"Big Kahuna Reef","p":["Windows"],"d":"Reflexive Entertainment","u":"Reflexive Entertainment","g":"Puzzle","r":"December 22, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Big_Kahuna_Reef","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/eq682bmchpqhjxg76308.jpg"},{"t":"Bike or Die!","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bike_or_Die!"},{"t":"Blinx 2: Masters of Time and Space","p":["Xbox"],"r":"November 18"},{"t":"Block Breaker Deluxe","p":["N-Gage","Windows","Mobile phone"],"d":"Gameloft Romania","g":"Breakout clone","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Block_Breaker_Deluxe","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/coc4j3.jpg","s":"Prepare for the frenzy of the coolest block-breaker game ever. Block Breaker Deluxe is a reinvention of the classic arcade brick-breaker game with a trendy graphical style, fun atmosphere and an exclusive multiplayer mode. Lively characters and amazing graphics provide distinctive settings of the jet-set nightlife, including a cool bar, dance club, casino and more. Special bricks, multiple bonuses, secret weapons, paddle size options and ball-speed variations make this fascinating game even more challenging. The Block Breaker Deluxe rage has arrived."},{"t":"Blockland","p":["Windows"],"d":"Eric \"Badspot\" Hartman, Anthony \"Rotondo\" Rotondo, Ben \"kompressor\" Garney","u":"Step 1 Games LLC & Blockland LLC","g":"Sandbox","r":"November 15, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blockland_(video_game)"},{"t":"Blood Will Tell","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"September 21","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blood_Will_Tell"},{"t":"BloodRayne 2","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"October 14","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BloodRayne_2"},{"t":"Blue Chairs","p":["Windows"],"d":"Chris Klimas","u":"Chris Klimas","g":"Interactive fiction","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_Chairs","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co6ye8.jpg","s":"A surrealist piece of interactive fiction by Chris Klimas about a man who is offered a hallucinatory drug at a party."},{"t":"Bobby Carrot","p":["Mobile phone"],"d":"FDG Mobile Games","u":"FDG Mobile Games","g":"Puzzle","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bobby_Carrot","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co8udz.jpg","s":"Bobby Carrot is a puzzle game for mobile phones starring a rabbit who has to solve dangerous challenges in order to catch all of the carrots in each stage to progress. \nIt is the first game in the Bobby Carrot series."},{"t":"Boktai 2: Solar Boy Django","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"October 19"},{"t":"Bomberman","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"February 14","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bomberman_(1983_video_game)"},{"t":"Bomberman Hardball","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Hudson Soft","u":"Hudson Soft, Ubisoft","g":"Party, puzzle","r":"October 7, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bomberman_Hardball","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4yix.jpg","s":"Bomberman Hardball is divided into four games. Battle mode (the standard Bomberman game), is joined by tennis, golf and baseball games. At the center of all this is the Living mode, a character building feature in which the player can design a Bomberman for use in any of the battle modes.\n\nBattle Mode is the centerpiece of this and all other Bomberman games. This mode is essentially the standard Bomberman formula; in the game, players navigate grid-based mazes, planting bombs in an attempt to hit other players (while avoided being hit by a bomb themselves). There are several different variations of Battle Mode, although they all center around the standard Bomberman gameplay.\n\nClassic Battle: A standard deathmatch-type game.\nStar Battle: Collect the most stars.\nCrown Battle: Find the crown in the level to win the game.\nPoint Battle: Earn the most points by killing opponents\nReplay: Watched game sessions saved to memory card."},{"t":"Bos Wars","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bos_Wars"},{"t":"BreakQuest","p":["Windows"],"d":"Nurium Games, Beatshapers","u":"Stardock, Nurium Games, Red Marble Games, Beatshapers","g":"Breakout clone","r":"November 15, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BreakQuest","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co70pj.jpg","s":"A huge corporation rules the world by making thousands of TV channels and shows for people to watch. Everyone becomes addicted, starting the destruction of human intelligence. The player has to put up a transmitter to stop the satellite signals and end the corporation's rule."},{"t":"Breed","p":["Windows"],"d":"Brat Designs","u":"CDV Software","g":"Tactical shooter, tactical wargame","r":"March 19, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Breed_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3uye.jpg","s":"In Breed, you must take control of a squad of soldiers and win 18 different missions. They take place on tropical islands, Antarctica and even outer space. There is a variety of vehicles including tanks, buggies and fighter jets, ensuring that a range of control skills must be mastered. Everything you see can be blown up, with weapons including plasma guns, assault rifles and grenades."},{"t":"Bujingai","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"July 22","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bujingai"},{"t":"Burnout 3: Takedown","p":["Xbox","PlayStation 2"],"u":"Electronic Arts","r":"September 8, 2004"},{"t":"Bush vs. Kerry Boxing","p":["Mobile phone"],"d":"Sorrent","u":"Sorrent","g":"Boxing","r":"August 22, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bush_vs._Kerry_Boxing"},{"t":"Cabela's Big Game Hunter 2005 Adventures","p":["Windows","Xbox","PlayStation 2","GameCube","Game Boy Advance"],"d":"Magic Wand Productions, Torus Games","u":"Activision Value, Zoo Digital Publishing","g":"First-person shooter, sports","r":"September 9, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cabela's_Big_Game_Hunter_2005_Adventures"},{"t":"Cabela's Deer Hunt: 2005 Season","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"Sand Grain Studios, Magic Wand Productions, Fun Labs","u":"Activision Value","g":"Sports","r":"August 31, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cabela's_Deer_Hunt:_2005_Season","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/m8fsl0kcr3q7ah3gcrvu.jpg","s":"Cabela's Deer Hunt: 2005 Season is the first sequel to Cabela's Deer Hunt: 2004 Season. It was developed by Sand Grain Studios (PlayStation 2), Magic Wand Productions (Windows) and FUN Labs (Xbox) and released on August 31, 2004. \n \nThe game was published by Activision, in conjunction with hunting supply company Cabela's."},{"t":"Call of Duty: Finest Hour","p":["GameCube","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"Spark Unlimited","u":"Activision","g":"First-person shooter","r":"November 16, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Call_of_Duty:_Finest_Hour","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3b6a.jpg","s":"\"Call of Duty: Finest Hour\" is an immersive first-person shooter set against the dramatic backdrop of World War II. Developed by Spark Unlimited and published by Activision, this installment transports players to the heart of historic battles across multiple fronts. Experience the intensity of warfare through the eyes of American, British, and Soviet soldiers, each with unique missions and storylines."},{"t":"Call of Duty: United Offensive","p":["Windows"],"g":"Action","r":"September 14","l":"https://store.steampowered.com/app/2640","i":"images/steam-2640.jpg","s":"Award-winning developer Gray Matter Interactive follows up on the success of Infinity Ward's Call of Duty™ - winner of over 80 Game of the Year and 50 Editors' Choice awards worldwide - with Call of Duty™: United Offensive™."},{"t":"Canvas 2: Akane-iro no Palette","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canvas_2:_Akane-iro_no_Palette"},{"t":"Care Bears: A Lesson in Caring","p":["V.Smile"],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Care_Bears:_A_Lesson_in_Caring","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co5yza.jpg","s":"A Care Bears video game. It teaches letters, numbers, matching, etc."},{"t":"Care Bears: Let's Have a Ball!","p":["macOS","Windows"],"g":"Arcade","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Care_Bears:_Let's_Have_a_Ball!","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co75jp.jpg","s":"Care Bears: Let's Have a Ball! is based on characters from a popular children's television show and feature films, originally developed by American Greetings in 1981.\n\nThe player is taken directly to the home screen among the clouds where he can select a Care Bear to play any of the eight arcade-style games they represent. Each game is prefaced with a description and instructions, and all the other games can also be accessed from here by clicking on the bears that line the bottom of the screen. The games have five levels that become progressively more difficult as the player reaches them. Actions are performed by moving items or Care Bears with the mouse and keyboard."},{"t":"Carmen Sandiego: The Secret of the Stolen Drums","p":["PlayStation 2","GameCube","Xbox"],"r":"September 8"},{"t":"Cartoon Network: Block Party","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"August 5"},{"t":"Carve","p":["Xbox"],"d":"Argonaut Games","u":"Global Star Software","g":"Racing","r":"February 24, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carve_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co8zdi.jpg","s":"Welcome to the world of extreme watercraft racing. Carve takes you and your teammate around the globe to battle watercraft racing teams vying for the top-rank position. Exotic locales and intense weather and wave conditions make for challenging courses. Master eight individual racing styles along with signature tricks that can be performed off the ramp or on the water."},{"t":"Castle Shikigami 2","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"November 17","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Castle_Shikigami_2"},{"t":"Castle Strike","p":["Windows"],"d":"Related Designs","u":"Data Becker, Witt Interactive Studios","g":"Strategy","r":"January 7, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Castle_Strike","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co908v.jpg","s":"Castle Strike is a real time strategy game. Enter into a virtual medieval world of knights and castles where an exciting saga of friendship, intrigues and betrayals, battles and sieges, unfolds against the background of the Hundred Years' War."},{"t":"Castlevania","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"August 10","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Castlevania_(1986_video_game)"},{"t":"Cat Girl Alliance","p":["Windows"],"d":"Sekilala","u":"CD Bros., G-Collections","g":"Visual novel","r":"February 2, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cat_Girl_Alliance"},{"t":"Catwoman","p":["Windows","GameCube","PlayStation 2","Xbox","Game Boy Advance"],"r":"July 20","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Catwoman_(video_game)"},{"t":"Cave Story","p":["Windows"],"g":"Action, Adventure, Indie","r":"December 20","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cave_Story","i":"images/steam-200900.jpg","s":"Run, jump, shoot, fly and explore your way through a massive action-adventure reminiscent of classic 8- and 16-bit games."},{"t":"Champions of Norrath","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Snowblind Studios","u":"Sony Online Entertainment, Ubisoft","g":"Action role-playing, hack and slash","r":"February 10, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Champions_of_Norrath","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co6e7d.jpg","s":"An action adventure RPG with a hack and slash (or dungeon crawler) style gameplay. Taking place in the EverQuest world you pick between a variety of classes and races and set off on an adventure that brings you across different lands, multiple dungeons, and tasks you with a multitude of quests to complete while leveling your character, finding new weapons and armour, and learning new abilities as you progress. You can share this adventure with a partner on the couch with co-operative gameplay or jump online."},{"t":"Chaos League","p":["Windows"],"d":"Cyanide","u":"Focus Home Interactive, Digital Jesters, Cyanide","g":"Sports, management, real-time strategy","r":"June 25, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chaos_League","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2gb1.jpg","s":"Chaos League is a fantasy-based sports management game developed by Cyanide Studios and published by Digital Jesters. It was released in Europe on 8 August 2004 and later in North America on 8 March 2005. The game is a spin on American football, the violence of the Medieval football with no rules and rugby-style of sports yet set in a fantasy world with teams being made up of fantasy races such as dwarves, elves, orcs and undead, along with the use of magic and other fictional elements during a \"match\". The tone of the game is satirical with comedic color commentary and adverts for fictional in-game universe products. An official expansion was later released in 2005 bundled with the original, titled Chaos League: Sudden Death that added new features and gameplay tweaks. \n \nWhile not a direct video game adaption, Chaos League bears resemblance to Games Workshop's Blood Bowl tabletop board game, which is also about fantasy sports. Cyanide Studios would later develop the video game version of Blood Bowl in 2009, which itself utilizes certain features from Chaos League."},{"t":"Chessmaster 10th Edition","p":["Windows","Xbox"],"d":"Ubisoft Bucharest","u":"Ubisoft","g":"Computer chess","r":"August 10, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chessmaster_10th_Edition","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co9qti.jpg","s":"The 10th Edition is the first game in the series to feature a working online component and also the first PC version to feature animated chess sets and customizable interface."},{"t":"Chinese Paladin 3 Gaiden: Wenqing Pian","p":["Windows"],"d":"Softstar Technology Co., Ltd.","u":"Softstar Entertainment Inc.","g":"Role-playing","r":"August 6, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chinese_Paladin_3_Gaiden:_Wenqing_Pian","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/hdiojphcvwh8fi5t23jz.jpg","s":"This waizhuan (side-story) to the third game in Xianjian Qixia Zhuan series is not directly connected to it story-wise, but graphically and gameplay-wise the two are nearly identical. It utilizes the same fully 3D graphical engine, role-playing system, and turn-based battles with visible regular enemies, an indicator that shows the speed of your and the enemies' actions (allowing additional strategies), and two kinds of energy bars for special techniques."},{"t":"Chris Sawyer's Locomotion","p":["Windows"],"u":"Atari Interactive","g":"Business simulation","r":"September 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chris_Sawyer's_Locomotion","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4oju.jpg","s":"Explore a vast and detailed world and build a Transportation Empire!"},{"t":"City of Heroes","p":["Windows","macOS"],"r":"April 28","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/City_of_Heroes"},{"t":"Clannad","p":["Windows"],"d":"Key","u":"Visual Arts, Interchannel, Prototype, Sekai Project","g":"Visual novel","r":"April 28, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clannad_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co6ytz.jpg","s":"Clannad follows the life of Tomoya Okazaki, a high school delinquent who meets many people in his last year at school, including five girls, and helps resolve their individual problems.\n\nThe gameplay of Clannad follows a branching plot line which offers pre-determined scenarios with courses of interaction, and focuses on the appeal of the five female main characters by the player character. The game was ranked as the best-selling PC game sold in Japan for the time of its release, and charted in the national top 50 several more times afterwards."},{"t":"Close Combat: Marines","p":["Windows"],"d":"Atomic Games","g":"Real-time tactics","r":"September 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Close_Combat:_Marines"},{"t":"Clu Clu Land","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"May 21","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clu_Clu_Land"},{"t":"Cocoto Platform Jumper","p":["GameCube","PlayStation 2"],"d":"Neko Entertainment","u":"BigBen Interactive, Neko Entertainment","g":"Platform","r":"July 9, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cocoto_Platform_Jumper","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co9pwo.jpg","s":"A long time ago in a faraway land, strange little creatures lived in the depths of Abyss. Cocoto, his little devil friends and the mysterious Fairy protect the secret of the magma - the source of their power - in a magic cauldron. Meanwhile, Zaron, the god of lightning who lusts after this force, is up to something. He can count on the rulers of the other kingdoms that Cocoto must cross. The tragic kidnapping of Shiny, Baggy and Neuro has left Cocoto alone to watch over the cauldron. Refusing to leave his friends, he will set out to find them with Fairy."},{"t":"Codename: Kids Next Door – Operation: S.O.D.A.","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"November 2"},{"t":"Codename: Panzers – Phase One","p":["Windows"],"d":"StormRegion","u":"cdv Software Entertainment","g":"Real-time tactics","r":"June 16, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Codename:_Panzers_%E2%80%93_Phase_One"},{"t":"Colin McRae Rally 04","p":["Windows"],"r":"March 4","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Colin_McRae_Rally_04"},{"t":"Colin McRae Rally 2005","p":["PlayStation 2","Windows","Xbox","N-Gage","Mobile phone"],"d":"Codemasters","u":"Codemasters, Nokia, Feral Interactive","g":"Racing","r":"September 24, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Colin_McRae_Rally_2005","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co7jbj.jpg","s":"Colin McRae Rally and more recently; Dirt, is a racing video game series developed and published by Codemasters. Colin McRae Rally and Dirt 2 have since been developed and published for Mac OS X by Feral Interactive.\n\nStarted in 1998, the franchise has been a critical and commercial success and is generally acknowledged as a pioneer of realistic rally sports racing games. The series is named after the World Rally Championship driver Colin McRae, who provided technical advice during development.\n\nDespite McRae's death in September 2007, Codemasters retained the use of his name on their rally games until the release of Dirt 3, where the moniker was dropped."},{"t":"Combat Wings","p":["Windows","Xbox 360"],"d":"City Interactive Games","u":"City Interactive Games","g":"Combat flight simulation","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Combat_Wings"},{"t":"Conan","p":["Windows","Xbox","GameCube","PlayStation 2"],"d":"Cauldron","u":"TDK Mediactive Europe","g":"Action-adventure, hack and slash","r":"April 7, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Conan_(2004_video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1yaq.jpg","s":"Complete Conan's quest across 5 vast regions of Hyboria, from the icy Cimmerial to the steaming jungles of Dafar!\n\nFind your way through endless secret temples, cursed catacombs and forgotten caves!\n\nDefeat 10 fearsome bosses!\n\nDevelop your fighting skills with 16 types of sword, axe and mace, plus 50 different combos!\n\nFollow the quest and find all lost parts of the legendary Atalantean Sword to combine them into the ultimate weapon!\n\nLive in the deep, exciting storyline created in the spirit of Robert E Howard's original Conan tales!\n\nBattle against your friends in the 11 arenas in 3 battle modes, Death Match, Body Count and Time Challenge!"},{"t":"Conflict: Vietnam","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"October 5"},{"t":"Cops 2170: The Power of Law (RU)","p":["Windows"],"r":"February"},{"t":"Counter-Strike: Condition Zero","p":["Windows"],"g":"Action","r":"March 23","l":"https://store.steampowered.com/app/80","i":"images/steam-80.jpg","s":"With its extensive Tour of Duty campaign, a near-limitless number of skirmish modes, updates and new content for Counter-Strike's award-winning multiplayer game play, plus over 12 bonus single player missions, Counter-Strike: Condition Zero is a tremendous offering of single and multiplayer content."},{"t":"Counter-Strike: Source","p":["Windows"],"u":"Valve","g":"Action","r":"November 1, 2004","l":"https://store.steampowered.com/app/240","i":"images/steam-240.jpg","s":"Counter-Strike: Source blends Counter-Strike's award-winning teamplay action with the advanced technology of Source™ technology."},{"t":"Crash 'n' Burn","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"Climax Racing","u":"Eidos Interactive","g":"Racing, vehicular combat","r":"November 15, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crash_'n'_Burn_(2004_video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1ots.jpg","s":"Crash 'n' Burn is a PS2 and Xbox racing game which focuses on doing anything necessary to win the race. The game features a sophisticated damage system, and up to 16 cars playing at once online."},{"t":"Crash Bandicoot Purple and Spyro Orange","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"d":"Vicarious Visions","u":"Vivendi Universal Games","g":"Action, platform","r":"June 1, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crash_Bandicoot_Purple_and_Spyro_Orange"},{"t":"Crash Twinsanity","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"September 28","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crash_Twinsanity"},{"t":"Crazy Bus","p":[],"r":"August 24","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crazy_Bus_(video_game)"},{"t":"Crazyracing KartRider","p":["Windows"],"d":"Lodumani Studio, Nexon, Nitro Studio","u":"Nexon, Tiancity, Gamania","g":"Kart racing","r":"June 1, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crazyracing_KartRider","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4byk.jpg","s":"Crazyracing Kartrider is an online multiplayer racing game serviced by NEXON. KartRider not only features fictitious fantasy vehicles but also branded game models based on real-life cars, developed from collaboration with companies such as BMW Korea. About 25% of South Koreans have played the game at least once."},{"t":"Crimson Room","p":["Browser"],"d":"Toshimitsu Takagi","u":"TAKAGISM Inc.","g":"Escape the room, Puzzle","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crimson_Room","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co6fhf.jpg","s":"An escape-the-room flash game where the player is trapped in a room. This would later be expanded into a bigger series, and eventually ported to the DS under the same name."},{"t":"Crimson Sea","p":["Xbox"],"d":"Koei","u":"Koei","g":"Third-person shooter, Hack and slash, Action adventure, RPG","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crimson_Sea"},{"t":"Crimson Tears","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"July 21","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crimson_Tears"},{"t":"Crisis Zone","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"September 17","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crisis_Zone"},{"t":"Cruis'n","p":["Arcade"],"d":"Raw Thrills, Just Games Interactive","u":"Raw Thrills, Midway Games","g":"Racing","r":"July 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cruis'n_(video_game)"},{"t":"Crusader Kings","p":["Windows"],"d":"Paradox Development Studio","u":"PAN Vision AB, Koch Media, Paradox Interactive","g":"Grand strategy","r":"April 23, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crusader_Kings","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2ptq.jpg","s":"Gather prestige and piety and the world will whisper your name in awe. Will you co-opt other monarchs, and the Pope, under your leadership to liberate the Holy Land? Do you have what it takes to become a Crusader King?"},{"t":"Crushed Baseball","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"d":"Griptonite Games","u":"Summitsoft Entertainment","g":"Sport","r":"August 31, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crushed_Baseball","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/guphxfvzqwpy7jj3qdxt.jpg","s":"With its unique comic-book inspired art style, Crushed Baseball 2004 will offer fast-paced arcade gameplay that will appeal to both sports and non-sports gaming fans. With its over-the-top style, players will be able to power-up characters and give them superhuman abilities and special powers called \"Mojo\" abilities. For example, a pitcher might throw a pitch that acts as a buzz-saw and slices through the hitter's bat; a batter may hit a ground ball that lodges itself in the field so it can't be picked up, and a fielder might use their suction glove ability to suction the ball into their glove to record an out."},{"t":"Crystal Key 2","p":["Windows"],"d":"Earthlight Productions, Kheops Studio","u":"The Adventure Company","g":"Graphic adventure","r":"March 17, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crystal_Key_2"},{"t":"CSI: Dark Motives","p":["Windows"],"d":"Radical Entertainment, Powerhead Games","u":"Ubisoft","g":"Adventure","r":"March 23, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CSI:_Dark_Motives","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co7ykj.jpg","s":"CSI: Dark Motives is a computer game based on the CSI: Crime Scene Investigation television series. The game was developed by 369 Interactive, published by Ubisoft, and was released for the PC in 2004. In November 2007 it was remade by Powerhead Games, published by Ubisoft and released for Nintendo DS."},{"t":"CSI: Miami","p":["Windows","Mobile phone"],"d":"Radical Entertainment, Gameloft","u":"Ubisoft, Gameloft","g":"Adventure","r":"November 16, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CSI:_Miami_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co7ri2.jpg","s":"CSI: Miami is a video game based on the CSI: Miami television series. The game was developed by 369 Interactive, published by Ubisoft, and was released for the Microsoft Windows on April 24, 2004. In 2008, Gameloft redeveloped the game for iOS.\nThis game, like CSI: Crime Scene Investigation, follows a distinct pattern of five cases, with the fifth case tying together the previous four."},{"t":"CT Special Forces 2: Back in the Trenches","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"June 29"},{"t":"Cube 2: Sauerbraten","p":["Windows","Linux","macOS"],"d":"Wouter van Oortmerssen, Lee Salzman, Mike Dysart","g":"First-person shooter","r":"May 6, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cube_2:_Sauerbraten","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2hqh.jpg","s":"Cube 2: Sauerbraten (German for \"sour roast\", also known as Sauer) is a cross-platform, Quake-like first-person shooter that runs on Microsoft Windows, Linux, FreeBSD and Mac OS X using OpenGL and SDL. The game features single-player and multiplayer gameplay and contains an in-game level editor. The game engine is free and open-source software, under the zlib License, with commercial support available from the developer's own business counterpart, Dot3 Labs. The game media is released under various non-free licenses. The aim of the project is not to produce the most features and highest-quality graphics possible, but rather to allow map-editing to be done in real-time within the game, while keeping the engine source code small and elegant."},{"t":"Cubis 2","p":["Windows","Mobile phone"],"d":"FreshGames","u":"FreshGames","g":"Puzzle, Strategy","r":"November 12, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cubis_2","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co9atp.jpg","s":"Cubis 2 is a puzzle video game that was released in 2004 by FreshGames. In Cubis 2, the player shoots different colored cubes into cubes that are already placed on the isometric game table. Once three of the same color are matched in a row or are stacked, the cubes disappear and the player earns points. Once the board is clear or enough points are earned, the player advances to the next board which features a new animated backdrop."},{"t":"Custom Robo","p":["GameCube"],"d":"Noise, Studiofake","u":"Nintendo","g":"Action role-playing","r":"March 4, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Custom_Robo_(2004_video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/coawq2.jpg","s":"You've been challenged to a fight, and the robots are waiting. Do you pick a Ray 01 body and equip it with a Wyvern gun and Burrow bomb P, or do you opt for a Javelin with Satellite pod and Feather legs? Custom Robo lets you and up to three friends customize robots with nearly 200 unique parts, then turns you loose in a virtual battlefield to prove who's the top robot commander."},{"t":"Cy Girls","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Konami Computer Entertainment Japan","u":"Konami","g":"Action-adventure, Third-person shooter","r":"February 19, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cy_Girls_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4pxz.jpg","s":"It's the 21st century (a couple of decades ahead of the present time), and the world is dark cyberpunk place where cyber gear may be as deadly as a real metal gear. The game features two main characters, both ready to handle any given situations, both with special skills and abilities, and what's most important, both girls. Each girl has different methods of dealing with things and different storylines, and you can select with whom to play the game through (each girl has its own disc to boot up). Ice takes her confidence in the firearms and is cool and loud, while Aska is a ninja who prefers stealth over exposure, and uses blunt weapons like swords and daggers."},{"t":"CyberCIEGE","p":["Windows"],"d":"Naval Postgraduate School and Rivermind, Inc.","u":"Naval Postgraduate School and Rivermind","g":"Construction and management sim","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CyberCIEGE"},{"t":"D-Day","p":["Windows"],"d":"Digital Reality","u":"O3 Entertainment","g":"Real-time tactics","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/D-Day_(2004_video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co8bkq.jpg","s":"WWII strategy game."},{"t":"Daigasso! Band Brothers","p":["Nintendo DS"],"d":"Nintendo R&D2, Nintendo SPD","u":"Nintendo","g":"Music","r":"December 2, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daigasso!_Band_Brothers","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4omd.jpg","s":"Daigasso! Band Brothers is a music video game published and developed by Nintendo as a launch game for the Nintendo DS. It features multiple songs, which include classical music, television themes, and video game music. The game is controlled using both the buttons on the DS as well as its touch screen in certain portions. It uses a variety of different instruments, which are combined selectively in order to compose a song. Besides the primary mode, players may play together, each one playing a different instrument in the song. Players may also compose their own songs."},{"t":"Dance Dance Revolution Extreme","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"September 21","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dance_Dance_Revolution_Extreme"},{"t":"Dance Dance Revolution Ultramix 2","p":["Xbox"],"d":"Konami Computer Entertainment Hawaii","u":"Konami","g":"Music, Rhythm game Exergaming","r":"November 18, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dance_Dance_Revolution_Ultramix_2","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co5txe.jpg","s":"The second installment of Xbox exclusive DDR games."},{"t":"Dancing Stage Fusion","p":["PlayStation","PlayStation 2"],"d":"Konami, Bemani","u":"Konami","g":"Music, Exercise","r":"November 5, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dancing_Stage_Fusion"},{"t":"Dancing Stage Unleashed","p":["Xbox"],"d":"Konami Digital Entertainment GmbH","u":"Konami","g":"Music and exercise","r":"March 12, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dancing_Stage_Unleashed","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co9657.jpg","s":"Dancing Stage Unleashed, or DS Unleashed, was released by Konami Digital Entertainment GmbH to the European Xbox audience on March 12, 2004. A sister release to the North American Dance Dance Revolution Ultramix, it features the same look and feel and the same options as Ultramix, including online play and content download through Xbox Live. Unleashed has a unique soundtrack and features music from Big Brovaz, Blondie and The Wonder Stuff as well as original tracks from Konami's in-house artists. The original release was followed by two sequels, Dancing Stage Unleashed 2 and 3, released May 13, 2005 and March 17, 2006 for the Xbox in Europe."},{"t":"Dark Age of Camelot: Catacombs","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dark_Age_of_Camelot:_Catacombs"},{"t":"Dark Age of Camelot: New Frontiers","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dark_Age_of_Camelot:_New_Frontiers"},{"t":"Dark Fall II: Lights Out","p":["Windows"],"d":"XXv Productions","u":"Darkling Room, Iceberg Interactive","g":"First-person adventure, psychological horror","r":"August 26, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dark_Fall_II:_Lights_Out"},{"t":"Dead Man's Hand","p":["Xbox","Windows"],"d":"Human Head Studios","u":"Atari","g":"First-person shooter","r":"March 2, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dead_Man's_Hand_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3jdc.jpg","s":"The game is somewhat unusual in that between levels, the player plays poker for extra health and ammunition. The character is armed with 4 default weapons; a knife, a pistol, a rifle and a shotgun. Other weapons that can be found are TNT and Whisky bombs. The player can shoot objects such as whisky bottles, cans and enemies to score legend points, thus filling up the \"trick shot\" meter that lets the character use the secondary mode of firing which varies depending on the current weapon. The combat in the game also makes use of the game's physics engine, with the player being able to trigger physics based traps such as shooting a rock and causing it to fall onto an enemy below - kills obtained this way are rewarded with extra points and a greater increase in the \"trick shot\" meter. Dead Man's Hand is noteworthy for featuring a protagonist of Hispanic (or Mestizo) descent."},{"t":"Dead or Alive Ultimate","p":["Xbox"],"r":"October 26","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dead_or_Alive_Ultimate"},{"t":"Dead to Rights","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"d":"Torus Games","u":"Zoo Digital Publishing, Namco Hometek","g":"Action","r":"November 26, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dead_to_Rights_(GBA_video_game)"},{"t":"DearS","p":["PlayStation 2"],"g":"Simulator, Visual Novel","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DearS","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co8y1y.jpg","s":"DearS for the PlayStation 2 is a dating sim and visual novel game based on the manga by Peach-Pit. You step into the shoes of a character who begins living with the DearS, a group of alien girls. The game includes a map that allows you to explore different locations, interact with the girls, and trigger new events.\n\nYou play as Takeya Ikuhara, a high school student who, after living alone for some time, now shares his home with two DearS girls, Ren and Tina, who see him as their \"master.\" The game is structured around daily routines, with different actions and locations unlocking based on the time of day and day of the week similiar to the Tokimeki Memorial series."},{"t":"Decisive Battles of WWII: Battles in Normandy","p":["Windows"],"d":"Strategic Studies Group","u":"Matrix Games","g":"Computer wargame","r":"September 15, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Decisive_Battles_of_WWII:_Battles_in_Normandy","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co7lnn.jpg","s":"Battles in Normandy is a computer wargame in the Decisive Battles of World War II series developed by Strategic Studies Group. It is based on the liberation of Normandy by the Allied forces.\n\nThe game depicts many historic World War II battles of the Western Front, such as Operation Neptune, Operation Cobra, and The Falaise Pocket."},{"t":"Deep Labyrinth","p":["Mobile phone"],"d":"Interactive Brains","u":"Interactive Brains, Atlus, 505 Games","g":"Role-playing","r":"December 1, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deep_Labyrinth"},{"t":"Def Jam: Fight for NY","p":["GameCube","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"September 20"},{"t":"Delta Force: Black Hawk Down – Team Sabre","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2"],"r":"January 20"},{"t":"Densetsu no Starfy 3","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"d":"Tose","u":"Nintendo","g":"Platform","r":"August 5, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Densetsu_no_Starfy_3","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4an6.jpg","s":"A short time after Densetsu no Starfy 2, everything was calm and everyone including Stafy was happy again, until another severe thunderstorm came and shook Pufftop Palace. This time, it is more severe than the ones in the past. A lightning struikes the Magic Jar, destroys it and Ogura is free again."},{"t":"Desert Rats vs. Afrika Korps","p":["Windows"],"d":"Digital Reality","u":"Encore Software, Monte Cristo, Atari Interactive","g":"Real-time tactics","r":"March 30, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Desert_Rats_vs._Afrika_Korps"},{"t":"Destruction Derby Arenas","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"April 1","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Destruction_Derby_Arenas"},{"t":"Dig Dug","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"May 21","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dig_Dug"},{"t":"Digimon Racing","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"September 13","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Digimon_Racing"},{"t":"Digimon Rumble Arena 2","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox","GameCube"],"r":"September 3","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Digimon_Rumble_Arena_2"},{"t":"Disney's Kim Possible 2: Drakken's Demise","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"September 22","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kim_Possible_(video_game_series)"},{"t":"Djibril – The Devil Angel","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Djibril_%E2%80%93_The_Devil_Angel"},{"t":"Dofus","p":["Browser","Windows","macOS","Linux"],"d":"Ankama Games","g":"Massively multiplayer online role-playing game","r":"September 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dofus","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co93i0.jpg","s":"Dofus is a tactical turn-oriented massively multiplayer online role-playing game (MMORPG) developed and published by Ankama Games. It is primarily a pay-to-play game, though it still offers a limited amount of free content."},{"t":"Dogz","p":["Game Boy Advance","Nintendo DS"],"d":"MTO, Backbone Entertainment","u":"Ubisoft","g":"virtual pet","r":"November 25, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dogz_(2005_video_game)"},{"t":"Dokodemo Chocobo 3: Taose! Niji Iro Daimaō","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dokodemo_Chocobo_3:_Taose!_Niji_Iro_Daima%C5%8D"},{"t":"Domino Master","p":["Windows"],"d":"TikGames","u":": TikGames, Real, : Microsoft Game Studios","g":"Casual game","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Domino_Master"},{"t":"Donkey Kong","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"February 14","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donkey_Kong_(arcade_game)"},{"t":"Donkey Kong Country 2","p":["Super Nintendo Entertainment System","Game Boy Advance"],"d":"Rare","u":"Nintendo","g":"Platform","r":"June 25, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donkey_Kong_Country_2","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co7n25.jpg","s":"Donkey Kong Country 2 is a remake of the SNES game Donkey Kong Country 2: Diddy's Kong Quest. It is the second game in the series of remakes of the original Country trilogy for the Game Boy Advance."},{"t":"Donkey Kong Country 2: Diddy's Kong Quest","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"November 15"},{"t":"Doom 3","p":["Windows"],"g":"Action","r":"August 3","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doom_3","i":"images/steam-208200.jpg","s":"A demonic invasion has overwhelmed the Union Aerospace Corporation's Mars research facility. As one of only a few survivors, you must fight your way to hell and back against a horde of demons in this award-winning horror/action FPS and reimagining of the original DOOM."},{"t":"Dr. Mario","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"May 21","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dr._Mario"},{"t":"Dragon Ball Z: Budokai 2","p":["GameCube"],"r":"December 15"},{"t":"Dragon Ball Z: Budokai 3","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"November 16"},{"t":"Dragon Ball Z: Buu's Fury","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"d":"Webfoot Technologies","u":"Atari","g":"Action-adventure","r":"September 14, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dragon_Ball_Z:_Buu's_Fury","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3klz.jpg","s":"Dragon Ball Z: Buu's Fury is the third and final game in the series. It was released on September 14, 2004 in North America. The game focuses on the final parts of the Dragon Ball Z series (season 7), namely the battles with Majin Buu. The game added several new additions to the series. First, the game added equipment, which could be equipped to characters to alter their stats and provide various other benefits. The game also allowed players to allocate their own stat points, of which three were given per level. Also added was the ability to block by holding the R button, and also to energy block by holding the B button while blocking. Using the energy block slowly drains the user's energy gauge. Both techniques greatly decrease the amount of damage that is received from attacks. The game also added various other features such as fusions and the ability to transform into a Super Saiyan 3. Although many features were added, the ability to use charge attacks by holding and releasing the A button was eliminated.\n\nThe dialogues used in the English edition of the game are very similar, and sometimes identical, to the ones used in the English dubbed animated series."},{"t":"Dragon Ball Z: Supersonic Warriors","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"June 22"},{"t":"Dragon Ball: Advanced Adventure","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"November 18"},{"t":"Dragon Quest VIII","p":["PlayStation 2"],"u":"Square Enix","r":"November 27, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dragon_Quest_VIII"},{"t":"Drakengard","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"March 2","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Drakengard_(video_game)"},{"t":"Driver 3","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"June 21","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Driver_3"},{"t":"Ducati Extreme","p":["Mobile phone"],"d":"Vir2L Studios","u":"Mforma","r":"November 5, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ducati_Extreme"},{"t":"Duel Masters","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"High Voltage Software","u":"Atari","g":"Strategy","r":"November 2, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duel_Masters_(2004_video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4ss5.jpg","s":"Based on the Duel Masters Trading Card game in Japan, Duel Masters: Sempai Legends puts you in the role of a kohai (junior duelist). Your grandfather, a great Sempai (senior duelist), gives you a valuable Duel Masters card, which is soon stolen by a mysterious man. Now it is up to you to travel to nearby towns and villages in hopes of regaining the stolen property. Along the way, you'll face many opponents in Duel Masters tournaments with the hope of one day becoming a professional Duelist."},{"t":"Duel Masters 2: Invincible Advance","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"g":"Strategy, Card & Board Game","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duel_Masters_2:_Invincible_Advance","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/coc4oa.jpg","s":"Duel Masters 2: Invincible Advance is a Japan-only card battle game. It focuses on fast-paced duels using decks built from over 500 cards (sets DM-01 to DM-06)."},{"t":"Duel Masters 3","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duel_Masters_3"},{"t":"Duel Masters: Kaijudo Showdown","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"g":"Fighting, Strategy","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duel_Masters:_Kaijudo_Showdown","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co5xjo.jpg","s":"Get ready for intense tournament battles in this card-battling game that features characters from the Duel Masters animated series. Kaijudo Showdown challenges you to build a fighting deck from 300 Duel Masters cards, which you'll need defeat your enemies. As you duel various opponents, you'll improve your skills and solve the mystery of the missing artifacts. With a Game Boy Advance link cable, you can battle against or trade cards with your friend."},{"t":"Duel Masters: Sempai Legends","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"d":"Mistic Software","u":"Atari","g":"Role-playing","r":"June 1, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duel_Masters:_Sempai_Legends","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4euq.jpg","s":"Based on the Duel Masters Trading Card game in Japan, Duel Masters: Sempai Legends puts you in the role of a kohai (junior duelist). Your grandfather, a great Sempai (senior duelist), gives you a valuable Duel Masters card, which is soon stolen by a mysterious man. Now it is up to you to travel to nearby towns and villages in hopes of regaining the stolen property. Along the way, you'll face many opponents in Duel Masters tournaments with the hope of one day becoming a professional Duelist."},{"t":"Duke Nukem Mobile","p":["Tapwave Zodiac"],"g":"Shooter","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duke_Nukem_Mobile","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3awh.jpg","s":"Duke Nukem Mobile for the Zodiac is one of two games that share the name \"Duke Nukem Mobile\", the other is a cell phone game."},{"t":"Echelon: Wind Warriors","p":["Windows"],"d":"Encore Software","u":"Buka Entertainment","g":"Simulator","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Echelon:_Wind_Warriors","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3prl.jpg","s":"You are a pilot in the government forces stationed at one of the planets under attack. As you get higher on your career ladder, you will be able to choose more advanced hovercrafts and ammunition, as well as to order your own squad and influence local battles.\n\nThe goal of the development of the game is to further expand our virtual universe. Based on the huge success of the first game, we are presenting you with the same world, occurring at the same time, but from the point of view of another character, whose adventures unfold according to a different storyline. At times, it will cross the storyline of the previous game, and if you have played \"Echelon\", you will recognize some places and characters.\n\nEchelon: Wind Warriors is a unique game. This is not a regular space-battle simulator, nor is it a simulator of combat in enclosed labyrinths. The action is taking place above the surfaces of a planet, the picturesque landscapes of which are one of the basic features of the game play. In the realism of the implementation of the gaming environment – the cockpit of the battle hovercraft – Echelon is comparable with the best flight simulators. The game play is similar to that of the MechWarrior series, but instead of a walking robot, you pilot a fighter."},{"t":"Echo Night: Beyond","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"FromSoftware","u":"FromSoftware, Agetec, Indie Games Productions","g":"First-person adventure, Survival horror","r":"January 22, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Echo_Night:_Beyond","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4psa.jpg","s":"Echo Night: Beyond, known in Japan as Nebula: Echo Night is a survival horror adventure video game. The game tells a science fiction ghost story, set in the not-too-distant future. Players take the role of a newlywed, off for a honeymoon on the moon. The vessel crashes before reaching its lunar resort destination, however, separating the just-married couple and leaving the hero alone at an abandoned research base. Players explore the station from a first-person perspective, inside a spacesuit. In addition to the many spiritual anomalies that haunt the forgotten station, strange lunar lighting and relative weightlessness add to the atmosphere of the game's environments."},{"t":"Egypt III","p":["Windows"],"d":"Kheops Studio","u":"The Adventure Company","g":"Adventure","r":"March 30, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Egypt_III"},{"t":"England International Football","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"Codemasters","u":"Codemasters","g":"Sports","r":"April 30, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/England_International_Football","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co48gt.jpg","s":"The official England football team game.\n· Take on any of 32 international teams\n· 8 game modes including European Championship and Int. League\n· Head-to-head or co-op play with up to four players\n· Commentary and presentation by Gary Lineker and Barry Davies\n\n+ Free DVD 'England's Path to Portugal'"},{"t":"Escape from Woomera","p":["Windows"],"g":"Adventure","r":"May 7, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Escape_from_Woomera","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3v15.jpg","s":"Escape from Woomera is an unfinished point-and-click adventure video game, intended to criticise the treatment of mandatorily detained asylum seekers in Australia as well as the Australian government's attempt to impose a media blackout on the detention centres."},{"t":"ESPN College Hoops 2K5","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"Visual Concepts","u":"Sega","g":"Sports","r":"November 17, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ESPN_College_Hoops_2K5","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/x4y7hxjo3qn4iqogxrki.jpg","s":"College Hoops 2K5 offers a comprehensive college basketball experience. Go through Legacy Mode to bring a small college respect and eventually earn a job with a major program. Go online to test your skills against players around the world."},{"t":"ESPN Major League Baseball","p":["Xbox","PlayStation 2"],"d":"Blue Shift","u":"Sega","g":"Sports","r":"April 6, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ESPN_Major_League_Baseball_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/kakwjerfp1mrq0yha2k8.jpg","s":"ESPN Major League Baseball is the successor to Sega's World Series Baseball 2k3. Back are all of the game play modes from last years release: exhibition, playoffs, season, and franchise. Additionally, gamecast, duel, situation and GM career have been added to the game."},{"t":"ESPN NBA 2K5","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"Visual Concepts","u":"Sega, Global Star Software","g":"Sports","r":"September 28, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ESPN_NBA_2K5","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2gne.jpg","s":"ESPN NBA 2K5 is the sixth installment of the NBA 2K series of realistic basketball games, updating the roster to the 2004/2005 NBA season while re-inventing the franchise mode (now known as \"The Association\")."},{"t":"ESPN NFL 2K5","p":["Xbox"],"u":"Sega","r":"July 20, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ESPN_NFL_2K5"},{"t":"ESPN NHL 2K5","p":["Xbox"],"u":"Sega","r":"August 30, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ESPN_NHL_2K5"},{"t":"EVE Online: Exodus","p":["Windows"],"u":"CCP Games","r":"November 17, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Expansions_of_Eve_Online#Exodus"},{"t":"EverQuest II","p":["Windows"],"g":"Massively Multiplayer, RPG, Free To Play","r":"November 8","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/EverQuest_II","i":"images/steam-201230.jpg","s":"EverQuest® II is a deep fantasy MMORPG with over two decades of content, a thriving world, and ongoing expansions that keep Norrath growing. Create your hero and adventure through a massively rich, ever-evolving universe."},{"t":"EverQuest: Gates of Discord","p":["Windows"],"r":"February 9","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gates_of_Discord"},{"t":"EverQuest: Omens of War","p":["Windows"],"r":"September 13","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Omens_of_War"},{"t":"Everybody's Golf Portable","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"d":"Clap Hanz","u":"Sony Computer Entertainment","g":"Sports","r":"December 12, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Everybody's_Golf_Portable","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4ogl.jpg","s":"The fifth game, and first portable golf title, in the Everybody's Golf series, known as Hot Shots Golf: Open Tee in North America."},{"t":"Evil Genius","p":["Windows"],"d":"Elixir Studios","u":"Sierra Entertainment","g":"Real-time strategy, simulation","r":"September 28, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Evil_Genius_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co231o.jpg","s":"Evil Genius focuses on building an island lair and the management of minions that are employed by the Evil Genius, allowing the player to progress through the main storyline with achieving world domination as the end goal of the game. Although not explicitly stated the use of historic regions the Eastern Block and events such as the Cuban Missile Crisis within the game suggest that it is set in the 1960s and 70s and that the game is progressing through an alternate timeline."},{"t":"Excitebike","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"February 14","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Excitebike"},{"t":"Extreme Ghostbusters: The Ultimate Invasion","p":["PlayStation"],"g":"Shooter","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Extreme_Ghostbusters:_The_Ultimate_Invasion","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co685u.jpg","s":"The Extreme Ghostbusters have detected highly paranormal activity! They must now act quickly to find out who is behind this new threat! Choose between 4 characters and 3 exclusive game modes (Training, Arcade and Adventure.) Confront dozens of enemies each one more terrifying than the next."},{"t":"EyeToy: AntiGrav","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"November 9"},{"t":"EyeToy: Monkey Mania","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Sony Computer Entertainment Japan","u":"Sony Computer Entertainment","g":"Party","r":"August 5, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/EyeToy:_Monkey_Mania","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4el2.jpg","s":"EyeToy: Monkey Mania (also known as Saru Eye Toy Oosawagi: Wakki Waki Game Tenkomori!! in Asia, Japan, and Korea) is a party game that requires the EyeToy camera to play. It is based on Ape Escape and the monkeys in the game are guided through 50 minigames. Up to four players can play together.\n\nThe game is available with a silver camera or without for those who may already have the EyeToy."},{"t":"F-Zero Climax","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"d":"Suzak","u":"Nintendo","g":"Racing","r":"October 21, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/F-Zero_Climax","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co90zl.jpg","s":"F-Zero Climax is the sixth installment in the F-Zero series and the third to be released for the Game Boy Advance. This is the first F-Zero game to have a built-in track editor without the need for an expansion or add-on. Custom tracks can be saved to one of thirty slots for future use and they can be exchanged with other players via link cable. If memory becomes full or link cable connection cannot be done, the game can generate a password for the track; when it is input on any F-Zero Climax cartridge, the password will generate the track instantly."},{"t":"F-Zero: GP Legend","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"September 20"},{"t":"Fable","p":["Xbox"],"r":"September 14","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fable_(2004_video_game)"},{"t":"Fallout: Brotherhood of Steel","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"January 13"},{"t":"Famicom Detective Club: The Girl Who Stands Behind","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"August 10","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Famicom_Detective_Club"},{"t":"Famicom Detective Club: The Missing Heir","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"August 10","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Famicom_Detective_Club"},{"t":"Far Cry","p":["Windows"],"u":"Ubisoft","g":"Action","r":"March 23, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Far_Cry_(video_game)","i":"images/steam-13520.jpg","s":"A tropical paradise seethes with hidden evil in Far Cry®, a cunningly detailed action shooter that pushes the boundaries of combat to shocking new levels. Freelance mariner Jack Carver is cursing the day he ever came to this island."},{"t":"Fate/Stay Night","p":["Windows"],"d":"Type-Moon","u":"Type-Moon, Kadokawa Shoten, Aniplex","g":"Visual novel","r":"January 30, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fate/Stay_Night","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2h3l.jpg","s":"Fate/Stay Night is a Japanese visual novel, which was originally released as an adult game. A version of Fate/Stay Night rated for ages 15 and up titled Fate/Stay Night Réalta Nua was released later. Fate/Stay Night'​s gameplay requires little interaction from the player as most of the game's duration is spent on reading the text that appears, representing either dialogue between the characters or the inner thoughts of the protagonist. Often, players will come to a \"decision point\" where they are given the chance to choose from options displayed on the screen, typically two to three at a time. There are three main plot lines that the player will have the chance to experience, one for each of the heroines in the story. To view all three plot lines, the player will have to replay the game multiple times and make different choices during the decision points to progress the plot in an alternate direction."},{"t":"Fear Factor: Unleashed","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"d":"DC Studios","u":"Hip Interactive","g":"Action video game","r":"November 17, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fear_Factor:_Unleashed","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co81mm.jpg","s":"The game puts the player inside the action of the hit TV show, and features 12 spine-tingling stunts that will test gamers' steadiness, stomachs and nerve. Players can choose to play Fear Factor: Unleashed single player mode, where they will face five other competitors in an intense three-challenge contest to crown a winner. They can also play other custom single player modes or set up profiles for six friends and challenge each other in several party-style multiplayer modes."},{"t":"Feeding Frenzy","p":["Windows"],"r":"February 11","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Feeding_Frenzy_(video_game)"},{"t":"Feel the Magic: XY/XX","p":["Nintendo DS"],"r":"November 16"},{"t":"FIFA Football 2005","p":["Windows","GameCube","PlayStation","PlayStation 2","Game Boy Advance","PlayStation Portable"],"r":"October 14","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/FIFA_Football_2005"},{"t":"Fight Club","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"November 16","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fight_Club_(video_game)"},{"t":"Fight Night 2004","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"April 5","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fight_Night_2004"},{"t":"Final Approach","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Final_Approach_(video_game)"},{"t":"Final Fantasy Crystal Chronicles","p":["GameCube"],"r":"February 9","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Final_Fantasy_Crystal_Chronicles"},{"t":"Final Fantasy I & II: Dawn of Souls","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"November 29","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Final_Fantasy_II"},{"t":"Final Fantasy XI (US)","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"March 23","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Final_Fantasy_XI"},{"t":"Final Fantasy XI: Chains of Promathia","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2"],"r":"September 21","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Final_Fantasy_XI"},{"t":"Finny the Fish & the Seven Waters","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Sega Wow","u":"Sony Computer Entertainment, Natsume Inc.","g":"Action","r":"July 15, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Finny_the_Fish_&_the_Seven_Waters","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co6t23.jpg","s":"Finny is a plucky fish who is charged with the task of restoring calm to the troubled waters that he calls home. These waters are not the seas that Ecco swam in, but are rather some smaller ponds that are connected to short streams and small waterfalls and such. With the ability to jump out of the water to clear some obstacles of climb upstream, Finny has some basic abilities to clear obstacles and explore different areas. He's also hungry and his stomach will help him out as well as get him into trouble."},{"t":"Firefighter F.D.18","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"March 9","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Firefighter_F.D.18"},{"t":"FirePower for Microsoft Combat Flight Simulator 3","p":["Windows"],"u":"Microsoft Game Studios","r":"June 11, 2004"},{"t":"Fish Tycoon","p":["Windows Mobile","Mobile phone"],"d":"Last Day of Work","u":"Big Fish Games Majesco","g":"Business simulation","r":"May 3, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fish_Tycoon","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co5xqm.jpg","s":"Fish Tycoon is a virtual fish breeding game. The object is to breed and cross breed fish until you find the 7 Magic Fish and solve the genetic puzzle. You will have to buy supplies like meds, eggs and special plants and then sell some of your fish in your virtual pet store. If you have enough money you can buy new supplies and customize your virtual aquarium."},{"t":"FlatOut","p":["Windows","Xbox"],"r":"November 5","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/FlatOut_(video_game)"},{"t":"Flyff","p":["Windows","Browser"],"d":"Gala Lab Corp.","u":"Gala Lab Corp., Gala Japan Inc., Macrowell Technologies Co., Ltd., Mail.Ru Games","g":"Fantasy MMORPG","r":"August 16, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flyff","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3xug.jpg","s":"Flyff (short for Fly for Fun) is a fantasy MMORPG by Korean development company Gala Lab (formerly Aeonsoft & nFlavor). Flyff is a fairly typical party-oriented grinding game where no character can do everything; efficient play requires working in groups to level up by killing monsters, or Masquerpets. Its main distinctiveness lies in its flying system: flying is the normal method of transportation for characters above level 20.\n\nFlyff is hosted in 13 countries and 10 languages and is played by over 30 million people.\n\nGAMEPLAY:\nPlayers control an avatar that spends most of its active time fighting and most of its inactive time running a shop. Character classes are chosen at level 15 and sub-classes at levels 60 and 130, referred to as the first, second, and third job changes. The job changes are obligatory—when a character reaches the requisite level, experience gain stops until the completion of one of the job quests. At level 120, the character can become a Master, returning to level 60 with enhanced powers and able to work its way back up to level 121 and become a Hero. As of version 17, Heroes may select a third job class at level 130 and level up to the current cap of 150.\n\nLevels are gained based on experience, which can be acquired by killing Masquerpets and by performing quests. Quests generally involve killing specific Masquerpets and collecting the different quest objects they drop; a typical early quest is that of \"Party of Is,\" with the requirement of collecting 7 Chupims through killing Pukepukes.\n\nAt each level, the character receives skill points that can be invested in skills available to its job(s). There are two types of skills: those used for attacking and those used for protection and/or enhancement. Skills may have cool-down times and may cause status effects, with confusion, stun, and bleed among the most common effect. It is not possible to acquire maximum levels in all available skills until becoming a level 60 Master.\n\nCharacters can be improved by acquiring objects such as improved equipment. Masquerpets drop equipment, the in-game currency penya, consumable items such as food and potions, and quest objects, or players can purchase equipment from other players note this is usually extremely expensive because of the high quality gear that can be acquired this way. These can all be traded between players; Flyff gameplay involves large amounts of buying and selling in order to collect desired equipment. Most equipment items have minimum levels at which they can be used.\n\nCombat\nFlyff features melee, ranged and magic combat, with different skills available to different classes. Health points, fight points, and magic power bars are able to be replenished through food, vital drinks and mana refreshers; some classes depend on assists to heal them with magic.\n\nPvP\nPlayer versus player (PvP) combat is allowed on all servers without penalty in the form of dueling. Both players must be over level 15, and within 30 levels of each other, then they must confirm the duel first unless they are within the PvP Arena, a free-for-all environment found on all servers. Player killing is allowed only on the Yetti server and carries a high penalty.\n\nSOCIAL SYSTEMS:\nLord System\nIntroduced in version 12, the Lord system allows eligible players to be voted as the Lord of their server for 2 weeks. Players must have obtained Hero or Master status to qualify as a Lord candidate. While a Lord, a player may introduce a number of events on the server. Lords are taxed between 0 to 20% on all NPC purchases and returns and are given a portion of all player taxes. 10% of eligible voters must participate in the Lord vote for a Lord to be chosen. To vote for a candidate, a player must be at least level 60 and must have logged in to the game within the last 30 days. Each player may only vote for one candidate per election.\n\nParty System\nPlayers who join a party gain increased experience and loot. A lone player does not benefit from or harm a party. A party starts as a Regular Party, in which experience is distributed evenly among party members in the same location. At level 10, the party becomes Advanced, at which point experience can be distributed to players based on their amount of damage done. An Advanced Party may have up to 8 players; having this many players in a party increases player experience with each monster killed during training.\n\nGuild System\nGuilds allow players to socialize; players within a guild can chat with each other and many in-game activities are guild-based. Guilds have a hierarchical chain of command, consisting of the Master/Leader, Kingpins, Captains, Supporters, and Rookies. The guild master may change the permissions for guild members, allowing members to withdraw items or money from the guild bank, rank-up or de-rank other members, and be paid daily. Guilds are able to choose an emblem and cloak to represent themselves and have the use of a warehouse. When a guild reaches the appropriate guild level, increased by supporting the guild through quest items and Penya, the guild master may create guild cloaks at a cost that sport the guild's symbol. A large amount of Flyff end-game content is guild-related.\n\nGuild Siege\nThis event, held on Saturday in channel 1 of each server, allows guilds to compete in a free-for-all environment. A total of 8 Guilds may enter, and each Guild may have 10 players. To compete, the Guild leader must place a bid; the 8 highest bidders compete.\n\nClockworks War\nThe Clockworks War is a guild dungeon that guilds of any level may enter a single time. If the guild fails against the dungeon boss, its players may reattempt to win as many times as necessary for a time period of one hour. Only one guild is permitted inside the Clockworks Arena at a time.\n\nCouple System\nThe couple system, implemented in Version 13, allows a marriage-style connection between two characters. Characters who become a couple are granted special buffs and skills and receive gifts with new couple level gained.\n\nMentor/Pupil System\nThe Mentor/Pupil system, implemented in Version 15, allows any player level 91 or above to take on any character who has not completed their second Job Change as a pupil after completing the mentor qualification quest. This Mentor/Pupil bond provides a special bonus to experience gained by both mentor and pupil while both characters are logged on to the same server. Additionally, upon the pupil reaching certain level marks, the mentor gains 'Mentor Points'; as the mentor gains more of these points, additional pupils may be taken on, to a maximum of 3 pupils when over 100 Mentor Points are gained. These additional pupils grant increases to the experience bonus of the mentor; the other pupils' experience bonus' remain unchanged.\n\nWhile no action apart from the initial bonding is necessary within the Mentor/Pupil relationship, mentors are encouraged to help their pupils with advice, quests, and/or occasional gifts. If at any time either pupil or mentor becomes dissatisfied, the player may cancel the bond. The Mentor Points of a mentor who loses all pupils returns to 0 and must be regained through new Mentor/Pupil bonds.\n\nOTHER GAME SYSTEMS:\nEvents\nEvents involving rare drops and extra experience are held almost every week by the gamemaster team. Maintenance is held every Tuesday evening (gPotato) and Thursday noon (FlyFF PH).\n\nCollector System\nRe-Introduced in version 11, the Collector System allows players to collect rare and unique game items through the use of a Collectors.\n\nPrivate Shops\nPlayers can open private shops, in which held items can be sold at any price. Other players can enter these shops and purchase the items within, with the purchase money transferred to the shop owner's inventory.\n\nRaising Pets\nPlayers may keep seven types of Raised Pets, which start out as eggs that may be dropped by any Masquerpet level 20 and above. An egg can be hatched by the Pet Tamer NPC after feeding the egg 50,000 pet feed. To evolve a pet, players must complete quests given by the Pet Tamer. Pets must also be fed to keep them alive. Each Raised Pet has five levels and three appearances. A player accompanied by a pet receives additional stat points based on the type of pet.\n\nElements\nMonsters are generally associated with a particular in-game elements, of which there are five. Each element is vulnerable to one element and resistant to another. Weapons and armor can be \"elemented\", conferring advantages against monsters of some types and disadvantages against others; many aggressive spells are also elemented.\n\nCash Shop\nFlyff uses a micropayment system through which users can obtain 'Game Cash'. Game Cash can be exchanged for premium items not otherwise available in the game, including clothing, potions, different kinds of scrolls and pick-up pets.\n\nDEVELOPMENT:\nIn December 2002, Aeonsoft developed the first provisional prototype of the game, called Clockworks Ltd. In September 2003, the company changed the game's name to Flyff, and began its first closed beta in Korea. In July 2004, it won the Game of the Month award from the Korean Ministry of Culture, Sports and Tourism. Over the next year, it was launched in three more countries: China, Taiwan, and Thailand. In October 2005, the US received the closed beta, which ran for a month before Flyff was commercially launched in December.\n\nTECHNICAL DEVELOPMENT:\nGame mechanics\nAeonsoft employs its own in-house core technology. The world object engine uses load balancing middle-ware, multi-thread and parallel game logic processing. The 3D flying engine uses faster process with vector and collide mesh and 3D space divided by Octree System. Its network sync engine utilities packet optimization by object move estimation, client-side sync calculation, and object move calibration processes."},{"t":"Football Manager 2005","p":["Windows"],"u":"Sega","r":"November 5, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Football_Manager_2005"},{"t":"Ford Racing 3","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"Razorworks, Visual Impact","u":"2K Games, Empire Interactive, ZOO Digital","g":"Racing","r":"October 29, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ford_Racing_3","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co9c2u.jpg","s":"Flex your racing skills with some of the most famous cars in history!"},{"t":"Forever Worlds","p":["Windows"],"d":"Hexagon Entertainment","u":"The Adventure Company","g":"Adventure","r":"April 5, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forever_Worlds"},{"t":"Forgotten Realms: Demon Stone","p":["Xbox"],"r":"November 17"},{"t":"Formula One 04","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Studio Liverpool","u":"Sony Computer Entertainment","g":"Racing","r":"July 30, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Formula_One_04","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4fgh.jpg","s":"This licensed F1 game includes all official tracks, sponsors, drivers and cars of the FIA Formula One championship. The 2004 update includes all the latest changes to the teams, up-to-date driver rosters, and also the new Bahrain and China circuits. Online multiplayer is introduced and the singleplayer mode has been extended with time attack races against ghost cars, and historic cars that can be unlocked upon completing a full championship.\n\nThe career mode is another new addition. You start at the back of the grid and you have to impress sponsors and manager to earn a spot on a team. Success leads to lucrative deals, while failure gets you fired. There are four difficulty levels and gamers can race as themselves, with their name lined up on the starting grid."},{"t":"FreeStyle Street Basketball","p":["Windows"],"d":"JCEntertainment","u":"JCEntertainment","g":"Massively multiplayer, sports","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/FreeStyle_Street_Basketball"},{"t":"Front Mission 4","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"June 15","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Front_Mission_4"},{"t":"Full House Kiss","p":["PlayStation 2"],"g":"Visual Novel","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Full_House_Kiss","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4ulq.jpg","s":"Full House Kiss is an otome game based on the shōjo manga of same name. It was published by Capcom for PlayStation 2 in 2004."},{"t":"Full Spectrum Warrior","p":["Xbox","Windows"],"d":"Pandemic Studios","u":"THQ","g":"Real-time tactics","r":"June 1, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Full_Spectrum_Warrior","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2h7d.jpg","s":"The U.S. Army is the most powerful ground force in the entire world. The backbone of a ground invasion is the U.S. Army Infantry, and in the midst of combat, their skills, courage, and teamwork are put to the test."},{"t":"Fullmetal Alchemist 2: Curse of the Crimson Elixir","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Racjin","u":"Square Enix","g":"Action role-playing","r":"September 22, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fullmetal_Alchemist_2:_Curse_of_the_Crimson_Elixir","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/cobmmg.jpg","s":"Fullmetal Alchemist 2: Curse of the Crimson Elixir is the third Fullmetal Alchemist video game for the PlayStation 2 and is the second Fullmetal Alchemist console role-playing game for the PlayStation 2. It is the prequel of sorts to Fullmetal Alchemist and the Broken Angel. The game has much improved visuals than the previous title, as well as all dialog being voiced over. To help boost sales, Square Enix decided to release the game with a bonus DVD in the United States containing the second and third episodes of Season 2 (episodes 27 Teacher and 28 One is all, All is One\") of the 2003 anime series, since the show took a 4 month break in its Adult Swim broadcast. This DVD contains only English audio, with the shortened version of the 2nd OP \"READY STEADY GO\" by L'Arc~en~Ciel and the shortened 3rd ED \"Motherland\" by Crystal Kay, since that is the version that was to be shown in the Adult Swim broadcast. As of August 31, 2005, the game has sold 160 thousand units in Japan."},{"t":"Fullmetal Alchemist: Dream Carnival","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Eighting","u":"Bandai","g":"Fighting","r":"August 26, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fullmetal_Alchemist:_Dream_Carnival","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3h7a.jpg","s":"Fullmetal Alchemist: Dream Carnival is the first Fullmetal Alchemist fighting game for the PlayStation 2 and is the second Fullmetal Alchemist video game for the PlayStation 2. It was released in Japan in 2004, but was never translated or sold in North America or Europe."},{"t":"Futakoi","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Futakoi"},{"t":"Future Tactics: The Uprising","p":["GameCube","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"May 7"},{"t":"Gadget & the Gadgetinis","p":["PlayStation 2","Windows"],"d":"Eko Software","u":"Hip Games","g":"Action-adventure, beat 'em up, platform","r":"November 5, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gadget_&_the_Gadgetinis_(video_game)"},{"t":"Galactic Wrestling","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"AKI Corporation","u":"Bandai","g":"Fighting","r":"April 22, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Galactic_Wrestling"},{"t":"Galleon","p":["Xbox"],"d":"Confounding Factor","u":"SCi Games, Atlus USA","g":"Action-adventure, Platformer","r":"June 11, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Galleon_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co7jtl.jpg","s":"Players control Rhama Sabrier who must stop the evil Jabez from wreaking havoc across the seven seas."},{"t":"Gallop Racer 2004","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Tecmo","u":"Tecmo, ZOO Digital","g":"Alternative sports","r":"February 19, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gallop_Racer_2004","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co6j1v.jpg","s":"In Gallop Racer 2004 (Also known as \"Gallop Racer Lucky 7\" in Japan, and \"Gallop Racer 2\" in Europe and Australia), high-resolution graphics, advanced racing, and a variety of new modes reach to a higher level in digital horse racing fun. Old favorites such as the betting system and the classic season mode will also be back in the new title. Features: Enhanced Revolution Mode. Players will now be able to experience the perfect ride using the \"Ability\" setting to create an enhanced revolution called the \"Big Revolution\". Dramatic graphics such as the screen breaking into a million pieces like a mirror will add to the player's rush once they achieve the \"Big Revolution\". Affinity of Ability System. A new breeding system that allows the player to produce a maximum of eight original horses at one time. Once created these horses can be used as either the player's ride of choice or used as a rival's horse. Increased Camera Angles. Allowing the player to see their horse from every angle during the race will keep their blood pumping. Season Mode. With over 17 characters battling it out for the title of top jockey, the season mode has never been hotter or more intense! New Stages. Various new stages such as competitions against rivals and negotiations with trainers help to create the complete horse racing experience. Improved Graphics. High-resolution textures, enhanced effects, and improved use of shadow and depth of color immerse have been included to make the game look more natural and realistic. More Tracks and Horses. Featuring over 4,000 new horses and 42 tracks."},{"t":"Ganbare Goemon! Karakuri Dōchū","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"May 21","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ganbare_Goemon!_Karakuri_D%C5%8Dch%C5%AB"},{"t":"Gangland","p":["Windows"],"d":"MediaMobsters","u":"Whiptail Interactive","g":"Real-time strategy, simulation, role-playing video game","r":"February 27, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gangland_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co245t.jpg"},{"t":"Garfield","p":["PlayStation 2","Windows"],"d":"The Code Monkeys","u":"Hip Games","g":"Puzzle, Adventure","r":"November 19, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garfield_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co83sc.jpg","s":"Garfield lets you play the role of the fat cat himself. As Garfield, you must clean up Odie's mess before John comes home if you want to win a big piece of lasagna. It's a race against the clock as you explore fully interactive environments and interact with familiar characters from the Garfield show. The game also includes minigames that let you race, cook lasagna, and play classic console games."},{"t":"Garry's Mod","p":["Windows"],"g":"Casual, Indie, Simulation","r":"December 24","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garry%27s_Mod","i":"images/steam-4000.jpg","s":"Garry's Mod is a physics sandbox. There aren't any predefined aims or goals. We give you the tools and leave you to play."},{"t":"Get on da Mic","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Artificial Mind and Movement / Highway 1 Productions","u":"Eidos Interactive","g":"Music","r":"October 5, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Get_on_da_Mic","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co9and.jpg","s":"Get On Da Mic requires the use of the same kinds of microphones also used with the Karaoke Revolution games. A hand-held karaoke microphone made by Logitech is available in a bundle with the game and is also sold separately; Logitech also sells a microphone headset. The game is also EyeToy compatible, and it censors out profanity.\nUnlike the many other singing games available for the PlayStation 2, this game focuses exclusively on Hip-Hop songs."},{"t":"Ghost Squad","p":["Arcade"],"d":"Sega AM2, Polygon Magic","u":"Sega","g":"Rail shooter","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ghost_Squad_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co6fle.jpg","s":"One of the first light gun games to arrive on the Wii, Ghost Squad will take full advantage of the unique controls of the Wii Remote.\n\nThree dangerous missions bring a new gameplay experience every time with multiple levels, alternate routes, changing daylight, a variety of player choices and secret weapons and costumes to unlock.\n\nAlone or with up to three squad mates, players will rescue hostages, apprehend suspects and deactivate bombs as they eliminate terrorist threats around the world.\n\nUnlock 25 different tactical weapons including sniper and assault rifles, submachine guns, hand guns, and more."},{"t":"Ghosts 'n Goblins","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"May 21","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ghosts_%27n_Goblins_(video_game)"},{"t":"Giga Wing Generations","p":["Arcade","PlayStation 2"],"d":"Takumi Corporation","u":"Taito, 505 Game Street","g":"Scrolling shooter","r":"October 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giga_Wing_Generations"},{"t":"Gish","p":["Windows","Linux","macOS"],"d":"Chronic Logic","u":"Chronic Logic","g":"Platform","r":"May 4, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gish_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co41ah.jpg","s":"Gish isn't your average hero. In fact, he's not your average anything...you see, Gish is a ball of tar. A Sunday stroll with his lady friend, Brea, goes awry when a shadowy figure emerges from an open manhole and pulls Brea below ground. Following Brea's calls for help, Gish suddenly finds himself in the subterranean sewers of Dross, a long forgotten city filled with twisting corridors, evil traps, and some of the most demented creatures imaginable.\n\nWith his gelatinous structure as his only means of defense, Gish must follow the echoing cries of his damsel in distress deep within the earth below. What freakish creatures dwell in this subterranean land? Who is Brea's captor? And just how far down does the rabbit hole go?\n\nLife isn't easy when you're a 12 pound ball of tar..."},{"t":"GL-117","p":["macOS","Windows","Linux"],"d":"Thomas Drexl, Jean-Marc Le Peuvedic, Eugene Andreeschev, Eric Cheung","g":"Combat flight simulator","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GL-117"},{"t":"Glest","p":["Windows","Linux"],"d":"Glest Team","g":"Real-time strategy","r":"December 25, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glest","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4087.jpg","s":"Glest is a free 3D real-time strategy game, where you control the armies of two different factions: Tech, which is mainly composed of warriors and mechanical devices, and Magic, that prefers mages and summoned creatures in the battlefield."},{"t":"Godzilla: Save the Earth","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"November 2"},{"t":"GoldenEye: Rogue Agent","p":["GameCube","PlayStation 2","Xbox","Nintendo DS"],"r":"November 22"},{"t":"Gotcha! Extreme Paintball","p":["Windows","Xbox"],"d":"Sixteen Tons Entertainment","u":"Gathering, Viva Media","g":"First-person shooter, sports","r":"July 30, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gotcha!_Extreme_Paintball"},{"t":"Gradius V","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"September 14","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gradius_V"},{"t":"Graffiti Kingdom","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Taito","u":"Taito, Hot-B, 505 GameStreet","g":"Action role-playing","r":"September 22, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Graffiti_Kingdom","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4chp.jpg","s":"Graffiti Kingdom is the sequel to Magic Pengel, an action adventure game developed by Taito. In the game, you play as a prince who must use his magic wand to save his parents and his home. Use the in-game drawing tools to transform your character into three different creatures at anytime, turn 2D shapes into 3D objects, and pull off a variety of special attacks"},{"t":"Gran Turismo 4","p":["PlayStation 2"],"u":"Sony Computer Entertainment","r":"December 28, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gran_Turismo_4"},{"t":"Grand Theft Auto Advance","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"October 26","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grand_Theft_Auto_(Game_Boy_Advance)"},{"t":"Grand Theft Auto: San Andreas","p":["PlayStation 2"],"u":"Rockstar Games","r":"October 26, 2004"},{"t":"Greg Hastings' Tournament Paintball","p":["Xbox"],"d":"The Whole Experience","u":"Activision","g":"First-person shooter, sports","r":"November 16, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greg_Hastings'_Tournament_Paintball","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co9uku.jpg","s":"Greg Hastings' Tournament Paintball is a First Person Shooter paintball game that came out exclusively for Xbox."},{"t":"Gretzky NHL 2005","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Page 44 Studios","u":"Sony Computer Entertainment","g":"Sports","r":"November 9, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gretzky_NHL_2005","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2gvq.jpg","s":"Experience the look, feel, and passion of hockey in Gretzky NHL 2005. This game features players with detailed facial animations; EyeToy functionality, which lets you put your face in the game; and enhanced arenas complete with arena-specific game intros, goal horns, and interactive crowds. Gretzky NHL 2005 offers a variety of gameplay modes, including Tournament, with customizable tournaments; Franchise, where you can act as the owner; Online, with downloadable rosters; and Rivalry, which lets you revisit heated matchups."},{"t":"Ground Control II: Operation Exodus","p":["Windows"],"d":"Massive Entertainment","u":"Vivendi Universal Games","g":"Real-time tactics","r":"June 23, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ground_Control_II:_Operation_Exodus","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co28md.jpg","s":"Like the original, Ground Control II is not a standard base-building RTS game. There is no technical upgrade tree, and no mining for gold, crystals, or any other random mineral to be used as a monetary source. New units are acquired by spending acquisition points which collect throughout the battle. If the player has a large force, the points will come in very slowly. While the army is small, the points will come in at faster rate. More points can be earned by destroying enemy units, or by capturing special locations called victory locations. Additional units are called in via dropship, which will land in designated landing zones. The player must hold at least one of these landing zones in order to receive these reinforcements. Acquisition points can also be spent on dropship upgrades which include more cargo space, speed, fuel capacity, armor, and weapons."},{"t":"Growlanser Generations","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"December 7","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Growlanser_Generations"},{"t":"GT Racers","p":["PlayStation 2","Windows","Game Boy Advance"],"d":"Aqua Pacific","u":"Oxygen Interactive, GBA: Liquid Games","g":"Racing","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GT_Racers","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/ktpznbinlovgytzgvlvt.jpg","s":"GT Racers is a Racing game, developed by Aqua Pacific and published by Oxygen Interactive, which was released in Europe in 2004"},{"t":"Gunbird Special Edition","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Psyworks","u":"Atlus, Xplosiv","g":"Scrolling shooter","r":"February 19, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gunbird_Special_Edition"},{"t":"Gungrave: Overdose","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Ikusabune Co., Ltd.","u":"Red Entertainment, Mastiff, Play-It","g":"Third-person shooter","r":"March 4, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gungrave:_Overdose","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co6il2.jpg","s":"Three years after the events that took place in the original Gungrave, the Corsione family has unleashed the deadly drug SEED upon the populace. Now it's up to Grave, Spike and Mika to follow the trail of SEED back to its source and eradicate it once and for all.\n\nMuch like its predecessor, Gungrave: Overdose offers up several action-packed levels that simply don't allow the player to let up on the fire button. This sequel ups the ante with even larger hordes of enemies to blast through along with a slew of destructible environments to wreak havoc in. Along the way, Grave will team up with newcomers Juji and Billy. Juji fights using a unique combination of close-range guns and swordplay, while Billy defeats his enemies with the sheer power of his electric guitar."},{"t":"Gungriffon Allied Strike","p":["Xbox"],"r":"December 14","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gungriffon#Gungriffon_Allied_Strike"},{"t":"Gurumin","p":["Windows"],"d":"Nihon Falcom","u":"Nihon Falcom, Mastiff, 505 Game Street, Flyhigh Works","g":"Action role-playing, Platform","r":"December 25, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gurumin","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co25gm.jpg","s":"The PSP releases are a port of the original Japanese PC game with the rhythm bar removed. The 2015 release is a remasted version of the original PC game. The game had to be remade for the 3DS, 'Gurumin 3D: A Monstrous Adventure'. It is a port of the remastered version that has been changed to better fit the systems controls and use the 3D feature.\n\n\"Gurumin: A Monstrous Adventure is a fantastic Action-RPG from leading Japanese developer Falcom (Developers of “Ys” and “Zwei” among other classics) featuring real-time combat, stunning 3D graphics, tons of fully voiced characters and mini-games , 90+ items, multiple endings, a rocking soundtrack, 35+ hours of playtime, and more.\n\nOriginally released outside Japan on Sony’s PSP, Mastiff is proud to bring a fully localized and updated version of Gurumin: A Monstrous Adventure to Windows and to offer it through Steam with a full set of Steam specific features including Achievements, Trading Cards, Big Picture and Cloud Save.\""},{"t":"Half-Life 2","p":["Windows"],"u":"Valve","g":"Action","r":"November 16, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Half-Life_2","i":"images/steam-220.jpg","s":"Reawakened from stasis in the occupied metropolis of City 17, Gordon Freeman is joined by Alyx Vance as he leads a desperate human resistance. Experience the landmark first-person shooter packed with immersive world-building, boundary-pushing physics, and exhilarating combat."},{"t":"Half-Life 2: Deathmatch","p":["Windows"],"g":"Action","r":"November 30","l":"https://store.steampowered.com/app/320","i":"images/steam-320.jpg","s":"Fast multiplayer action set in the Half-Life 2 universe! HL2's physics adds a new dimension to deathmatch play. Play straight deathmatch or try Combine vs. Resistance teamplay. Toss a toilet at your friend today!"},{"t":"Half-Life: Source","p":["Windows"],"r":"June 1"},{"t":"Halo 2","p":["Xbox"],"u":"Microsoft Game Studios","r":"November 9, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Halo_2"},{"t":"Hamsterball","p":["Windows"],"d":"TikGames LLC, Raptisoft","u":"GameHouse","g":"Racing, puzzle, action","r":"February 8, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hamsterball","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2o28.jpg","s":"Take control of a hamster ball and race across 15 courses. Hamsterball will ensure that you never want to see another checkered pattern in your life!"},{"t":"Harry Potter and the Prisoner of Azkaban","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2","Xbox","GameCube","Game Boy Advance"],"r":"May 25","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harry_Potter_and_the_Prisoner_of_Azkaban_(video_game)"},{"t":"Haru no Ashioto","p":["Windows"],"d":"Minori, HuneX","u":"Minori, Alchemist","g":"Eroge, Visual novel","r":"July 23, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haru_no_Ashioto"},{"t":"Harukanaru Toki no Naka de 3","p":["PlayStation 2"],"g":"Role-playing (RPG), Simulator, Adventure","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harukanaru_Toki_no_Naka_de_3","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2fab.jpg","s":"An otome dating sim."},{"t":"Headhunter Redemption","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"August 27","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Headhunter_Redemption"},{"t":"High Rollers Casino","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"Cinemaware, Virtual Toys","u":"Mud Duck Productions","g":"Casino","r":"November 11, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/High_Rollers_Casino","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/snbh0q0dwbbondjkx9rk.jpg","s":"High Rollers Casino is a 2004 casino video game co-developed by Cinemaware and Virtual Toysfor the PlayStation 2 and Xbox gaming consoles."},{"t":"Hitman: Contracts","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"g":"Action","r":"April 20","l":"https://store.steampowered.com/app/247430","i":"images/steam-247430.jpg","s":"Enter the world of a HITMAN - a world of crime, sin and greed. Delve into the mind of Agent 47 and encounter his greatest adversaries, completing the work that made him so brutally efficient and shaped him as an assassin. Eliminate your targets by any means necessary. There are no rules... only the contract, signed in blood."},{"t":"Home on the Range","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Home_on_the_Range_(video_game)"},{"t":"Hot Wheels: Stunt Track Challenge","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox","Game Boy Advance"],"r":"November 10"},{"t":"Hugo: Cannon Cruise","p":["PlayStation 2","Windows","Mobile phone"],"d":"ITE Media","u":"ITE Media, Kiloo","g":"Platform game","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hugo:_Cannon_Cruise","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4ugl.jpg","s":"Hugo: Cannon Cruise is a Simulation game released in Europe in 2004."},{"t":"Ice Climber","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"February 14","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ice_Climber_(video_game)"},{"t":"IHRA Professional Drag Racing 2005","p":["PlayStation 2","Windows","Xbox"],"d":"Bethesda Game Studios","u":"Bethesda Softworks","g":"Racing","r":"November 10, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IHRA_Professional_Drag_Racing_2005","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co73vi.jpg","s":"Bethesda brings 50 vehicles, 24 pro drivers, and 11 sanctioned tracks to the 2005 edition of their drag racing franchise."},{"t":"Immaterial and Missing Power","p":["Windows"],"d":"Twilight Frontier, Team Shanghai Alice","u":"Twilight Frontier, Team Shanghai Alice","g":"Fighting game","r":"December 30, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Immaterial_and_Missing_Power"},{"t":"Immortal Cities: Children of the Nile","p":["Windows"],"d":"Tilted Mill Entertainment","u":"Myelin Media, Sega","g":"City building","r":"November 9, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Immortal_Cities:_Children_of_the_Nile","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2n1t.jpg","s":"Create an empire by providing for your people, and make your mark on history. From hunter-gatherers to immortal civilization. Watch your people go about their daily lives; make the right decisions and help them, and society, move forward. Lead your people. Immortal Cities: Children of the Nile is the first and only strategy game where citizens, who behave like living, independent beings, are your primary resource. Power and prestige cannot be purchased, they must be earned. Build your dynasty over 2,000 years. The fate of civilization is in your hands - you must balance your own ambition with your people's needs. The monuments you ask them to build are a testament to the prestige you have among your people."},{"t":"Imperishable Night","p":["Windows"],"d":"Team Shanghai Alice","u":"Team Shanghai Alice","g":"Bullet hell","r":"August 15, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Imperishable_Night"},{"t":"Imperivm: Great Battles of Rome","p":["Windows"],"d":"Haemimont Games","u":"FX Interactive","g":"Real-time strategy, real-time tactics","r":"December 21, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Imperivm:_Great_Battles_of_Rome"},{"t":"In the Groove","p":["Arcade","macOS","PlayStation 2","Windows"],"d":"Roxor Games","u":"Roxor Games, RedOctane","g":"Music, Exercise","r":"August 30, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/In_the_Groove_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/cobw7b.jpg","s":"In the Groove (abbreviated ITG) is the first game in the In the Groove franchise, published by RedOctane and developed by Roxor Games, and first released in video arcades around August 30, 2004."},{"t":"IndyCar Series 2005","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"Codemasters","u":"Codemasters","g":"Racing","r":"June 22, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IndyCar_Series_2005","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/cocj94.jpg","s":"IndyCar Series 2005 is a racing simulator developed by Codemasters. It is the sixteenth game of the Official IndyCar Series games series. The game was released on June 24, 2004 for PlayStation 2 and Xbox, and is based on the 2003 IndyCar Series season."},{"t":"InkBall","p":["Windows"],"d":"Microsoft","u":"Microsoft","g":"Puzzle","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/InkBall","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1wr9.jpg","s":"InkBall is a game that comes with Windows Vista and Windows XP Tablet PC Edition 2005."},{"t":"Inuyasha: The Secret of the Cursed Mask","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Bandai","u":"Bandai","g":"Role-playing video game","r":"March 18, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inuyasha:_The_Secret_of_the_Cursed_Mask","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co85b7.jpg","s":"Inuyasha: The Secret of the Cursed Mask is based on an anime series of the same name. You can play either as a teenager boy or a teenager girl, named by the player. The two scenarios are very similar and basically follow the same story: you live in modern-day Tokyo and one day discover a strange symbol in an old storehouse. As a result, you are transported to medieval Japan. You encounter the half-demon Inuyasha, who introduces you to Kagome Higurashi, the heroine of the anime series. Together you embark on a journey to retrieve scattered pieces of the Sacred Jewel and to find a way to get back home.\n\nThis is a fairly traditional Japanese-style RPG with random encounters and turn-based combat viewed from over-the-shoulder perspective. You can attack physically, use special techniques, and power up to combo attacks with multiple characters."},{"t":"Iron Warriors: T-72 Tank Commander","p":["Windows"],"d":"Crazy House","u":"Battlefront.com, Strategy First","g":"Vehicle simulation game","r":"September 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iron_Warriors:_T-72_Tank_Commander"},{"t":"It's Mr. Pants","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"December 7","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/It%27s_Mr._Pants"},{"t":"Jack the Ripper","p":["Windows"],"d":"Galilea Games","u":"The Adventure Company, Microids","g":"Puzzle, Adventure","r":"January 29, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jack_the_Ripper_(2004_video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co9e51.jpg","s":"Since August 31, 1888, the identity of Jack the Ripper has eluded criminologists. Using the actual clues and evidence assembled from years of painstaking research, now you can solve the mystery. Travel around authentic Victorian London locations in search of clues and interview over one hundred actual persons and suspects. Only you can stop Jack before he strikes again."},{"t":"Jackie Chan Adventures","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Atomic Planet Entertainment","u":"Sony Computer Entertainment","g":"Action","r":"October 1, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jackie_Chan_Adventures_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co9e0t.jpg","s":"Jackie Chan Adventures is based on the hit kid's action cartoon of the same name, which features Jackie as an ancient artifact expert and special agent for the government's secret \"Section 13\". Jade, his 11-year-old tomboy niece quickly becomes his apprentice and partner as they scour the globe looking for sacred talismans and protecting the planet from ancient Chinese demons. Jackie Chan Adventures follows the story of the cartoon series very closely, as Jackie's Uncle sends him to recover 12 ancient talismans. Each talisman unlocks new powers for Jackie, allowing him to access new areas within the game world. A bonus EyeToy mini-game is included."},{"t":"Jak 3","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"November 9","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jak_3"},{"t":"James Bond 007: Everything or Nothing","p":["GameCube","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"February 17"},{"t":"Jet Li: Rise to Honor","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"February 17"},{"t":"Jets'n'Guns","p":["Windows","macOS","Linux"],"d":"Rake in Grass","u":"Rake in Grass, Reflexive Entertainment and Stardock, Soft-World, Linux Game Publishing","g":"Scrolling shooter","r":"November 17, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jets'n'Guns","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2qgf.jpg","s":"You take the role of a freelance pilot who has to save the Universe from evil warlord Xoxx, who has stolen a gigantic space gun with the power to destroy the entire Universe. Buckle up because it's going to be a blast!"},{"t":"Jewel Quest","p":["Windows","macOS"],"d":"iWin","u":"iWin","g":"Puzzle","r":"October 29, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jewel_Quest"},{"t":"JFK Reloaded","p":["Windows"],"r":"November 22","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/JFK_Reloaded"},{"t":"John Deere: American Farmer","p":["Windows"],"d":"Gabriel Entertainment","u":"Destineer","g":"Construction and management simulation","r":"June 29, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Deere:_American_Farmer","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/yejztdr6ufvermor83eb.jpg","s":"John Deere American Farmer is a farming simulator that allows you to grow crops, hire workers, and expand."},{"t":"Joint Operations: Escalation","p":["Windows"],"r":"November 16"},{"t":"Joint Operations: Typhoon Rising","p":["Windows"],"r":"June 15"},{"t":"Kaena","p":["PlayStation 2"],"g":"Hack and slash/Beat 'em up","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kaena_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4tri.jpg","s":"Based on the 2003 French-Canadian CGI-animated film, 'Kaena: The Prophecy', by Xilam."},{"t":"Kaido Battle 2: Chain Reaction","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"February 26"},{"t":"Kakyūsei","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kaky%C5%ABsei"},{"t":"Katamari Damacy","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"September 22","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Katamari_Damacy"},{"t":"Kengo 3","p":["PlayStation 2"],"g":"Fighting","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kengo_3","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/pjfcuqjhtzmndozupdu5.jpg","s":"The Japan-exclusive third installment in Genki's samurai-based fighting game series."},{"t":"Kessen III","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Koei","u":"Koei","g":"Real-time tactics","r":"December 22, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kessen_III","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co48k3.jpg","s":"In Kessen III the player takes control of Nobunaga Oda, and unlike the previous two games, you cannot choose a side to play on, and Nobunaga has one goal only... to unify the lands and rid his world of misery and suffering.\n\nFollowing the prequels, this game comes with lots of cinematics and stays true to strategic as well as action gameplay, adding a few new things along the road, like collecting items during battles.\n\nThe two main aspects of this game are planning and engaging in battle. Select officers and strategically place them on the field of battle, assign commands and issue orders. When on the battlefield, each of the officers, including Nobunaga, will have his/her army at their disposal which can be controlled at any point. Level-ups bring additional special attacks to both officers and their troops."},{"t":"Kid Icarus","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"August 10","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kid_Icarus"},{"t":"Kidō Senshi Gundam: Fushigi no Dungeon","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kid%C5%8D_Senshi_Gundam:_Fushigi_no_Dungeon"},{"t":"Kidō Senshi Gundam: Senshitachi no Kiseki","p":["GameCube"],"d":"BEC","u":"Bandai","g":"Third-person shooter","r":"March 18, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kid%C5%8D_Senshi_Gundam:_Senshitachi_no_Kiseki"},{"t":"Kiekko.tk","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kiekko.tk"},{"t":"Killzone","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"November 2","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Killzone"},{"t":"King Arthur","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"November 17","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/King_Arthur_(video_game)"},{"t":"King of Colosseum II","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"September 9","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/King_of_Colosseum_II"},{"t":"King's Field Mobile","p":["Mobile phone"],"g":"Role-playing (RPG)","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/King's_Field_Mobile","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co9p48.jpg","s":"King's Field is the first game released by FromSoftware for mobile phones. It introduces quick saving and the auto map function. Its map layout is different from its Playstation namesake, and features no discernible story nor music."},{"t":"Kingdom Hearts: Chain of Memories","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"December 7"},{"t":"Kingdom Under Fire: The Crusaders","p":["Xbox"],"d":"Phantagram, Microsoft Game Studios Japan","u":"Microsoft Game Studios, Deep Silver","g":"Hack and slash, real-time tactics","r":"October 12, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_Under_Fire:_The_Crusaders","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2111.jpg","s":"Kingdom Under Fire: The Crusaders is a tactical wargame developed by the Korean studio Phantagram for the Xbox. It is the sequel to the 2001 game Kingdom Under Fire: A War of Heroes, and continues its storyline. Kingdom Under Fire: The Crusaders combines third-person action and role-playing elements in its gameplay, which differs from its predecessor.\n\nIts sequel is Kingdom Under Fire: Heroes. Another sequel is to be released in 2015 entitled Kingdom Under Fire II for PC and PlayStation 4."},{"t":"Kirby & the Amazing Mirror","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"October 18","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kirby_%26_the_Amazing_Mirror"},{"t":"Knight's Apprentice: Memorick's Adventures","p":["Xbox"],"d":"MC2 France","u":"Microids, XS Games","g":"Platformer","r":"April 16, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Knight's_Apprentice:_Memorick's_Adventures"},{"t":"Knights of Honor","p":["Windows"],"d":"Black Sea Studios","u":"Sunflowers Interactive, Paradox Interactive, Atari","g":"Real-time strategy","r":"September 30, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Knights_of_Honor_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co9wf7.jpg","s":"As King, it is your duty to lead your people in their struggle to raise your kingdom from its humble beginnings to a position of power and prestige. War, diplomacy and a burgeoning economy are the means by which you increase your power and expand your influence. A unique Knight-management system will offer you brand new possibilities to enhance your personal strategy."},{"t":"Knights of the Temple: Infernal Crusade","p":["GameCube","Windows","Xbox","PlayStation 2"],"d":"Starbreeze Studios","u":"TDK Mediactive Europe","g":"Action-adventure, hack and slash","r":"March 19, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Knights_of_the_Temple:_Infernal_Crusade","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1utw.jpg","s":"An action/adventure role playing game from the developers behind Chronicles of Riddick and The Darkness. The game was never released outside Europe."},{"t":"KOF: Maximum Impact","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Noise Factory","u":"SNK Playmore, Ignition Entertainment","g":"Fighting","r":"August 12, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/KOF:_Maximum_Impact"},{"t":"Kohan II: Kings of War","p":["Windows"],"d":"TimeGate Studios","u":"Take Two Interactive, Global Star Software","g":"Real-time strategy","r":"September 17, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kohan_II:_Kings_of_War","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2djn.jpg","s":"A real-time strategy game continuing the story of the fantasy world of Khaldun. Even as the world erupts in civil war, an ancient evil gives out a call, and the Shadow-touched begin to gather."},{"t":"Konung: Legend of the North","p":["Windows"],"d":"1C","u":"1C, PAN Interactive, Strategy First","g":"Role-playing video game","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Konung:_Legend_of_the_North"},{"t":"Kowloon High-School Chronicle","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Shout! Design Works, Toybox Inc.","u":"Atlus, Arc System Works, PQube","g":"Action role-playing, visual novel","r":"September 16, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kowloon_High-School_Chronicle"},{"t":"Kult: Heretic Kingdoms","p":["Windows","macOS"],"g":"Action, Adventure, Indie, RPG","r":"October 1","l":"https://store.steampowered.com/app/277650","i":"images/steam-277650.jpg","s":"Kult is prequel to Shadows: Heretic Kingdoms originally released in 2005. It is isometric RPG with action combat, engaging storyline and unique RPG system. Kult has been very positively acclaimed by players and called as a sleeper hit by many..."},{"t":"Kuma\\War","p":["Windows"],"d":"Kuma Reality Games","u":"Kuma Reality Games","g":"Shooter","r":"March 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kuma%5CWar","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co9h19.jpg","s":"Kuma\\War is a free tactical first and third-person shooter game created by developer Kuma Reality Games. Kuma\\War is an episodic game that re-creates real-world conflicts in video game format using information culled from news accounts, military experts, Department of Defense records and original research. Episodes consist of a playable mission, extensive background text, and often include interviews with military experts, soldiers and other actual participants in the events described."},{"t":"Kuon","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"December 7","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kuon"},{"t":"Kururin Squash!","p":["GameCube"],"d":"Eighting","u":"Nintendo","g":"Puzzle, action","r":"October 14, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kururin_Squash!","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4snp.jpg","s":"Kururin Squash! is an action-puzzle video game developed by Eighting and published by Nintendo. It was released only in Japan on October 14, 2004. The game is the successor to Kururin Paradise and is the only title of the Kururin series with 3D computer graphics."},{"t":"Lamune","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lamune"},{"t":"Law & Order: Justice Is Served","p":["Windows"],"d":"Legacy Interactive","u":"Legacy Interactive, Mindscape Inc.","g":"Adventure","r":"October 5, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Law_&_Order:_Justice_Is_Served","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co7bqu.jpg","s":"An up and coming female tennis star is found dead in a locker room. Join the cast of the popular TV series to hunt down the murderer and work with the D.A to put together a convincing case to nail the guilty verdict."},{"t":"Legacy: Dark Shadows","p":["Windows"],"d":"Razbor Studios","u":"GMX Media","g":"Adventure","r":"November 29, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Legacy:_Dark_Shadows","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co5td5.jpg","s":"Legacy: Dark Shadows is a 3 disc PC adventure game in a sci-fi setting. It was made by TriSynery and Razbor Studios."},{"t":"Legend of Golfer","p":["GameCube"],"g":"Sport","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Legend_of_Golfer","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co9ecc.jpg","s":"A Nintendo published arcade golf game released only in Japan for the Nintendo GameCube"},{"t":"Lego Knights' Kingdom","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"d":"Razorback Developments","u":"THQ","g":"Action-adventure","r":"October 4, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lego_Knights'_Kingdom","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co56pj.jpg","s":"Knights' Kingdom is a top-down perspective action-adventure game. The player controls one of four characters, with only one character being controlled at a time. The character run through a series of nine levels, attacking Shadow Knights and solving tasks along the way. The player collects shields in levels as a form of health: upon being hit by an enemy or harmful obstacle, the player's health will deteriorate.\n\nThe game also includes a tournament arena mode, where the characters compete against each other in three modes: Hand to Hand Combat, Jousting and Lightning Combat."},{"t":"Leisure Suit Larry: Magna Cum Laude","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"October 5"},{"t":"Lemonade Tycoon 2","p":["Windows","macOS"],"d":"Jamdat Mobile","u":"MumboJumbo","g":"Business simulation game","r":"August 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lemonade_Tycoon_2"},{"t":"Lemony Snicket's A Series of Unfortunate Events","p":["Windows","GameCube","PlayStation 2","Xbox","Game Boy Advance","Nintendo DS"],"r":"November 10","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lemony_Snicket%27s_A_Series_of_Unfortunate_Events_(video_game)"},{"t":"Lethal Enforcers 3","p":["Arcade"],"d":"Polygon Magic, Konami","u":"Konami","g":"Rail shooter","r":"November 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lethal_Enforcers_3","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co96bd.jpg","s":"A light gun shooting game with the motif of a job that protects peace. There are stages for each occupation, and police officers, coast guard officers, riot police, etc. are active."},{"t":"Lifeline","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"March 2","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lifeline_(video_game)"},{"t":"Like Life","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Like_Life"},{"t":"Lilo & Stitch 2: Hämsterviel Havoc","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"October 14","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lilo_%26_Stitch_(franchise)#Video_games"},{"t":"Lords of the Realm III","p":["Windows"],"d":"Impressions Games","u":"Sierra Entertainment","g":"Real-time strategy","r":"March 16, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lords_of_the_Realm_III","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2ie3.jpg","s":"At the start of a game, the player must choose a noble by either selecting one of the default nobles or creating a new one. Nobles act as user accounts within the game, wherein completed campaigns and saved games are local to each noble. A noble consists of three customizable features: housename, portrait, and heraldry.\n\nOnce a noble is selected, the player can choose to play a campaign or battle map, or load a saved game. While all the battle maps are available when a noble is created, the campaigns require that the player complete each level in sequence."},{"t":"Love and Berry: Dress Up and Dance!","p":["Arcade"],"d":"Sega","u":"Sega","g":"Simulator, Arcade, Card & Board Game","r":"October 30, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Love_and_Berry:_Dress_Up_and_Dance!","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co7ncj.jpg","s":"Love and Berry are magical witches who possess the power of \"Fashion Magic\", which allows them to change clothes instantaneously."},{"t":"Lumines: Puzzle Fusion","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"u":"Bandai","r":"December 12, 2004"},{"t":"Mabinogi","p":["Windows"],"d":"devCAT","u":"Nexon Korea","g":"Massively multiplayer online role-playing game","r":"June 22, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mabinogi_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/cocrdn.jpg","s":"Embark on amazing adventures, build lasting friendships or even find romance in this unique social game, where a welcoming community with thousands of devoted players await! Whoever you are, or whatever your heart’s desire, come express it in Mabinogi and start living your fantasy life!"},{"t":"Madden NFL 2005","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox","GameCube"],"u":"EA Sports","r":"August 9, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Madden_NFL_2005"},{"t":"Maestro","p":["Windows"],"d":"Mike Oldfield","g":"Simulation, Music game, Art game","r":"April 12, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maestro_(2004_video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4a26.jpg","s":"Maestro is a MusicVR video game by British musician Mike Oldfield. It is the second publicly released MusicVR game after 2002's Tres Lunas."},{"t":"Mafia: The City of Lost Heaven","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"January 28"},{"t":"Magna Carta: Tears of Blood","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Softmax","u":"Sony Computer Entertainment, Banpresto, Atlus, 505 Game Street","g":"Role-playing","r":"November 11, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magna_Carta:_Tears_of_Blood","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co90q2.jpg","s":"Magna Carta: Tears of Blood is a Korean-made RPG in Japanese style, and a sequel to Phantom of Avalanche; it is set in the same world and has the same protagonist. The game's combat system is turn-based at core, but requires the player to press buttons in a rapid succession and with precise timing to execute attacks. The characters can store up energy to unleash a stronger attack later. Using the technique named Carta, they can also perform various special moves which are based on elemental affinities."},{"t":"Malice","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"Argonaut Games","u":"Mud Duck Productions, Evolved Games","g":"Platform","r":"April 30, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Malice_(2004_video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co8zdg.jpg","s":"In this action-adventure platformer you play the part of Malice. Malice starts the game being resurrected by Death himself and it is explained that she is actually a demi-goddess who has stripped of her powers. Hell-bent on revenge, you must help Malice traverse many worlds armed with a variety of weapons; including the Mace of Clubs, the Clockwork Hammer and the Quantum Tuning Fork. Malice can also learn and use elemental magic to help her overcome many hazards. Can you help Malice beat the rising Crow Army to reach the evil Dog God and restore the shattered world once more?"},{"t":"Mall of America Tycoon","p":["Windows"],"d":"4HEAD Studios","u":"Activision","g":"Business simulation game","r":"September 28, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mall_of_America_Tycoon","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/kfxs87rgx9tj5bloffji.jpg","s":"Mall of America Tycoon is a Mall simulator that takes place in the Mall of America."},{"t":"Manhunt","p":["Windows","Xbox"],"g":"Action","r":"April 20","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manhunt_(video_game)","i":"images/steam-12130.jpg","s":"You awake to the sound of your own panicked breath. In Manhunt, you must run, hide and fight to survive. If you can stay alive long enough, you may find out who did this to you. This is a brutal blood sport."},{"t":"Mappy","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"February 14","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mappy"},{"t":"Mario Bros.","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"May 21","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mario_Bros."},{"t":"Mario Golf: Advance Tour","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"d":"Camelot Software Planning","u":"Nintendo","g":"Sports, role-playing","r":"April 22, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mario_Golf:_Advance_Tour","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2204.jpg","s":"Grab your clubs and start down the road to golfing perfection in this role-playing golf adventure! Chat up the locals at golf clinics, hone your skills in challenges like Club Slots and Go-Go Gates, and try to become the champ of all the country clubs! The Mushroom Kingdom residents take on only the very best."},{"t":"Mario Party 6","p":["GameCube"],"r":"December 6","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mario_Party_6"},{"t":"Mario Pinball Land","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"d":"Fuse Games","u":"Nintendo","g":"Pinball","r":"August 26, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mario_Pinball_Land","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1wsi.jpg","s":"Jumping has always helped Mario perform heroic feats, but in Mario Pinball Land, the plumber must learn how to roll to rescue the princess. When Bowser kidnaps Peach and escapes to another dimension, a scientist transforms Mario into a ball to chase after the fiend. Now you must use your flippers to shoot a much rounder Mario into doors that lead to new areas. In his new form, Mario is also useful for knocking down enemies, picking up special bonuses, and finding power-ups."},{"t":"Mario Power Tennis","p":["GameCube"],"r":"October 28","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mario_Power_Tennis"},{"t":"Mario vs. Donkey Kong","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"May 24","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mario_vs._Donkey_Kong_(video_game)"},{"t":"Martin Mystère: Operation Dorian Gray","p":["Windows"],"d":"Artematica","u":"Leader S.p.a., GMX Media, The Adventure Company","g":"Adventure game","r":"December 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Martin_Myst%C3%A8re:_Operation_Dorian_Gray","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/coavbf.jpg"},{"t":"Mashed","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox","Windows"],"d":"Supersonic Software","u":"Empire Interactive, D3 Publisher, Vivendi Games","g":"Vehicular combat, racing","r":"June 18, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mashed_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1owx.jpg","s":"A combat-heavy racer from developer Supersonic, played from a top-down perspective. Mashed features four players racing at one time either in teams of two or every man for himself. The 13 different race environments are spread over various terrain including ice, sand and highways. An assortment of weapons are used to batter opponents into submission and gain rank in the race. However, once another car is blasted off road the player will still be able to target the race leader with air missile strikes. Developed for the European market for Xbox, PlayStation 2, and PC."},{"t":"Maximo vs. Army of Zin","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"January 20","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maximo_vs._Army_of_Zin"},{"t":"Mazera","p":["Mobile phone","Windows Mobile"],"d":"Cold River Studios","u":"Astraware","g":"Puzzle, adventure","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mazera","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co98ud.jpg","s":"Mazera is an adventure game created by Cold River Studios and published by Astraware for Palm OS and Pocket PC. The player plays Ix, who as a boy was captured by an alien race called the Mazerians and imprisoned in their zoo, until one day something happens that gives him a chance to escape. As Ix makes his escape, he must solve a large variety of puzzles and challenges so that he can return to his home planet Ixus."},{"t":"MC Groovz Dance Craze","p":["GameCube"],"d":"Mad Catz","u":"Mad Catz","g":"Music","r":"November 22, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MC_Groovz_Dance_Craze","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co5ns3.jpg","s":"Produced by the long-time peripheral maker Mad Catz, MC Groovz Dance Craze puts players on the dance floor for songs from popular artists. Enjoy dancing to many of your favorite tunes by Jessica Simpson, Jewel, Kevin Lyttle, DJ Jazzy Jeff & the Fresh Prince, KC and the Sunshine Band... just to name a few. Groove out in single player modes or bring friends out for multiplayer modes including: Just Dance, Dance Together, Dance Face Off and Dance Work Out. You can practice to become a better dancer, show off your talent, compete against a friend, and even get dance-tastic exercise. Plus, you can still boogie down using the Nintendo GameCube Controller. The game is available with a bundled dance pad, or available separately."},{"t":"McFarlane's Evil Prophecy","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Konami Computer Entertainment Hawaii","u":"Konami","g":"Action","r":"June 15, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/McFarlane's_Evil_Prophecy","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co90qb.jpg","s":"In the 19th century, the dead are rising from their graves and other chaos is happening all over the world. People fear that the end of the world is coming. A book predicts that an eternal age of darkness on Earth is beginning. Dr. Hans Jaeger summons three of the best monster hunters in the world to fight the evil creatures: Logan the pirate, Delphine the gunslinger, and Sundano, a mystical African warrior. Among the monsters are Dracula, Frankenstein's monster, the werewolf, the mummy, the sea creature, and the voodoo queen."},{"t":"MechAssault 2: Lone Wolf","p":["Xbox"],"d":"Day 1 Studios, FASA Studio","u":"Microsoft Game Studios","g":"Third-person shooter","r":"December 28, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MechAssault_2:_Lone_Wolf","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3gar.jpg","s":"MechAssault 2: Lone Wolf continues the destruction, intense combat, and online play introduced by the first MechAssault game. Set in the 31st century, the game lets you encounter new experiences in the expansive BattleTech world. Choose from a variety of weapons and vehicles--from the stealthy Raptor mech to the mech-jacking BattleArmor--all equipped with different weapon configurations and artillery. Embark on the new single-player campaign, or test your teamwork skills in the online multiplayer arena."},{"t":"Medal of Honor: Pacific Assault","p":["Windows"],"r":"November 2"},{"t":"Medieval Conquest","p":["Windows"],"d":"Cat Daddy Games","u":"Global Star Software","g":"Real-time strategy","r":"September 6, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Medieval_Conquest","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2il8.jpg","s":"A PC strategy cross tycoon game, set in a goofy fantasy world. Control units, build cities, destroy evil."},{"t":"Medieval Lords: Build, Defend, Expand","p":["Windows"],"d":"Monte Cristo Multimedia","u":"Monte Cristo Multimedia","g":"Strategy","r":"October 29, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Medieval_Lords:_Build,_Defend,_Expand","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/ehhkyka96tkkkr7vnbse.jpg","s":"Medieval Lords is a 3D city-building game set in the Middle Ages. Players develop towns by constructing buildings connected by a network of roads, managing resources, and fulfilling citizens' needs for food, security, entertainment, and religious services. The game incorporates geographical elements like water proximity and soil fertility that affect town development. Unlike traditional medieval strategy games, the combat system focuses on defensive fortifications and numerical advantage rather than tactical warfare. The game uses a zone-of-influence system where certain structures provide benefits to nearby buildings, and success depends on efficient tax collection and strategic placement of facilities to maintain population growth and unlock advanced construction options."},{"t":"Mega Man Anniversary Collection","p":["GameCube","PlayStation 2","Game Boy Advance"],"r":"June 23","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mega_Man_Anniversary_Collection"},{"t":"Mega Man Battle Network 4","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"June 27","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mega_Man_Battle_Network_4"},{"t":"Mega Man X8","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"December 7","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mega_Man_X8"},{"t":"Mega Man X: Command Mission","p":["GameCube","PlayStation 2"],"r":"July 29"},{"t":"Mega Man Zero 3","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"October 5","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mega_Man_Zero_3"},{"t":"Memories Off: Sorekara","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2"],"g":"Adventure, Visual Novel","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Memories_Off:_Sorekara","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2wl3.jpg","s":"The fourth entry in the main Memories Off series of visual novels."},{"t":"Men of Valor","p":["Xbox","Windows"],"d":"2015","u":"Vivendi Universal Games","g":"First-person shooter","r":"October 19, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Men_of_Valor","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3jde.jpg","s":"Vietnam, 1965. You are Dean Shepard, a \"cherry\" to the 'Nam with zero war experience other than standard boot camp training at Parris Island, SC. Along with your platoon, you will fight the NVA and the Vietcong in true historic locales and battles."},{"t":"Metal Gear Solid 3: Snake Eater","p":["PlayStation 2"],"u":"Konami","r":"November 17, 2004"},{"t":"Metal Gear Solid: The Twin Snakes","p":["GameCube"],"r":"March 9"},{"t":"Metal Slug 3","p":["Xbox"],"r":"May 25","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Metal_Slug_3"},{"t":"Metal Slug Advance","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"December 2","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Metal_Slug_Advance"},{"t":"Metal Wolf Chaos","p":["Xbox"],"d":"FromSoftware","u":"FromSoftware, Devolver Digital","g":"Third-person shooter","r":"December 22, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Metal_Wolf_Chaos","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2sii.jpg","s":"Metal Wolf Chaos is a mecha action game where you control fictional U.S. President Michael Wilson as he fights to stop Vice President Richard Hawk’s coup. Using a custom combat mech, you take on missions across recognizable American locations, battling rebel forces through high-intensity third-person shooter gameplay.\n\nThe mech can be outfitted with a wide arsenal of weapons for different combat styles, letting you tailor loadouts as the conflict escalates."},{"t":"Metin2","p":[],"d":"Webzen Games","g":"Massively multiplayer online role-playing game","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Metin2"},{"t":"Metroid","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"August 10","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Metroid_(video_game)"},{"t":"Metroid Prime 2: Echoes","p":["GameCube"],"u":"Nintendo","r":"November 15, 2004"},{"t":"Metroid Prime Hunters: First Hunt","p":["Nintendo DS"],"r":"November 21"},{"t":"Metroid: Zero Mission","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"u":"Nintendo","r":"February 9, 2004"},{"t":"Michigan: Report from Hell","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Grasshopper Manufacture","u":"Spike, 505 GameStreet","g":"Adventure, Survival horror","r":"August 5, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michigan:_Report_from_Hell","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co9mbd.jpg","s":"Michigan: Report from Hell, released as Michigan in Japan, is a survival horror game developed by Grasshopper Manufacture and published by Spike. It was released in Japan on August 5, 2004, in Europe on September 30, 2005, and in Australia in 2005. This game was never released in North America. Directed by Akira Ueda and planned by Goichi Suda, the game focuses on a news crew for the fictional ZaKa TV, dedicated to covering strange phenomena. The game is unique in the sense that it is played almost entirely though the viewfinder of a camera; and the game is lost if the player runs out of film before solving the mysteries in a mission."},{"t":"Midway Arcade Treasures 2","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox","GameCube"],"d":"Digital Eclipse","u":"Midway","g":"Various","r":"October 11, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midway_Arcade_Treasures_2"},{"t":"Might and Magic Mobile","p":["Nintendo DS"],"d":"Gameloft Beijing","u":"Gameloft","g":"Action-adventure","r":"October 19, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Might_and_Magic_Mobile","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co8d9e.jpg","s":"For centuries, Erathia has been devastated by a war between humans and demons. To make matters worse, the king is being held prisoner by the demon armies. The hero, Ewan, is sent to rescue the king by a mysterious nobleman. His quest will result in encounters with an elf archer, a captain of mercenaries and countless other friends and foes. The monstrous kidnappers will try to set traps in these hostile environments, but any hero knows to proceed with caution when dealing with demons."},{"t":"Mission: Impossible – Operation Surma","p":["GameCube"],"r":"March 23"},{"t":"MLB 2005","p":["PlayStation","PlayStation 2"],"d":"San Diego Studio","u":"Sony Computer Entertainment","g":"Sports","r":"March 16, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MLB_2005","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/wmeracfsphnnutm8l5ic.jpg","s":"The MLB (Year#) series, is a series of Major League Baseball video games by Sony Computer Entertainment published under their 989 Sports label. The series was originally developed by Sony Interactive Studios America, who later became 989 Studios until eventually merging into Sony Computer Entertainment America. Following the merge the games were released under the 989 Sports brand up until 2006. Following that, MLB games from SCEA were released by SCEA San Diego under the MLB: The Show series."},{"t":"MLB Slugfest: Loaded","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"Point of View","u":"Midway Sports","g":"Sports","r":"June 21, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MLB_Slugfest:_Loaded","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co5dgn.jpg","s":"Action baseball game, featuring Midway's classic fast and furious gameplay with beanballs, hard tags, and over-the-top animations. SlugFest features some of the greatest baseball players with the addition of over-the-top abilities, including turbo-speed running, highlight reel-worthy fielding, Earth-shaking collisions and the ability to catch fire and turbo charge the game action. All-new gameplay features add customizable replay, exploding Scoreboards, and updated MLB team rosters. You can also take your coaching skills, players and/or teams online, voice chat with other players, and access an on-screen sports Ticker Tape. Also features an Online Tournament Mode and a soundtrack featuring Ivory Wire, Buckfast Superbee and Flipswitch."},{"t":"Mob Enforcer","p":["Windows"],"d":"Touchdown Entertainment","u":"ValuSoft, Kemco U.S.A.","g":"First-person shooter","r":"June 11, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mob_Enforcer","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co8z9j.jpg","s":"Mob Enforcer is a video game published in 2004 on Windows by ValuSoft, Inc.. It's an action game, set in a shooter, interwar and crime themes."},{"t":"Mobile Suit Gundam: Gundam vs. Zeta Gundam","p":["PlayStation 2","GameCube"],"d":"Capcom","u":"Bandai","g":"Action, Mecha simulation, Third-person shooter, Hack and slash, Air combat simulation and Naval combat simulation","r":"December 9, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mobile_Suit_Gundam:_Gundam_vs._Zeta_Gundam","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co9ded.jpg","s":"Mobile Suit Gundam: Gundam vs. Zeta Gundam takes place seven years after the end of the devastating One-Year War, with the Titans police force assuming dictatorial powers. As the A.E.U.G. rebel group struggles to defeat the Titans, the heroes and villains of the original Mobile Suit Gundam series find themselves on the same side of this new conflict. You can choose whether to play as a member of the A.E.U.G. or Titans, and strap yourself into one of 31 new mobile suits. Practice your maneuvering skills in single-player story mode or take on a friend in multiplayer battles."},{"t":"Mobile Suit Z Gundam: Hot Scramble","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"March 18"},{"t":"Monster Garage","p":["Windows","Xbox"],"d":"Invictus Games, Impulse Games","u":"Activision Value","g":"Simulation","r":"January 21, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monster_Garage_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/dzelsxdaveapby2xe2em.jpg"},{"t":"Monster Hunter","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Capcom Production Studio 1","u":"Capcom","g":"Action role-playing","r":"March 11, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monster_Hunter_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2w44.jpg","s":"Monster Hunter is an online action-hunting game by CAPCOM for the PlayStation 2 released on March 11th, 2004 in Japan, and September 21st, 2004 in North America. The game is a fantasy hunting simulator filled with many deadly monsters. Like actual hunting, successfully killing or capturing the monsters requires significant strategy, skill and involved resource management. While initially considered a commercial failure, Monster Hunter would go on to become one of CAPCOM's highest selling franchises.\n\nDespite featuring an offline mode, Monster Hunter was primarily an online game. The official servers were shut down on December 31, 2007 in North America and Europe, and July 1, 2011 in Japan. This means that it is now impossible to play online on official CAPCOM servers. Despite this, the game still features a small active community on private servers."},{"t":"Monster Trux: Arenas","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Data Design Interactive","u":"Phoenix Games B.V., Metro3D Europe, Data Design Interactive, Conspiracy Entertainment","g":"Racing","r":"December 10, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monster_Trux:_Arenas"},{"t":"Mortal Kombat: Deception","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"October 4"},{"t":"Mr. Driller Drill Spirits","p":["Nintendo DS"],"r":"November 30","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mr._Driller_Drill_Spirits"},{"t":"MTV Music Generator 3","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MTV_Music_Generator_3"},{"t":"MTX Mototrax","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox","Windows"],"r":"March 2","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MTX_Mototrax"},{"t":"Mudcraft","p":["Windows"],"d":"The LlamaPad","u":"The LlamaPad","g":"Real-time strategy","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mudcraft"},{"t":"Mushihimesama","p":["Arcade"],"d":"Cave","u":"AMI, Taito, Cave, Degica","g":"Vertically scrolling shooter, bullet hell","r":"October 12, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mushihimesama","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/cobkwg.jpg","s":"Mushihimesama is a manic shooter developed by Cave and released by Taito in 2004. It was ported to the PlayStation 2 in 2005 and iOS in 2011. An Xbox 360 port was released in May 2012 (with ver1.5 as first print DLC). A significantly changed \"version 1.5\" was released to arcades in 2011. The game has an insect theme as all of the enemies resemble various insects such as beetles and butterflies. The game is set in various forest environments. It received a sequel in 2006, known as Mushihimesama Futari, and a spin-off iOS game entitled Mushihimesama Bug Panic."},{"t":"MVP Baseball 2004","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox","GameCube"],"u":"EA Sports","r":"March 9, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MVP_Baseball_series"},{"t":"MX Unleashed","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox","Mobile phone"],"d":"Rainbow Studios, Humagade","u":"THQ","g":"Racing","r":"February 17, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MX_Unleashed","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co6dx3.jpg","s":"MX Unleashed is a motocross racing game for PlayStation 2, Xbox, and mobile phone. It was developed by Rainbow Studios and Humagade, published by THQ, and released in 2004. It was the first game in the MX series to be developed by Rainbow Studios"},{"t":"Myst IV: Revelation","p":["Windows"],"g":"Adventure, Casual","r":"September 28","l":"https://store.steampowered.com/app/925940","i":"images/steam-925940.jpg","s":"In Myst IV: Revelation, the next chapter in the greatest adventure saga of all time, you'll travel through environments pulsing with life to unearth a treacherous scheme involving two of Myst's most sinister villains."},{"t":"N","p":["Windows","Nintendo DS"],"r":"March 1","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/N_(video_game)"},{"t":"Nancy Drew: Curse of Blackmoor Manor","p":["Windows"],"u":"DreamCatcher Interactive","g":"Adventure","r":"October 5, 2004","l":"https://store.steampowered.com/app/31830","i":"images/steam-31830.jpg","s":"Delve into Dark Legends Lurking in the Shadow of an Old English Mansion!"},{"t":"Nancy Drew: The Secret of Shadow Ranch","p":["Windows"],"g":"Adventure","r":"August 30","l":"https://store.steampowered.com/app/572740","i":"images/steam-572740.jpg","s":"Take a Wild Ride into Terror and Trickery to Rein in a Ghostly Secret!"},{"t":"Nanosaur 2: Hatchling","p":["macOS","Windows"],"d":"Pangea Software","u":"Pangea Software","g":"Third-person shooter","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nanosaur_2:_Hatchling","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2zax.jpg","s":"As a genetically-engineered pterodactyl, players fight against insurgent dinosaur forces in order to save Earth."},{"t":"Naruto Ninja Council 2","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"d":"Aspect, Tomy","u":"Tomy, D3 Publisher","g":"Beat-'Em-Up","r":"April 29, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Naruto_Ninja_Council_2"},{"t":"Naruto: Ultimate Ninja 2","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"CyberConnect2","u":"Bandai, Namco Bandai Games","g":"Fighting game","r":"September 30, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Naruto:_Ultimate_Ninja_2","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1u9f.jpg","s":"\"The ultimate ninja battle returns!\n\nBattle the best in the land with intense, anime-style head-to-head ninja fighting with over 30 playable characters and 16 unique stages. Choose from more than 60 exciting missions, test your skills with challenging mini-games or play through the anime storyline - and even unlock an original story - in the all-new mode, Ultimate Road. Earn money and points to unlock tons of bonus content as you unleash your chakra and ascend the ranks on your way to becoming the greatest ninja of all!\""},{"t":"NASCAR 2005: Chase for the Cup","p":["GameCube"],"u":"EA Sports","r":"September 4, 2004"},{"t":"NBA Ballers","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"Midway","u":"Midway Sports","g":"Sports","r":"April 5, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NBA_Ballers","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co6tv9.jpg","s":"NBA Ballers is the exclusive one-on-one basketball videogame highlighting the \"bling-bling\" lifestyle of NBA Superstars; chromed-out cars, ice, ladies, tatts and jets all hinge on the killer cross-over. NBA Ballers also features NBA Legends dropping dimes and dunking in your grill to determine who is the greatest baller of all time. 60+ NBA Players: Including Kobe Bryant, Vince Carter, Allen Iverson, Kevin Garnett, Shaquille O’Neal, Yao Ming, Steve Francis, Chris Webber, Gary Payton, Latrell Sprewell, and more! 24 NBA Legends: Including Rick Barry, Larry Bird, Wilt Chamberlain, Clyde Drexler, Julius Irving, Magic Johnson, Bill Russell, Jerry West, James Worthy, and more!"},{"t":"NBA Live 2005","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox","GameCube","Windows"],"d":"EA Canada","u":"Electronic Arts","g":"Sports","r":"September 28, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NBA_Live_2005","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2gna.jpg","s":"NBA Live 2005 is the 2004 installment of the NBA Live video games series. The cover features Carmelo Anthony as a member of the Denver Nuggets. The game was developed by EA Sports and released in 2004 for PlayStation 2, Xbox, Nintendo GameCube, and Windows."},{"t":"NCAA Football 2005","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox","GameCube"],"u":"EA Sports","r":"July 15, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NCAA_Football_2005"},{"t":"NCAA March Madness 2005","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"EA Canada","u":"EA Sports","g":"Sports","r":"November 16, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NCAA_March_Madness_2005","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/suayly6sp2xzlb0vvmsq.jpg","s":"NCAA March Madness 2005 is the 2004 installment in the NCAA March Madness series. Former Connecticut, Charlotte Bobcats, New Orleans Hornets, Washington Wizards, and New Orleans Pelicans player, and current NBA free agent player Emeka Okafor is featured on the cover."},{"t":"Need for Speed: Underground 2","p":["Windows","GameCube","PlayStation 2","Xbox","Game Boy Advance","Nintendo DS"],"r":"November 15"},{"t":"Neighbours from Hell 2: On Vacation","p":["Windows"],"d":"JoWooD Vienna","u":"JoWooD Productions, Cinemaware, THQ Nordic","g":"Puzzle, strategy","r":"February 20, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neighbours_from_Hell_2:_On_Vacation","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co9x12.jpg","s":"The reality TV show of neighbourly nastiness and community commotion moves on to the next round.\n\nThe Neighbour from Hell wants to enjoy an undeserved holiday – reason enough for Woody and the camera team to sneak along onto the cruise liner to make the nasty neighbour's holiday a living hell. This time, the neighbour's mum has joined him, and she is taking good care of her baby.\n\nGet the Neighbour from Hell into his mum's and fellow travellers' bad books, play tricks on him and give free reign to your vengeance."},{"t":"Neo Contra","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"October 19","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neo_Contra"},{"t":"Neocron 2: Beyond Dome of York","p":["Windows"],"d":"Reakktor Media GmbH","u":"10tacle Studios","g":"Shooter, Role-playing (RPG)","r":"September 29, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neocron_2:_Beyond_Dome_of_York","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co5v6w.jpg","s":"Neocron 2: Beyond Dome of York is a 2004 video game which is a follow-up to 2002's Neocron. Originally slated to be an expansion pack Neocron 2 was released separately under a new publisher, 10tacle Studios AG.\n\nNeocron 2 features a large persistent world and massive multiplayer gaming. Divided into two factions, Neocron and Dome of York, and separated by the vast radiated wastelands between the cities, the players try to build a career in one of the many industrial and military organizations. There are various player classes offered, including different types of fighters, PSI powered monks and hackers. The game allows free exploring of the world, NPC missions or engaging in PvP-combat, using an Egoshooter-like interface for gameplay and fighting.\n\nNoteworthy features, amongst others, are the Hacknet (a network similar to the matrix of the pen&paper-game Shadowrun) which allows skilled hackers to travel the whole game-world through a great number of network nodes or attack enemy bases and the usability of driving and flying vehicles in the wastelands."},{"t":"Neon Genesis Evangelion: Shinji Ikari Raising Project","p":["Windows"],"g":"Simulator, Visual Novel","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neon_Genesis_Evangelion:_Shinji_Ikari_Raising_Project","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2wlr.jpg","s":"Neon Genesis Evangelion: Shinji Ikari Raising Project (新世紀エヴァンゲリオン 碇シンジ育成計画 Shin Seiki Evangerion: Ikari Shinji Ikusei Keikaku) is a computer game based on the anime series Neon Genesis Evangelion. The player assumes control of Shinji Ikari, the protagonist and main character of the normal Neon Genesis Evangelion series, in the expanded alternate universe that was glimpsed upon for a few moments in the TV episode 26. Basically, the player decides Shinji's fate in how he lives his life. The story begins with the attack of the 3rd Angel, much like the anime. Different decisions and actions lead to various outcomes etc."},{"t":"Neverwinter Nights: Kingmaker","p":["Windows"],"d":"BioWare","u":"Atari Interactive","g":"Role-playing","r":"November 10, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neverwinter_Nights:_Kingmaker"},{"t":"Nexus: The Jupiter Incident","p":["Windows"],"d":"Mithis Entertainment","u":"HD Interactive, THQ Nordic","g":"Real-time tactics, Space combat simulator","r":"November 5, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nexus:_The_Jupiter_Incident","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co256f.jpg","s":"At the dawn of the 22nd century, the conquest of space and the colonization of the solar system is being monopolized by several huge and ambitious mega-corporations. Although extremely delicate and vulnerable, a balance is maintained by these companies. At the very edge of the solar system the companies make a discovery which will shift the technological advantage and upset the balance. And so a new conflict is born: \"The Jupiter Incident\".\n\nNexus - The Jupiter Incident is a real-time mission-based tactical space game featuring spectacular real time battles and breathtaking motion picture quality. Focus on tactics and action as you control up to a dozen battleships encountering aliens, unknown solar systems and astrophysical phenomena in your struggle to save Earth."},{"t":"NFL GameDay 2005","p":["PlayStation"],"r":"August 1","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NFL_GameDay_2005"},{"t":"NFL Street","p":["PlayStation 2","GameCube","Xbox"],"d":"EA Tiburon","u":"EA Sports BIG","g":"Sports","r":"January 13, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NFL_Street","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2ekg.jpg","s":"NFL Street is a series of sports video games developed by EA Tiburon and published by Electronic Arts. It combines the talent and big names of the NFL with the atmosphere of street football"},{"t":"NFL Street 2","p":["GameCube","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"December 22","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NFL_Street_2"},{"t":"NHL 2005","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2","GameCube","Xbox"],"d":"EA Black Box","u":"EA Sports","g":"Sports","r":"September 14, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NHL_2005","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2got.jpg","s":"Capture all the speed, finesse, and action of professional hockey with NHL 2005, the successor to NHL 2004. The game's new EA Sports Open Ice Control lets you execute offensive plays, such as a give-and-go and a breakaway pass, and you can also call for defensive double-teams. Dynasty mode has been enhanced with more interactive GM/owner relationships, including a new e-mail system. NHL 2005 also delivers all the action of the World Cup of Hockey with International Teams and venues from North America and Europe."},{"t":"NHL Eastside Hockey Manager","p":["Windows"],"d":"Sports Interactive","u":"Sega","g":"Sports, ice hockey","r":"September 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NHL_Eastside_Hockey_Manager"},{"t":"Nicktoons Movin'","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Mass Media","u":"THQ","g":"Action, party","r":"October 22, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nicktoons_Movin'"},{"t":"Nicktoons: Freeze Frame Frenzy","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"d":"Altron","u":"THQ","g":"Photography","r":"September 27, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nicktoons:_Freeze_Frame_Frenzy","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co68ql.jpg","s":"NICKTOONS characters from THE FAIRLY ODDPARENTS, SPONGEBOB SQUAREPANTS, ROCKET POWER, JIMMY NEUTRON, and DANNY PHANTOM come together in an all new adventure for Game Boy Advance called NICKTOONS: FREEZE FRAME FRENZY. This game also marks the first appearance in a video game by the characters in RUGRATS: ALL GROWN UP. The characters from the popular television shows and evildoers work to move through a number of cartoon settings in order to solve different puzzles in this unique venture. Nicktoons characters are surfacing in places that they don't belong and confusion has followed. Jimmy Neutron, the boy genius has used his advanced intellect to come up with a plan to work through this strange situation. Jimmy has enlisted the help of his fellow Nicktoon friends to get to the bottom of the strange occurrences. The object of the game is to take a picture of each lost character and send them back to their corresponding show. Choose from 8 different Nicktoon characters to search through different shows like HEY ARNOLD, SPONGEBOB SQUAREPANTS, THE FAIRLY ODDPARENTS, AND WILD THORNBERRIES. The game begins with THE FAIRLY ODDPARENTS and progresses to the other show as the player unlocks the levels. Photographers are sent out into each show and the vertical scrolling adventure begins with characters moving onto the screen. New characters can be unlocked with enough points accumulated by taking photos. Fans of Nicktoons and any of the characters featured in this game are in for the most unique treat watching different characters interact in atypical surroundings."},{"t":"Nightshade","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"February 10","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nightshade_(2003_video_game)"},{"t":"Ninja Gaiden","p":["Xbox"],"u":"Tecmo","r":"March 2, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ninja_Gaiden_(2004_video_game)"},{"t":"North Wind","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_Wind_(video_game)"},{"t":"Notpron","p":["Browser"],"d":"David Münnich","g":"Puzzle game","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Notpron","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4s5o.jpg","s":"Notpron is an online puzzle game and internet riddle created in 2004 by German game developer David Münnich. It has been hailed by fans, journalists, and Münnich himself as \"the hardest riddle available on the internet\".\n\nRegarded as one of the first of the online puzzle game genre, Notpron follows a standard puzzle game layout, where the player is presented with a webpage containing a riddle and must find the answer to the riddle in order to proceed to the next webpage."},{"t":"O-Chan no Oekaki Logic","p":["PlayStation","Sega Saturn","Super Nintendo Entertainment System","WonderSwan","Mobile phone"],"d":"Sunsoft","u":"Sunsoft","g":"Puzzle, Nonogram","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/O-Chan_no_Oekaki_Logic"},{"t":"Ojamajo Adventure: Naisho no Mahō","p":["Windows"],"d":"Amada Printing","g":"Visual novel","r":"November 19, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ojamajo_Adventure:_Naisho_no_Mah%C5%8D"},{"t":"Ollie King","p":["Arcade"],"d":"Amusement Vision","u":"Sega","g":"Racing, platform","r":"March 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ollie_King","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/kykimrexl79decglqjuv.jpg","s":"Brought to you by the makers of the Jet Set Radio games, Ollie King is an arcade skateboarding game released in 2003."},{"t":"Onimusha 3: Demon Siege","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Capcom, Sourcenext","u":"Capcom, Sourcenext, Ubisoft","g":"Action-adventure, hack and slash","r":"February 26, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Onimusha_3:_Demon_Siege","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4qts.jpg","s":"Onimusha 3 is the third game of the Onimusha series. The game retains elements from previous games in the franchise including the use of multiple special weapons in order to fight enemies and absorb their energy to enhance the weaponry. This time the player primarily controls both Samanosuke and Jacques in separate scenarios. The two are able to exchange items in order to solve puzzles. The development from this game started after the release of the PlayStation 2 which allowed the team to work on a 3D engine to design 3D backgrounds. In order to appeal to the Western market, the team set this game in Paris and chose French actor Jean Reno to portray Jacques.\n\nOnimusha 3 has been generally well received by publications for video games. Most of the writer's praise focused on the improved controls and the use of a 3D engine that allowed better combat and visuals, respectively. The game also generated good sales with over 1.5 million copies sold as of May 2008."},{"t":"Oolite","p":["Windows","Linux","macOS"],"d":"Giles Williams, Jens Ayton","u":"Giles Williams, Jens Ayton","g":"Space trading and combat simulator","r":"July 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oolite_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1pcy.jpg","s":"Oolite is a space sim game, inspired by Elite, powered by Objective-C and OpenGL, and designed as a small game that is easy for users to pick up, modify and expand upon. Almost every aspect of the game can be changed by using simple, free graphics packages and text editors."},{"t":"OpenTTD","p":["Windows","macOS","Linux"],"g":"Simulator, Strategy, Indie","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OpenTTD","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1ngl.jpg","s":"OpenTTD is a business simulation game initially developed by Ludvig Strigeus in which players earn money by transporting passengers and cargo via road, rail, water, and air. It is an open-source remake and expansion of the 1995 Chris Sawyer video game Transport Tycoon Deluxe.\n\nConnect industries and cities on procedurally-generated maps of up to 4096 x 4096 tiles by building a network of roads, railways, docks, and airports. Navigate dense city streets, cross oceans and rivers, and conquer high mountains in one of four climates.\n\nWork alone or with friends to complete production chains and transport finished goods to towns. Assemble a fleet of hundreds of vehicles, transferring cargo as needed in an interconnected, multimodal network with optional cargo destinations.\n\nKeep up with technological improvements through the years as towns grow; new modes of transport are invented; and industries appear, change production, or fail. Expand stations and build network capacity to keep up with demand and avoid delays.\n\nCustomize your OpenTTD experience via community-made mods downloaded through an in-game content service, including real-world vehicles, new industry sets, custom scenarios, and more.\n\nOpenTTD is free and open-source software, licensed under the GNU General Public License version 2.0. OpenTTD is under ongoing development. OpenTTD is not an abbreviation of anything."},{"t":"Operation Shadow","p":["N-Gage"],"d":"Torus Games","u":"Nokia","g":"Action-adventure","r":"September 29, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operation_Shadow","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3wrf.jpg","s":"Operation Shadow is an ACtion Adventure game for the N-Gage"},{"t":"Out of the Park Baseball 6","p":["Windows"],"u":"Out of the Park Developments","r":"June 14, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Out_of_the_Park_Baseball"},{"t":"Outdoor Life: Sportsman's Challenge","p":["Windows"],"d":"Cat Daddy Games","u":"Take-Two Interactive","g":"Business simulation game","r":"October 5, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Outdoor_Life:_Sportsman's_Challenge"},{"t":"Outpost Kaloki","p":["Xbox 360","Windows"],"d":"NinjaBee","u":"Microsoft Game Studios","g":"City-building","r":"September 18, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Outpost_Kaloki","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4wnw.jpg","s":"A space station tycoon game where you strive to satisfy visiting aliens while running a financially successful space station."},{"t":"OutRun 2","p":["Xbox"],"r":"October 25","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OutRun_2"},{"t":"Pac-Man","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"February 14","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pac-Man"},{"t":"Pac-Man World","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"November 17","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pac-Man_World"},{"t":"Pacific Fighters","p":["Windows"],"d":"1C:Maddox Games","u":"1C Company, Ubisoft","g":"Combat flight simulation game","r":"October 21, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pacific_Fighters","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co9nfo.jpg","s":"Pacific Fighters is a World War II Combat flight simulation game. It is in fact a stand-alone expansion pack of IL-2 Sturmovik.\n\nPacific Fighters focuses on the Pacific theater, with theater-appropriate aircraft, as well as aircraft carriers and battleships. The game gives the player 74 flyable aircraft, including variants. It has two types of missions that can be flown, \"dogfights\" or \"cooperative campaign\" modes. In either type, the player can play as either Allied or Axis forces, and the type of aircraft flown usually depends on the mission picked. The game also features a mission editor, allowing the player to make their own missions."},{"t":"Painkiller","p":["Windows"],"g":"Action","r":"April 12","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Painkiller_(game)","i":"images/steam-2300120.jpg","s":"The classic Painkiller series is back! Battle through Purgatory in fast-paced co-op action, wielding infernal weapons against relentless demonic hordes. Condemned for your sins, the Voice of the Creator offers you a chance at redemption. Will you seize it or be lost to darkness?"},{"t":"Painkiller: Battle out of Hell","p":["Windows"],"r":"December 1","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Painkiller_(video_game)#Battle_Out_of_Hell"},{"t":"PangYa","p":["Windows"],"d":"Ntreev Soft","u":"Smilegate Megaport, NHN Corp., Smilegate Europe","g":"Golf, MMORPG","r":"June 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PangYa","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2x9z.jpg","s":"PangYa is a fantasy-themed online multiplayer golf game where players compete on vibrant, imaginative courses. With anime-inspired characters, customizable outfits, and special power shots, it offers a fun twist on traditional golf. Players can enjoy various game modes, including tournaments, team battles, and seasonal events, all while earning in-game currency (Pang) to unlock new gear. Social features like guilds and mini-games add to the community experience, making PangYa an exciting blend of golf, fantasy, and strategy."},{"t":"Panzer Front Ausf.B","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Enterbrain","u":"505 Games","g":"Vehicle simulation game","r":"March 27, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Panzer_Front_Ausf.B","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/ttefts3zgtz3obn9arzh.jpg","s":"You are sent out to the North African front of WWII where hell has broken loose. As the commander of a tank squadron you are going to need all your nerves, wits and strategy to succeed in your mission and gain victory."},{"t":"Paper Mario: The Thousand-Year Door","p":["GameCube"],"u":"Nintendo","r":"July 22, 2004"},{"t":"Pardus","p":["Browser"],"d":"Bayer&Szell OG","u":"Bayer&Szell OG","g":"MMORPG space simulation browser game","r":"September 14, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pardus_(video_game)"},{"t":"Parkan II","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parkan_II"},{"t":"Pathway to Glory","p":["N-Gage"],"d":"Ubisoft RedLynx","u":"Nokia","g":"Turn-based tactics","r":"November 24, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pathway_to_Glory","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co63g4.jpg","s":"Pathway to Glory is a military turn-based strategy game for the N-Gage. One of the rare worthwhile exclusives on the N-Gage platform, Pathway to Glory is considered a cult classic and lost gem by most turn-based tactics fans."},{"t":"Peace@Pieces","p":["Windows"],"d":"Unisonshift","u":"Unisonshift","g":"Eroge, Visual novel","r":"December 23, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peace@Pieces"},{"t":"Perimeter","p":["Windows"],"d":"K-D Lab","u":"1C Company, Codemasters","g":"Real-time strategy","r":"May 21, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Perimeter_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2fyo.jpg","s":"Perimeter is an innovative Real-Time-Strategy game that pits players against each other or AI opponents in a life and death struggle to seize territory and establish critical protective “perimeters.” Players will be introduced to the game’s unique “terraforming” feature, allowing them to move, build, construct and destroy the map environment. Set in a future where the Exodus civilization has abandoned the dying Earth, the game offers a well-balanced combination of new terraforming principles and territorial wars with traditional strategy elements."},{"t":"Phantom Brave","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Nippon Ichi Software","u":"Nippon Ichi Software, NIS America, Koei","g":"Tactical role-playing game","r":"January 22, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phantom_Brave","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3bg0.jpg","s":"Phantom Brave is a strategy RPG which takes place in the world of Ivoire. Ivoire consists of vast seas and numerous islands; it used to be a peaceful place, but an ancient (and powerful) force is now threatening life in the various lands. The character you control in the game is Marona, a 13 year old orphaned girl. Marona has the ability to communicate with phantoms, an ability that brings a lot of resentment from other people but will help her to head out into the world and solve the problems that are occurring. A phantom known as Ash acts as Marona's guardian; as the game progresses, other phantoms will join your party, each of which have different capabilities.\n\nThe game features a turn based combat system. During battles, Marona is able to attack enemies by herself, and she can also summon phantoms in her party to help out. To summon phantoms, you will need to confine them to an object on the screen (such as a rock or tree). Once confined to an object, you will then be able to control the phantom in battle, though phantoms only remain controllable for a limited number of turns. The object you confine a phantom to will affect it's abilities; for example, a rock may make a phantom stronger but move slower. By defeating enemies in battle you earn experience points allowing to level up and become more powerful."},{"t":"Phoenix Wright: Ace Attorney – Trials and Tribulations","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"d":"Capcom Production Studio 4","u":"Capcom","g":"Visual novel, adventure","r":"January 23, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phoenix_Wright:_Ace_Attorney_%E2%80%93_Trials_and_Tribulations"},{"t":"Pikmin 2","p":["GameCube"],"u":"Nintendo","r":"April 29, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pikmin_2"},{"t":"Pinball Hall of Fame: The Gottlieb Collection","p":["PlayStation 2","GameCube","PlayStation Portable","Xbox"],"d":"FarSight Studios","u":"Crave Entertainment, Play It","g":"Pinball","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pinball_Hall_of_Fame:_The_Gottlieb_Collection","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1po6.jpg","s":"Pinball Hall of Fame: The Gottlieb Collection is a pinball video game developed by FarSight Studios and published by Crave Entertainment. The tables in the game are recreations of real tables. The game was later released as Gottlieb Pinball Classics, published by System 3, in Europe and Australia. This expanded version featured additional tables and was released in North America on Wii and PSP under the original name, Pinball Hall of Fame: The Gottlieb Collection."},{"t":"Ping Pals","p":["Nintendo DS"],"d":"WayForward Technologies","u":"THQ","g":"Simulation","r":"December 7, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ping_Pals","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/gsnbzyeewhuehe1o2rnk.jpg","s":"A chat program for the DS. Functionally, it's very similar to Pictochat, a program that comes preloaded on all DS units."},{"t":"Pitfall: The Lost Expedition","p":["GameCube","PlayStation 2","Xbox","Game Boy Advance","Windows"],"d":"Edge of Reality, Torus Games, Beenox","u":"Activision, Aspyr","g":"Action, platform","r":"February 17, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pitfall:_The_Lost_Expedition","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1pe2.jpg","s":"Twenty-two years after making his groundbreaking debut on the Atari 2600, Activision's Pitfall Harry returns for more jungle-exploring action. The intrepid adventurer is brought to life for more than 50 perilous levels set in such exotic South American locales as rainforests, glaciers, mines, and ancient ruins. As in the original, players must utilize Harry's athletic prowess to swing from vines, run from rolling logs, hop over treacherous pits, avoid snapping crocodiles, and more, while trying to survive the hostile environment.\n\nHis objectives? To retrieve lost artifacts before they fall into the hands of his rival and to save those in danger. Pitfall Harry will eventually encounter situations that even he can't conquer with a well-timed jump or two, so players can pull items stored in his knapsack to assist him. Like the character's single foray on the original PlayStation, this game is designed to make players smile while exploring the mysterious lands before them. Although Pitfall 3D made use of Bruce Campbell's voice for its comic effect, Pitfall Harry attempts to use its visuals to elicit grins, with the protagonist drawn as a caricature, with a large head balanced atop a slender body.\n\nAs the story begins, Harry is a member of a treasure-hunting expedition whose plane goes down in the forest. The other survivors are scattered throughout the game; an older, wiser adventurer who was on the plane -- and who becomes incapacitated during the accident -- urges Harry to embark on a quest to save them while battling a rival, eco-unfriendly group of treasure hunters for the relics of the jungle so they can be returned to their rightful owners. He hands Harry the \"Hero's Handbook\" and Harry's off to adventure. The \"Hero's Handbook's\" pages are scattered throughout the levels just like the crash survivors are. Find new pages, and Harry will learn new moves."},{"t":"Pixelus","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pixelus"},{"t":"Planetarian: The Reverie of a Little Planet","p":["Windows"],"d":"Key","u":"Visual Arts, KineticNovel, Prototype, Sekai Project","g":"Visual novel","r":"November 29, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Planetarian:_The_Reverie_of_a_Little_Planet","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2z8m.jpg","s":"Planetarian: The Reverie of a Little Planet is a Japanese post-apocalyptic visual novel developed by Key and is rated for all ages. The story centers on a middle-aged man who comes across a malfunctioning robot in a dead city. The man, known simply as \"the junker\", stays with this robot for a time and attempts to fix the projector of the planetarium where the story takes place."},{"t":"Pocket Kingdom: Own the World","p":["N-Gage"],"d":"io-Spiral","u":"Nokia","g":"Massively multiplayer online role-playing game","r":"November 24, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pocket_Kingdom:_Own_the_World","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co63g6.jpg","s":"A massively multiplayer online game centered around removing three griefers from power. The game is very self-referential, and consistently breaks the fourth wall."},{"t":"Pokémon Emerald","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"September 16","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pok%C3%A9mon_Emerald"},{"t":"Pokémon FireRed and LeafGreen","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"January 29","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pok%C3%A9mon_FireRed_and_LeafGreen"},{"t":"Polar Bowler","p":["Windows"],"d":"WildTangent, Engine Software","u":"WildTangent, MumboJumbo","g":"Sports","r":"August 3, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polar_Bowler","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1u5a.jpg","s":"Humorous take on bowling. Aim for strikes at the Chill Pin Alley lanes as you steer Polar Bowler around obstacles and watch him plunge into the pins."},{"t":"Polar Golfer","p":["Windows"],"d":"WildTangent","u":"WildTangent","g":"Sports","r":"September 1, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polar_Golfer","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2nbd.jpg","s":"Play through 9 or 18 holes that trek through gorgeous valleys and alongside inlets. Forget making divots - Polar Golfer has so much talent; he whacks the ball with just one paw! Guide the ball in mid-air and steer it on the putting green with your mouse. Score bonus points and shoot farther with power rings, and unlock Polar Bowler's friends with your high scores. The characters you met and clicked with in Polar Bowler are back in a fun-filled sequel: Polar Golfer! \n9 or 18 hole courses \nYou guide the ball \nEarn bonus points and power rings \nUnlock PB's friends"},{"t":"Pool Paradise","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2","GameCube"],"d":"Awesome Studios","u":"Ignition Entertainment","g":"Sports","r":"April 2, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pool_Paradise","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co6uec.jpg","s":"Pool Paradise lets players experience playing pool in exotic locations in the South Pacific. There are 30 different computer opponents to compete against as well as 10 different table designs to play on. There are 11 different rule types to compete in and 10 different tournaments to compete in. There are five different modes to play in including Practice, Championship, Tournament, Trick Shots and a series of mini-games such as playing a game of darts on the beach, skee ball with cue balls and even shooting coconuts out of a cannon."},{"t":"Pool Shark 2","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox","Windows"],"d":"Blade Interactive","u":"Zoo Digital Publishing","g":"Sports","r":"November 12, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pool_Shark_2","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4jma.jpg","s":"Billiards game simulator created by a company that has been developing the well-known and recognized World Championship Snooker series for many years."},{"t":"Popotan","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Popotan"},{"t":"Port Royale 2","p":["Windows","Mobile phone"],"d":"Ascaron Entertainment, Elkware","u":"Take-Two Interactive, Tri-Synergy, Capcom, Elkware","g":"Business simulation game","r":"April 30, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Port_Royale_2","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3vij.jpg","s":"Conquer the Caribbean with mercantile prowess or buccaneer audacity in this open-world business simulation."},{"t":"Portugal 1111: A Conquista de Soure","p":["Windows"],"d":"Ciberbit","u":"Visão","g":"Real-time strategy","r":"April 22, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Portugal_1111:_A_Conquista_de_Soure","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co5wye.jpg","s":"Portugal 1111: A Conquista de Soure is a real-time strategy game developed by Ciberbit, a Portuguese multimedia company, in partnership with the Municipality of Soure and historians from the University of Coimbra. The game depicts the historical events of the Portuguese Reconquista, when the Christians fought against Moorish invaders."},{"t":"Power Rangers Dino Thunder","p":["GameCube","PlayStation 2","Xbox","Game Boy Advance"],"r":"September 14","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Power_Rangers_Dino_Thunder"},{"t":"Powerdrome","p":["Atari ST","Amiga","MS-DOS"],"u":"Electronic Arts","g":"Racing","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Powerdrome"},{"t":"Powerdrome","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"Argonaut Sheffield","u":"Mud Duck Productions, Evolved Games, Zoo Digital Publishing","g":"Racing","r":"June 15, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Powerdrome_(2004_video_game)"},{"t":"Predator","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Predator_(mobile_game)"},{"t":"Premier Manager 2004–2005","p":["Game Boy Advance","PlayStation 2","Windows"],"d":"Zoo Digital Publishing","u":"Zoo Digital Publishing","g":"Sports","r":"November 5, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Premier_Manager_2004%E2%80%932005"},{"t":"Prince of Persia: Warrior Within","p":["Windows","GameCube","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"g":"Action, Adventure","r":"December 2","l":"https://store.steampowered.com/app/13500","i":"images/steam-13500.jpg","s":"Enter the dark underworld of Prince of Persia Warrior Within, the sword-slashing sequel to the critically acclaimed Prince of Persia: The Sands of Time™. Hunted by Dahaka, an immortal incarnation of Fate seeking divine retribution, the Prince embarks upon a path of both carnage and mystery to defy his preordained death."},{"t":"Pro Evolution Soccer 3","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2"],"r":"February 17","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pro_Evolution_Soccer_3"},{"t":"Pro Evolution Soccer 4","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox","Windows"],"u":"Konami","r":"August 5, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pro_Evolution_Soccer_4"},{"t":"Pro Fishing Challenge","p":["Xbox"],"d":"Opus","u":"Atlus","g":"Fishing","r":"August 31, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pro_Fishing_Challenge","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/sewj5h8j1b9jbreevw6x.jpg","s":"The most realistic fishing game to date. With the ability to play with up to 8 players online."},{"t":"Psi-Ops: The Mindgate Conspiracy","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"June 14"},{"t":"Psychotoxic","p":["Windows"],"d":"NuClearVision Entertainment","u":"Vidis, Whiptail Interactive","g":"First-person shooter","r":"September 3, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Psychotoxic","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co908k.jpg","s":"PsychoToxic places gamers in the shoes of heroine Angie Prophet who is faced with the daunting task of saving mankind from impending Nuclear Armageddon.\n\nThe year is 2022, the place is New York City.\n\nAngie Prophet... half human, half angel... is the only one who can defeat the Fourth Horseman of the Apocalypse, an evil character from ancient Babylon.\n\nThroughout the game, Angie comes to an understanding of her role as civilization's savior, discovering a series of unique abilities, such as invisibility, the slowing of time and the infiltration of other's dreams all of which aid her progress."},{"t":"Puyo Pop Fever","p":["GameCube"],"r":"July 20","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Puyo_Pop_Fever"},{"t":"Quest of D","p":["Arcade"],"d":"Sega AM2","u":"Sega","g":"Action role-playing game, digital collectible card game","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quest_of_D"},{"t":"R-Type Final","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"February 2","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/R-Type_Final"},{"t":"RalliSport Challenge 2","p":["Xbox"],"u":"Microsoft Game Studios","r":"May 4, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/RalliSport_Challenge_2"},{"t":"Ran Online","p":["Windows"],"d":"Min Communications, Inc.","u":"GameSamba","g":"MMORPG","r":"April 20, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ran_Online","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/cockhc.jpg","s":"MMORPG set in modern times. Each faction is a school campus."},{"t":"Ratchet & Clank: Up Your Arsenal","p":["PlayStation 2"],"u":"Sony Computer Entertainment","r":"November 3, 2004"},{"t":"Red Dead Revolver","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"May 4","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_Dead_Revolver"},{"t":"Red Skies Over Europe","p":["Windows"],"d":"Interactive Vision","u":"Akella","g":"Action, flight simulator","r":"October 10, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_Skies_Over_Europe"},{"t":"Red Stone","p":["Windows"],"d":"L&K Logic Korea","u":"GamenGame, GameOn, L&K Logic Korea","g":"Fantasy, MMORPG","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_Stone"},{"t":"Remember 11: The Age of Infinity","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"KID","u":"KID, Success, Cyberfront, Mages","g":"Visual novel","r":"March 18, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Remember_11:_The_Age_of_Infinity","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co5rw6.jpg","s":"Remember11: The Age of Infinity is a visual novel video game.\nIt is the third entry in the Infinity series; it is preceded by Never7: The End of Infinity and Ever17: The Out of Infinity, and followed by 12Riven: The Psi-Climinal of Integral and Code_18."},{"t":"Requiem of Hell","p":["N-Gage"],"d":"Digital Red","u":"Nokia","g":"Roleplaying Game","r":"November 22, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Requiem_of_Hell","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co63gd.jpg","s":"When a master demon from Hell named Dalu raises an army of undead, demons and fiends to ravage the world, an old wizard (Shaman) steps forth to stop Dalu and his forces. In a pitched battle, Shaman uses most of his power to decimate much of the demon army and fools Dalu into fleeing briefly. However, the old man realizes his weakened state won't stand up to another assault once Dalu returns from Hell. Shaman tells the fairy accompanying him (Gigi) to choose and revive a recently killed corpse that can fight against Dalu's minions and eventually gain enough power to defeat Dalu. After the introductory cinema, the player can choose to revive either a male (Troy) or female (Linda) who will take on enemies in different (and increasingly tougher) levels as the game progresses. Each character has a back story that ties them together, but the tragic connection between the two only becomes apparent as the endgame approaches..."},{"t":"Resident Evil Outbreak","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"March 31","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Resident_Evil_Outbreak"},{"t":"Resident Evil Outbreak: File 2","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Capcom","u":"Capcom","g":"Survival horror","r":"September 9, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Resident_Evil_Outbreak:_File_2"},{"t":"Return to Mysterious Island","p":["Windows"],"d":"Kheops Studio","u":"The Adventure Company","g":"Adventure","r":"November 2, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Return_to_Mysterious_Island","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co220n.jpg","s":"Join intrepid sailor and recent island castaway Mina as she explores the hidden secrets within the Jules Verne classic inspired Mysterious Island. Gather key articles left from the island's previous inhabitants and combine them in unique and interesting ways to stay alive and stay hopeful for rescue. Surviving means more than living off this lush land, but also fending off the haunting resident specter and solving the islands deepest secrets!"},{"t":"RF Online","p":["Windows"],"d":"CCR","u":"CCR International, Codemasters, Lyto, RedFox Games","g":"Science fiction/fantasy MMORPG","r":"August 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/RF_Online","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2enp.jpg","s":"RF Online, which stands for 'Rising Force Online', is a Korean MMORPG that was developed by CCR, and published by Sega in Japan and Codemasters in the United States and Europe. It is a mix of fantasy with science fiction elements and is based upon a three way race versus race versus race system (RvRvR) where the three races of the game do battle through mass player versus player (PvP) battles known as Chip Wars.\n\nOriginally, RF Online was subscription based. However, within October 2007, RF Online became free-to-play, with the addition on an online cash shop where real money can be spent on in-game items."},{"t":"Ribbit King","p":["GameCube","PlayStation 2"],"r":"June 8","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ribbit_King"},{"t":"Richard Burns Rally","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"July 9","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Richard_Burns_Rally"},{"t":"Ricochet Lost Worlds","p":["Windows","Xbox"],"d":"Reflexive Entertainment","u":"Reflexive Entertainment","g":"Breakout clone","r":"April 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ricochet_Lost_Worlds","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2xfb.jpg","s":"With its stunning visuals and sound effects, gripping soundtrack and compelling level design, Ricochet Lost Worlds could quite possibly be the most addictive game ever made. This remarkable breakout action game will entertain your whole family for hours on end! Throw into the mix a slew of innovative power-ups, a new \"Ring Game\" and a level editor where you can make your own levels and you have an unbeatable combination. You just have to download this brick-busting game... it's a blast!"},{"t":"Ricochet Lost Worlds: Recharged","p":["Windows"],"d":"Reflexive Entertainment","u":"Reflexive Entertainment","g":"Breakout game","r":"October 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ricochet_Lost_Worlds:_Recharged","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/coc79y.jpg","s":"The award-winning game play of Ricochet Lost Worlds is back! From the talented minds of designers all over the world comes the most dynamic brick-busting experience ever! This wild and warped game has you smashing your way through over 350 beautiful and exhilarating rounds that are truly the best of the best. With its gorgeous artwork and innovative \"Ring Game\", you need to download it today. Rejuvenated, Reloaded...RECHARGED!"},{"t":"Ridge Racer","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"u":"Namco","r":"December 12, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ridge_Racer_(2004_video_game)"},{"t":"Ridge Racer DS","p":["Nintendo DS"],"r":"December 7","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ridge_Racer_64"},{"t":"Rise of Nations: Thrones and Patriots","p":["Windows"],"u":"Microsoft Game Studios","r":"April 27, 2004"},{"t":"Robotech: Invasion","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"Vicious Cycle Software","u":"Global Star Software","g":"First-person shooter","r":"October 5, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robotech:_Invasion","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1oz7.jpg","s":"In the 21st century, humankind was freed from the confines of the solar system through the discovery of an alien technology known as Robotech. Contact with the stars also brought war with the Invid, a race of parasitic aliens bent on conquering and transforming the Earth into their new home world."},{"t":"RocketBowl","p":["Windows"],"d":"LargeAnimal","u":"GarageGames","g":"Sports","r":"November 4, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/RocketBowl","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co47ml.jpg","s":"In RocketBowl you will compete in tournaments, challenge your friends in multiplayer, test your skill in mini-games and more."},{"t":"Rockman EXE 4.5 Real Operation","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"d":"Capcom Production Studio 2","u":"Capcom","g":"Real-time tactical role-playing game","r":"August 6, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rockman_EXE_4.5_Real_Operation"},{"t":"Rockman EXE Phantom of Network","p":["Mobile phone"],"u":"Capcom","g":"Real-time tactical role-playing game","r":"October 4, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rockman_EXE_Phantom_of_Network","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co84k8.jpg","s":"Rockman EXE Phantom of Network is a video game in the Mega Man Battle Network series for mobile phones developed by Capcom. The game was only released and made available in Japan. It is most well known for featuring five original characters that did not appear in any other video games: the magician Mr. Hat with his NetNavi HatMan and son Shuichi Ubochi as well as the NetNavis JammingMan and Cache. All of these characters, however, appeared in the Rockman EXE anime series. The game was followed by a Japan-exclusive sequel for mobile phones entitled Rockman EXE Legend of Network."},{"t":"Rockman: Power Battle Fighters","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rockman:_Power_Battle_Fighters"},{"t":"Rocky Legends","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"Venom Games","u":"Ubisoft","g":"Fighting","r":"September 28, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rocky_Legends","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3d3o.jpg","s":"Be Rocky, Apollo Creed, Clubber Lang, or Ivan Drago in this fighting game prequel to the movie series. Using classic Rocky characters, locations, and music, Rocky: Legends puts the player in the boxing, ring recreating or rewriting the careers of the boxing franchise's heroes and villains.\n\nPlay the career mode or jump into a 1-2 player slugfest. As you progress through the career mode, you must train to improve your skills just like a professional would, and use your fight purse to unlock more playable characters, arenas, movie trailers and more. Combinations of punches can be executed powerfully."},{"t":"RollerCoaster Tycoon 3","p":["Windows"],"r":"November 2","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/RollerCoaster_Tycoon_3"},{"t":"Romance of the Three Kingdoms IX","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"February 24","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Romance_of_the_Three_Kingdoms_IX"},{"t":"Romance of the Three Kingdoms X","p":["Windows"],"d":"Koei","u":"Koei","g":"Turn-based strategy","r":"July 2, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Romance_of_the_Three_Kingdoms_X","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4as2.jpg","s":"Romance of the Three Kingdoms X is the tenth installment of the long-running series and takes place right after the fall of the Han Dynasty. It nearly covers 147 years of Chinese history. Gameplay is the same as previous incarnations, an overhead view, letting the player and the CPU move armies, build cities, gather supplies and attack one another, watching the battles from afar.\n\nThere are two different ways to play the game. The player can choose the Historical mode where the characters of the game will follow history to the letter, acting the way the did in real life, but players can also choose a Fictional mode where everything is random and the player can change history as they see fit.\n\nThere are 650 playable characters to choose from, as well as the ability to create over 100 different officers. Players can also trade generals and view stats using online capability."},{"t":"Rome: Total War","p":["Windows"],"u":"Activision","r":"September 22, 2004"},{"t":"RPM Tuning","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Babylon Software","u":"Wanadoo, Kemco, Valusoft","g":"Racing","r":"November 19, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/RPM_Tuning","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co82qe.jpg","s":"RPM Tuning (also known as Top Gear RPM Tuning, and Midnight Outlaw: Six Hours To Sun Up for the PC) is a racing video game released in 2004 and was developed by Babylon Software and published Wanadoo Edition. It is part of the Top Gear game series. This is the only installment in the series to not be released in Japan. North America was only able to see an Xbox release.\n\nThe player assumes the role of Vincent Riker, who is trying to avoid being stopped by the police. Around 40 square miles of Los Angeles have been recreated for the game, including streets and parks.\n\nPlayers can customize their vehicles with up to 221,184 possibilities for mechanical parts and 1,382,976 different possibilities for the exterior; the number of accidents a vehicle sustains also affects performance. There are seven game modes, with 54 different missions in the story mode."},{"t":"Rumble Roses","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Konami Computer Entertainment Tokyo, Yuke's","u":"Konami","g":"Sports, fighting","r":"November 9, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rumble_Roses","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/cod2ab.jpg","s":"Get ready for sexy yet challenging in-the-ring combat. WWX: Rumble Rose delivers intense girl-on-girl wrestling action with an all-female roster of vixens--each with specialty moves. The combat system lets you humiliate your opponents through insults, taunting, and aggressive moves and holds. Your player's costume, attitude, and wrestling style change depending on whether you fight dirty or fair. Naughty or nice, becoming a popular wrestler will earn benefits, including expanded gameplay, additional skills and moves, and more-revealing and flamboyant costumes."},{"t":"Ryzom","p":["Windows","macOS","Linux"],"d":"Nevrax, community contributors","g":"Massively multiplayer online role-playing game","r":"September 16, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ryzom","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2hqi.jpg","s":"Ryzom, also known as The Saga of Ryzom, is a free and open source massively multiplayer online role-playing game developed by Nevrax for Microsoft Windows, OS X, and Linux."},{"t":"Sabotain: Break the Rules","p":["Windows"],"r":"November 12"},{"t":"Sabre Wulf","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"d":"Rare","u":"THQ","g":"Platform","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sabre_Wulf_(2004_video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/cobrwf.jpg","s":"The portable resurrection of a classic Spectrum series.\n\nThe game is separated into two modes of play: the 3D exploration mode and the 2D platforming sections. The 3D exploration mode is how Sabreman gets around the eight different themed worlds of Sabre Wulf. While there are no enemies in this mode, there are plenty of people to talk to, who might help you in your quest. Also strewn about are more than fifty 2D platforming levels, which you can access through the wulf's head tunnels."},{"t":"Sacred","p":["Windows"],"r":"March 19","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sacred_(video_game)"},{"t":"Sacred Plus","p":["Windows"],"r":"October 22","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sacred_(video_game)"},{"t":"Saishū Shiken Kujira","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saish%C5%AB_Shiken_Kujira"},{"t":"Samurai Jack: The Shadow of Aku","p":["GameCube","PlayStation 2"],"r":"March 24"},{"t":"Samurai Shodown V Special","p":["Arcade","Neo Geo AES"],"d":"Yuki Enterprise","u":"SNK Playmore","g":"Fighting","r":"April 22, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Samurai_Shodown_V_Special","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1thg.jpg","s":"An ordained meeting of 28 fierce warriors begins, to precede a series of duels to the death. These individuals entrust their fates to their skill and their weapons. For those not up to the task, a cherished end in battle is their only hope.\n\nThe twenty-eight Samurai characters clash in one epic title. Samurai Shodown V Special was the final release for the Neo Geo. The most iconic addition to this entry in the series is the inclusion of character specific “Overkill Moves”, which can be used to finish off an opponent with style."},{"t":"Samurai Warriors","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"May 6","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Samurai_Warriors"},{"t":"Scaler","p":["GameCube","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"October 1","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scaler_(video_game)"},{"t":"School Tycoon","p":["Windows"],"d":"Cat Daddy Games","u":"Global Star Software","g":"Business simulation game","r":"January 15, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/School_Tycoon","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/m8cpnar2rtyrwjorgy7q.jpg","s":"Build and expand a school in School Tycoon."},{"t":"Scions of Fate","p":["Windows"],"d":"KRG Soft","u":"CDC Games, Gemscool","g":"MMORPG","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scions_of_Fate"},{"t":"Scooby Doo: Mystery Mayhem","p":["GameCube","PlayStation 2","Xbox","Game Boy Advance"],"r":"March 2"},{"t":"Scrapland","p":["Windows"],"r":"December 1","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scrapland"},{"t":"SD Gundam World: Gachapon Senshi - Scramble Wars","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"August 10","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SD_Gundam_World_Gachapon_Senshi"},{"t":"Second Sight","p":["GameCube","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"September 21","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Second_Sight_(video_game)"},{"t":"Sega Superstars","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Sonic Team","u":"Sega","g":"Party","r":"October 22, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sega_Superstars","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1ozt.jpg","s":"There are a total of 12 different full games to play in the main mode of Sega Superstars:\n\nSonic the Hedgehog – As Sonic runs down a round tunnel, he follows the position of the player's hand. Using this method, the aim of the game is to gather rings and Chaos Emeralds in order to obtain the highest score at the end of the game. It is much like the Special Stage on Sonic the Hedgehog 2, Sonic Heroes, and especially Sonic Rush.\nSamba de Amigo – Players choose a song, and then must hit 6 different targets around the screen as the 'beat balls' reach them in time with the music. Posing with hands over 2 of the targets, or holding one position until a trail of beat balls is complete, may also be required from the player.\nChuChu Rocket! – Movement over a certain target on the screen will cause a bridge to raise, which the chu-chus then follow to the goal. The bridge also must be dropped at certain moments to prevent KapuKapus from destroying the score.\nPuyo Pop Fever – Differently colored puyos will fall from the top of the screen, and the player's body must be positioned to guide them into the corresponding pots and allow bombs to topple off the bottom of the screen.\nCrazy Taxi – Large movements and loud sounds must be undertaken to stop the Crazy Taxi and complete the level.\nSuper Monkey Ball – The player must move their arms into different positions in order to guide the monkey ball around obstacles and towards the goal, picking up as many bananas as possible along the way.\nNiGHTS Into Dreams – NiGHTS must be controlled and navigated through rings, collecting chips along the way, by raising your arms into a 'flying' position and adjusting them along the way.\nHouse of the Dead – A multitude of different zombies must be attacked and defeated by hitting them. Innocent people who occasionally appear must also be avoided.\nVirtua Striker – As footballs drop from the top of the screen, the aim is to head them into differently colored and scored balloons on the opposite side of the screen in order to obtain the highest score.\nVirtua Fighter – Standing to one side, players kick and punch the corresponding attack prompts on the screen in order to defeat the opponent. Block and counter prompts also appear, and must be reacted to accordingly.\nSpace Channel 5 – Different dance move combination must be remembered when shown by the Morolians, and then repeated in time to the music by hitting six different buttons on the screen.\nBilly Hatcher and the Giant Egg – By waving their hands over two different targets, players must move Billy and the egg around, and crush enemies and collect fruits along the way to the goal."},{"t":"Sentinel: Descendants in Time","p":["Windows"],"d":"Detalion","u":"The Adventure Company","g":"Adventure","r":"December 14, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sentinel:_Descendants_in_Time","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co93uk.jpg","s":"SENTINEL Descendants in Time is a gripping science fiction adventure set more than 1900 years from the present day in a rich pastoral region of our own future Earth.\n\nIn this quest for riches and knowledge, you can uncover the mystery behind the Tastan Caverns. As you begin your dangerous journey, you'll encounter a female sentinel programmed to guard the sacred caverns. Her dark purpose, however, may impede your progress through more than 20 puzzles. A built-in hint system may come in especially handy as the puzzles become more challenging.\n\nEach of the game's eight worlds features diverse environments, ranging from snowcapped mountains to active volcanoes."},{"t":"Serious Sam Advance","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"April 12","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Serious_Sam_Advance"},{"t":"Serious Sam: Next Encounter","p":["GameCube","PlayStation 2"],"d":"Climax Solent","u":"Global Star Software","g":"First-person shooter","r":"April 14, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Serious_Sam:_Next_Encounter","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2ayf.jpg","s":"In this installment of the Serious Sam series, Sam takes on a new arch-nemesis \"Mini Sam\", an evil clone of the hero Sam \"Serious\" Stone. Mini Sam has taken control of the timelock and is going through time wiping out ancient civilizations - and it is up to Serious Sam to put a stop to him.\n\nThe game takes the player through over 40 levels in three historic locations; Ancient Rome, Feudal China and Legendary Atlantis. The PS2 version includes online multiplayer support for up to 8 players via the broadband adapter and two players on one PS2, while the GC version allows 4 players to battle it out on one GameCube.\n\nCompetitive multiplayer modes include Deathmatch, Hold the Flag and Pass the Bomb. The entire single player campaign can be played through co-operatively, allowing two players to help each other take on the vicious armies of Mental and Mini-Sam."},{"t":"Seven Samurai 20XX","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"March 12","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seven_Samurai_20XX"},{"t":"Sexy Poker","p":["Mobile phone"],"d":"Gameloft Montreal","u":"Gameloft","g":"Card","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sexy_Poker"},{"t":"Shade: Wrath of Angels","p":["Windows"],"d":"Black Element Software","u":"Cenega Publishing, Tri Synergy","g":"Action-adventure","r":"October 1, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shade:_Wrath_of_Angels","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2r9z.jpg","s":"Shade: Wrath of Angels is a third person adventure game where players took the role of a person who is looking for his brother while fighting various enemies throughout the game."},{"t":"Shadow Hearts: Covenant","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"September 27"},{"t":"Shadow Ops: Red Mercury","p":["Xbox","Windows"],"d":"Zombie Studios","u":"Atari","g":"First-person shooter","r":"June 15, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shadow_Ops:_Red_Mercury","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3jdd.jpg","s":"Shadow Ops: Red Mercury is an action-oriented first person shooter based on modern military weapons, equipment and tactics, although presented as a \"blockbuster action movie\" rather than a hardcore realistic military simulation. Players proceed through linear levels while battling terrorists and hostile enemy soldiers in locations spanning all around the globe, such as Syria and France, using an assortment of modern firearms."},{"t":"Shaman King: Funbari Spirits","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Dimps","u":"Bandai","g":"Fighting","r":"April 8, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shaman_King:_Funbari_Spirits","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/gmzgwwxz8fvsg5ji5wwb.jpg","s":"A cel-shaded fighter based in the Shaman King universe."},{"t":"Shaman King: Master of Spirits","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"November 9"},{"t":"Shaman King: Power of Spirit","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"November 9"},{"t":"Shark Tale","p":["Windows","GameCube","PlayStation 2","Xbox","Game Boy Advance"],"r":"September 27","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shark_Tale_(video_game)"},{"t":"Shellshock: Nam '67","p":["PlayStation 2","Windows","Xbox"],"d":"Guerrilla Games","u":"Eidos Interactive","g":"Third-person shooter","r":"September 3, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shellshock:_Nam_'67","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co5dgk.jpg","s":"ShellShock: Nam '67 depicts, for the first time in a video game, the true horrors of the Vietnam War. Focusing on one man's ordeals during one of the most controversial wars of modern times, Shellshock: Nam '67 dares to go where no other war game has gone. The player assumes the role of a rookie soldier on his first tour of duty, as he experiences all the fear, chaos and atrocities of the Vietnam War."},{"t":"Sherlock Holmes: The Case of the Silver Earring","p":["Windows"],"d":"Frogwares","u":"Digital Jesters, Ubisoft, Frogwares","g":"Adventure","r":"August 27, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sherlock_Holmes:_The_Case_of_the_Silver_Earring","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1rjh.jpg","s":"The party Sherlock Holmes and his trusted friend, Dr. Watson, have been invited to turns into tragedy: a murder is committed right before their very eyes. Our famous detective is on the case immediately, but the list of suspects is getting no shorter, while other crimes are being committed. Will you succeed in uncovering the truth before other innocent people suffer? Experience an amazing plot, written by a true Sherlock Holmes fan, in a unique environment."},{"t":"Shin Megami Tensei: 20XX","p":["Mobile phone"],"d":"Atlus","u":"Atlus, G-Mode","g":"Role-playing","r":"August 26, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shin_Megami_Tensei:_20XX","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co845q.jpg","s":"Shin Megami Tensei: 20XX is a Japanese cellphone game, created as a prequel to Shin Megami Tensei II, showing what happened in Valhalla before Aleph was born."},{"t":"Shin Megami Tensei: Digital Devil Saga","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"July 15"},{"t":"Shin Megami Tensei: Nocturne","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"October 14"},{"t":"Shin Onigashima","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"August 10","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shin_Onigashima"},{"t":"Shiren Monsters: Netsal","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"g":"Sport","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shiren_Monsters:_Netsal","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4d7c.jpg","s":"A soccer game developed by Chunsoft for the GBA."},{"t":"Shot Online","p":["Windows"],"d":"WebzenOnNet Co. Ltd.","u":"Webzen","g":"Sports, MMORPG","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shot_Online"},{"t":"Showdown: Legends of Wrestling","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"Acclaim Studios Austin","u":"Acclaim Entertainment","g":"Sports","r":"June 24, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Showdown:_Legends_of_Wrestling","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4yv9.jpg","s":"Showdown: Legends of Wrestling features more than 70 of the greatest wrestlers throughout history. Send your favorite wrestlers to the squared circle for bone-breaking matches, including Table, First Blood, Ladder, Cage, and Battle Royal. Create dream matches, unlock classic feuds, and customize your own wrestler. You'll travel down the path of pain in the new era-based career mode. If you can master the new Ready-To-Brawl controls, you'll be prepared to take on the icons of professional wrestling."},{"t":"Shrek 2","p":["GameCube","PlayStation 2","Xbox","Game Boy Advance","Windows","macOS","Mobile phone"],"d":"Luxoflux, KnowWonder, Beenox, Aspyr","u":"Activision, Aspyr","g":"Action-adventure, beat 'em up, platform","r":"May 4, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shrek_2_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1pee.jpg","s":"Game based on the second movie, developed by the makers of Vigilante 8. Shrek is on a journey to meet his in-laws, so Shrek 2 follows his adventure to Far Away Land and the chaos that ensues once Fiona's parents learn that their precious daughter is an ogre -- and is married to the crudest of them all. Shrek 2 features a mixture of puzzle solving and enemy bashing. Players are able to control one of four characters at any given time -- swapping between them at will. Each character has a set of basic attack moves and a special ability. Donkey has a \"Burro Blast\" that can knock down large objects, Shrek can pick up and throw heavy objects, and Fiona -- in a nod to her fight scene in the first movie -- can slow down time, Matrix-style."},{"t":"Shuffle!","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2"],"g":"Simulator, Adventure, Visual Novel","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shuffle!","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4133.jpg","s":"The world of the gods, demons, and humans have converged, and magic has become the norm. This is the story of the very busy romantic adventure of a boy called “The man who can become either God, Demon, or Human.”"},{"t":"Sid Meier's Pirates!","p":["Windows"],"u":"Atari","g":"RPG","r":"November 22, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sid_Meier%27s_Pirates!_(2004_video_game)","i":"images/steam-3920.jpg","s":"Sail the Caribbean, marauding all on the high seas or ally your ship and crew as a privateer in search of riches - the life you choose is up to you. Face dogged enemies, raid unsuspecting villages, woo fair maidens, avoid capture or dig for buried treasure. Discover what it takes to become one of the most famous pirates in history!"},{"t":"Silent Hill 4: The Room","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"September 7"},{"t":"Silent Scope Complete","p":["Xbox"],"d":"Konami","u":"Konami","g":"Rail shooter","r":"February 10, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silent_Scope_Complete"},{"t":"Silver Strike Bowling","p":["Arcade"],"g":"Sport","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silver_Strike_Bowling","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/p20jjoeioxnvxxwxvdif.jpg","s":"Silver Strike Bowling is an arcade game that mimics ten-pin bowling on a monitor corresponding to a player's trackball control. Users may play standard bowling games or, depending on local availability, can select the Vegas Tournament option allowing players to draw cards for each spare and strike in an attempt to produce the best poker hand. While relatively basic, the 8 players mode and leaderboards can keep players coming back for more."},{"t":"Ski Resort Extreme","p":["Windows"],"d":"Cat Daddy Games","u":"Global Star Software","g":"Business simulation game","r":"October 29, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ski_Resort_Extreme","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/dvc7yq8pkic3pcohdhdv.jpg","s":"Ski Resort Extreme is a computer simulation game which puts the player in charge of creating and running a ski resort. It was developed and released in 2004 by Cat Daddy Games who also developed the very similar Ski Resort Tycoon and Ski Resort Tycoon II. \nSki Resort Extreme puts the player in the shoes of a ski resort developer whose aim is to attract varied groups of skiers and snowboarders by catering to their needs and expectations, be it ski runs, equipment, entertainment or amenities. \nResorts may be started from scratch, with more or less money depending on the difficulty level. Alternatively, players may take challenges where the task is to fix the problems of an existing resort in a specified period of time. \nThe game also allows the player to create a terrain with the map editor, with the option to import one's own height map."},{"t":"Sly 2: Band of Thieves","p":["PlayStation 2"],"u":"Sony Computer Entertainment","r":"September 14, 2004"},{"t":"Smash Court Tennis Pro Tournament 2","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Now Production","u":"Sony Computer Entertainment, Namco Hometek, Namco","g":"Sports","r":"May 28, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smash_Court_Tennis_Pro_Tournament_2","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co7k5m.jpg","s":"The Playstation 2 sequel to Smash Court Tennis offers player a deeper tennis simulation experience, expanding on existing features, aswell as adding new modes."},{"t":"Snail Mail","p":["Windows","macOS"],"u":"Sandlot Games","g":"Racing","r":"December 3, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snail_Mail_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2sks.jpg","s":"Guide Turbo the Snail as he rushes to deliver Intergalactic Mail throughout the furthest reaches of the universe in Snail Mail, a fast-paced racing adventure from Sandlot Games for the WiiWare service."},{"t":"Soldiers: Heroes of World War II","p":["Windows"],"d":"Best Way","u":"Codemasters","g":"Real-time tactics","r":"June 29, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soldiers:_Heroes_of_World_War_II","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1rh7.jpg","s":"The player can take control of American, British, Russian, or German forces to play out battles that are set in World War II. The game is primarily a strategy game, but the player can take control of his or her forces and direct them with the keyboard and mouse for additional depth of control."},{"t":"Sonic Advance 3","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"June 7","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sonic_Advance_3"},{"t":"Sonic Battle","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"January 5","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sonic_Battle"},{"t":"Sonic Heroes","p":["Windows","GameCube","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"March 23","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sonic_Heroes"},{"t":"Sora no Iro, Mizu no Iro","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sora_no_Iro,_Mizu_no_Iro"},{"t":"Soul Link","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soul_Link"},{"t":"Space Battleship Yamato: Iscandar e no Tsuioku","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Bandai","u":"Bandai","g":"Action","r":"October 6, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Space_Battleship_Yamato:_Iscandar_e_no_Tsuioku"},{"t":"Space Combat","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Space_Combat"},{"t":"Space Rangers 2: Dominators","p":["Windows"],"d":"Elemental Games","u":"1C Company, Excalibur Publishing, Cinemaware Marquee","g":"Text adventure, real-time strategy, space trading and combat simulator, turn-based strategy, shoot 'em up, role-playing game, third-person shooter","r":"November 25, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Space_Rangers_2:_Dominators","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2xs1.jpg","s":"Reboot is an expansion pack for the critically acclaimed Space Rangers 2: Rise of the Dominators. It adds new missions, equipment, maps, and other additional content to the original game."},{"t":"Spartan","p":["Windows"],"d":"Slitherine Strategies","u":"Just Play, Graphsim Entertainment","g":"Turn-based strategy","r":"March 24, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spartan_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co5q7y.jpg","s":"Over 2000 years ago there was a city called Sparta. The city had only two purposes – to train for war and to fight the wars she trained for. Over time Sparta became renowned for having the strongest, fastest, bravest and most deadly fighters in the known world."},{"t":"Special Force","p":["Windows"],"d":"DragonFly GF Co., Ltd.","u":"DragonFly GF Co., Ltd., True Digital Plus, LaMate Taiwan, Asiasoft Online Pte Ltd","g":"First-person shooter","r":"July 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special_Force_(2004_video_game)"},{"t":"Spider-Man 2","p":["Windows","Nintendo DS"],"r":"July 9","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spider-Man_2_(2004_video_game)"},{"t":"Spider-Man 2 (US)","p":["Windows"],"r":"June 29","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spider-Man_2_(2004_video_game)"},{"t":"Sprung","p":["Nintendo DS"],"r":"December 8","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sprung_(video_game)"},{"t":"Spyro: A Hero's Tail","p":["GameCube","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"November 3"},{"t":"Stacker","p":["Arcade"],"g":"Arcade","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stacker_(arcade_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co5vip.jpg","s":"Stacker is a game merchandiser manufactured by LAI Games, first produced in 2004. The goal of the game is to align rows of lights on top of each other. A player who stacks 11 rows can choose to take a minor prize. A minor prize is usually low in value, sometimes lower than the amount of money the player paid to play the game. A player who stacks the blocks to the top row wins the jackpot prize, called the \"major prize.\" Major prizes vary from machine-to-machine but will often include high-value items such as game consoles, mobile phones, and gift cards."},{"t":"Star Soldier","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"February 14","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Star_Soldier_(video_game)"},{"t":"Star Sonata","p":["Windows"],"d":"Landauer Games","u":"Landauer Games","g":"MMORPG Space simulation","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Star_Sonata"},{"t":"Star Trek: Shattered Universe","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"Starsphere Interactive","u":"TDK Mediactive","g":"Space combat simulator","r":"January 13, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Star_Trek:_Shattered_Universe","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4ebb.jpg","s":"The universe is not as you know it...Think Fast, Shoot Faster! All hands to battle stations! Get ready for a frenetic, adrenaline pumping experience in an entirely new breed of Star Trek.An intense,edgy high-energy space-combat action game set in the dark mirror universe of Star Trek: The Original Series classic-era setting, Star Trek Shattered Universe challenges the player to adapt to a new reality where everything once familiar is now a dark reflection - where the noble Federation is now an evil and relentless foe."},{"t":"Star Wars Galaxies: Jump to Lightspeed","p":["Windows"],"r":"October 26","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Star_Wars_Galaxies#Jump_to_Lightspeed"},{"t":"Star Wars Trilogy: Apprentice of the Force","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"September 21"},{"t":"Star Wars: Battlefront","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"g":"Action, Adventure, Strategy","r":"September 21","l":"https://store.steampowered.com/app/1237980","i":"images/steam-1237980.jpg","s":"The STAR WARS™ Battlefront™ Ultimate Edition includes the STAR WARS™ Battlefront™ Deluxe Edition as well as the STAR WARS™ Battlefront™ Season Pass."},{"t":"Star Wars: Knights of the Old Republic II The Sith Lords","p":["Windows","Xbox"],"g":"RPG","r":"December 6","l":"https://store.steampowered.com/app/208580","i":"images/steam-208580.jpg","s":"5 years after the events of the award winning original, the Sith are on the verge of crushing the Old Republic. As a lone Jedi, will you follow the light side or succumb to the dark?"},{"t":"Star Wolves","p":["Windows"],"d":"X-bow Software","u":"1C Company","g":"Real-time tactics, RPG, Space simulation","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Star_Wolves","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co422m.jpg","s":"Star wolves is a 3D space RPG with deep strategy and tactical elements. The game thrusts players into a world of freelance space hunters in the XXI-XXII century A.D. during a time of political crisis for the all-powerful Empire and the three mega-corporations that control all the known worlds. Corruption prospers planet-side and only space can give a man his freedom, but not without a cost: space is not a safe place anymore. Human space pirates, rogue AI computers that rebelled against humanity and empire patrol ships roam space in search of easy prey.\n\nPlayers begin the game as a bounty hunter with little more than an old, run-down space fighter and a dream, but as they advance in the game and prosper, their piloting and battle skills improve, allowing access to more advance spacecraft. Players can control a party of up to six bounty hunters, each possessing different skills, abilities and personality.\n\nTeam tactics give players vast opportunities in battles when shear fire power isn't enough. Tactical ruses, planning and executing ambushes or deploying spaceships' special abilities provide cunning commanders the ability to crush enemies according to their style of play."},{"t":"Star Wraith IV: Reviction","p":["Windows"],"d":"StarWraith 3D Games LLC","u":"StarWraith 3D Games LLC","g":"Space simulation","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Star_Wraith_IV:_Reviction"},{"t":"Star Wraith: Shadows of Orion","p":[],"d":"StarWraith 3D Games","u":"StarWraith 3D Games","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Star_Wraith:_Shadows_of_Orion"},{"t":"Stardoll","p":["Browser"],"d":"Glorious Games Group AB","g":"Fashion, Style, Social","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stardoll","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/coa6dp.jpg","s":"Stardoll is a world of Fame, Fashion & Friends. Create, style and dress up your own virtual doll in the largest and most popular online fashion game. You can be a designer, stylist, interior decorator, makeup artist or everything at once!"},{"t":"Starshatter","p":["Windows"],"d":"Destroyer Studios","u":"Matrix Games","g":"Space flight simulator","r":"July 7, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Starshatter"},{"t":"Starshatter: The Gathering Storm","p":["Windows"],"d":"Destroyer Studios","u":"Matrix Games","g":"Space combat simulator","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Starshatter:_The_Gathering_Storm","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/n1kxzncsmca6vajcxozi.jpg","s":"A sequel to and remake of the original Starshatter, The Gathering Storm is a space combat game from developer Destroyer Studios."},{"t":"Starsky & Hutch","p":["GameCube"],"r":"August 24","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Starsky_%26_Hutch_(video_game)"},{"t":"Steel Battalion: Line of Contact","p":["Xbox"],"r":"February 27"},{"t":"Steer Madness","p":["Windows","macOS"],"d":"Johnathan Skinner","u":"Johnathan Skinner","g":"Adventure","r":"December 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steer_Madness"},{"t":"Stella Deus: The Gate of Eternity","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Atlus, Additional work by:, Pinegrow, Designer 7","u":"Atlus, 505 Games","g":"Tactical role-playing","r":"October 28, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stella_Deus:_The_Gate_of_Eternity","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/cobgv9.jpg","s":"Stella Deus is a story-driven tactical role-playing game in which the player controls a group of characters both picked up during the course of the story and in side events. The world is navigated using an overworld map using point-to-point navigation, with a date system showing the length of time it takes to get to a selected location. Alongside the story missions, Towns can be visited, in which characters can customize and create new weapons and armor, sell existing equipment in exchange for money, and shop for items such as healing potions. In camps set up on a journey, characters can swap out weapons and armor, equip items such as healing potions and beneficial charms for future battles. Special items used in character leveling can also be crafted by the player. Alongside story-based missions, there is a special dungeon called the Catacomb of Trials, where characters can battle and gain experience levels, raising their general statistics. The number of available levels in the Catacomb increases as players progress through the game. Each character has a specific character class, which they keep throughout the game and continue to level up as they gain experience points (XP). Higher amounts of XP are awarded for executing special abilities. Along with swordsmen and archers, there are alchemists (mages), priests (healers), and units who fight using most things from axes to fists.\n\nMost battles are triggered based on story events, and are completed when the stated object has been accomplished by the player, be it defeating all enemies, defeating a boss, or performing a specific task. At the end of each battle, the players gain a summery of their performance and spoils gained. The game uses the turn-based Replaceable Action Position battle system, much of which was carried over from the battle system used in Hoshigami: Ruining Blue Earth. Players navigate the field across a grid-based map, which can include obstacles such as bodies of water and high structures. Character positioning within the environment can be used to their advantage, such as an archer gaining higher accuracy when at a high point in the level. Character actions are arranged in a set order, and each character's weapon dictates their attack range. Each time a character performs an action, they gain experience points and additional Skill Points (SP) that can be used to purchase supplies or raise individual character stats. Three types of Skills can be equipped for characters: Action Skills, a special attack that player execute for a certain amount of Magic Points (MP); Support Skills, which grant passive abilities such as scaling higher obstacles; and Zone Skills, which grant passive abilities to both the equipped character and those in close proximity to them.\n\nAlongside Action Skills, two or more characters in conjunction trigger unique special moves called Team Attacks. The amount of damage done depends on how many characters took part in the action. Team attacks also increase the rewards gained at the end of battles. Characters' actions are governed by their stored Action Points (AP): a character's turn begins when their AP meter is at 100. A character's actions can continue until the meter reaches 0, meaning that they can move and attack multiple times within their turn. The amount of AP used with each action depends on the weight of the armor the character is wearing."},{"t":"Street Fighter Anniversary Collection","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"Capcom","u":"Capcom","g":"Fighting","r":"August 31, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Street_Fighter_Anniversary_Collection"},{"t":"Street Hacker","p":["Windows"],"d":"VirtuWeb Interactive","u":"VirtuWeb Interactive","g":"Simulation","r":"February 13, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Street_Hacker"},{"t":"Street Jam Basketball","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"d":"Prograph Research","u":"DSI Games","g":"Sports video game","r":"April 25, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Street_Jam_Basketball","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/vlefbwidnbt9qc7lunvo.jpg","s":"Street Jam is a three-on-three street basketball game for Game Boy Advance. Select your team from a roster of 15 teams and over 40 different characters and enter the world of street-ball. Your aim is to win all illegal tournaments held in various locations of the downtown. The individual players differ in game style, speed, special dunks and graphic presentation. Compete in the arcade mode and win eight challenging matches against the CPU, or partake in the story mode. The latter lets you select your team, and try to rise up in the ranks via five different levels from beginner to violence mode throughout 20 different tournaments with animated story sequences."},{"t":"Street Racing Syndicate","p":["GameCube","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"August 31","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Street_Racing_Syndicate"},{"t":"Strength & Honour","p":["Windows"],"d":"Magitech","u":"Magitech","g":"Real-time tactics","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strength_&_Honour"},{"t":"Strike Force Bowling","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"LAB Rats Games","u":"Enlight Software, Crave Entertainment, Play-It","g":"Sports","r":"January 7, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strike_Force_Bowling","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co6uf3.jpg","s":"Strike Force Bowling is a video game of the sports genre released in 2004 by LAB Rats. A previous game, Fast Lanes Bowling, was published by Enlight Software. The two games are very similar sharing the same physics engine and graphics, although Strike Force featured more locations as well as left-handed, and reverse-hook bowlers. LAB Rats assisted in the development of Brunswick Circuit Pro Bowling so the game has the same physics engine, but has a more fantasy-oriented theme. Strike Force features 14 places to Bowl (12 in Fast Lanes) and 8 Playable characters. There are only 7 locations, but each has its own \"nighttime\" variant which is unlocked as a secret stage. It also features Golf Mode, Challenge Mode, Skins, and Tournaments. There are also 14 different bowling balls to use, such as the Lightning, and level specific ones like the Bone Crasher and Pharaoh's Magic."},{"t":"Sudeki","p":["Xbox"],"r":"July 20","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sudeki"},{"t":"Suikoden IV","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Konami Computer Entertainment Tokyo","u":"Konami","g":"Role-playing","r":"August 19, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suikoden_IV","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co26g2.jpg","s":"Suikoden IV features the return of the 108 Stars of Destiny, as well as an enhanced interface in a new oceanic environment. You'll follow a young knight while he struggles with Rune, which slowly steals the life of its bearer. The game's strategic battle systems let you attack or cast magic spells with help from other party members. Recruit members of the Stars of Destiny and create a base from the ground up. With a brand-new storyline, characters, and cutscenes, Suikoden IV takes the series to the next level."},{"t":"Summon Night: Swordcraft Story 2","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"d":"Flight-Plan","u":"Banpresto, Atlus","g":"Action role-playing game","r":"August 20, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Summon_Night:_Swordcraft_Story_2","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2w42.jpg","s":"In Summon Night: Swordcraft 2, the player is an orphan from the Colthearts clan raised by a Craftknight (a smith/warrior). The character aspires to be a Craftknight as well. The player character, either Edgar Colthearts or Aera Colthearts, who are Edge Fencers, find themselves at the site of an abandoned ruin where a violent Summon Beast named Goura is awakened. In order to protect their new family, Edgar/Aera is bound to a wild Summon Beast (stray summon) and embarks on a journey to reseal the ruins."},{"t":"Super DX-Ball","p":["Windows","macOS"],"d":"Michael P. Welch","u":"BlitWise Productions","g":"Breakout clone","r":"November 10, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Super_DX-Ball","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1xwk.jpg","s":"Super DX-Ball delivers a vibrant and colorful brick-breaking game that the whole family can enjoy. Created by Michael P. Welch, the original author of DX-Ball, this game brings together the amazing world of tessellation and repeating patterns with the classic game play of DX-Ball. Hand-crafted by an old pro, Super DX-Ball is the quintessential brick-breaking game that you've been searching for."},{"t":"Super Mario 64 DS","p":["Nintendo DS"],"r":"November 21","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Super_Mario_64_DS"},{"t":"Super Mario Bros.","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"February 14","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Super_Mario_Bros."},{"t":"Super Mario Bros.: The Lost Levels","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"August 10"},{"t":"Super Robot Wars MX","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Banpresoft","u":"Banpresto","g":"Tactical role-playing game","r":"May 27, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Super_Robot_Wars_MX","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3gpo.jpg","s":"Super Robot Taisen MX is a video game for the PlayStation 2. It is part of the Super Robot Wars series by Banpresto, a division of Bandai, and was released on May 27, 2004. It was later ported to the PlayStation Portable on December 19, 2005, with minor gameplay tweaks, titled Super Robot Wars MX Portable."},{"t":"SuperPower 2","p":["Windows"],"d":"GolemLabs","u":"DreamCatcher Interactive","g":"Government simulation game","r":"October 12, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SuperPower_2","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/fj1zhvmuhczz4mm0gwhw.jpg","s":"SuperPower 2 is a real-time strategy wargame developed by Canadian based GolemLabs and published by DreamCatcher Games in 2004, following SuperPower. It was released between October 11 and November 19, 2004 in North America and Europe, respectively."},{"t":"SuperTux","p":["Windows","Linux","macOS"],"g":"Platform, Arcade","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SuperTux","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4bkj.jpg","s":"Classic 2D jump'n'run sidescroller featuring Tux the penguin. Run and jump through multiple worlds, fighting off enemies by jumping on them, bumping them from below or tossing objects at them, grabbing power-ups and other stuff on the way."},{"t":"Survival Crisis Z","p":["Windows"],"d":"Ska Studios","u":"Ska Studios","g":"Role-playing video game, Survival horror","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Survival_Crisis_Z","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/cock8v.jpg","s":"Survival Crisis Z is an open ended intense survival experience that is nearly as much RPG as it is arcade. Make money or steal it. Buy weapons or pick them off a fresh corpse. Work for the leaders of the post-apocalyptic ruin or have them working for you.\n\nMarauders, terrorists, merchants and heroes are all equals here. They are all either one of us or one of them, warm-blooded or cold, survivors or monsters."},{"t":"Syberia II","p":["Xbox"],"r":"October 5","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Syberia_II"},{"t":"Symphonic Rain","p":["Windows"],"d":"Kogado Studio","u":"Kogado Studio, Degica","g":"Rhythm game, Visual novel","r":"March 26, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Symphonic_Rain","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co6yqy.jpg","s":"Set in Piova, the city of music and endless rain. Guide Chris Vertin on the path to become a master musician in a harmonious fusion of Visual Novel and Music-based gameplay."},{"t":"Syphon Filter: The Omega Strain","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Sony Computer Entertainment America","u":"Sony Computer Entertainment","g":"Third-person shooter","r":"May 4, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Syphon_Filter:_The_Omega_Strain","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2gfs.jpg","s":"Syphon Filter: The Omega Strain is a third-person shooter developed by Bend Studio and published by Sony Computer Entertainment. Released in May 2004 for the PlayStation 2, it is the fourth instalment in the Syphon Filter series. The game follows a global bioterrorism crisis, and players assume the role of a new recruit in Gabe Logan’s agency, tasked with stopping the spread of the deadly Omega Strain virus."},{"t":"Söldner: Secret Wars","p":["Windows"],"d":"Wings Simulations","u":"JoWooD Productions, Encore, Inc., Evolved Games","g":"Tactical shooter","r":"May 27, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/S%C3%B6ldner:_Secret_Wars","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4s24.jpg","s":"Soldner: Secret Wars is similar to the recent online FPS combat games involving infantry and vehicular warfare. But it also has a few features that separate it from the rest.\n\nThe Advanced Destruction System means you're no longer restricted to how a map should look. You can knock down trees to block a road or destroy a bridge to prevent armour from crossing. Damage remains until the end of the round instead of being just a decal that does not affect game play.\n\nUnit are able to be customized. You can choose your look, headgear, uniform and add extras like sunglasses and backpacks. Soldner features a large variety of weapons including the basic pistols and rifles but also features specialized items like sniper rifles, explosives and rocket launchers. There is a large variety of vehicles available to the player as well.\n\nThe other major game play feature is the command structure. An elected leader is able to set out objectives and waypoints for team members. As well as allocating funds for weapon and vehicle purchases. Bringing a more cohesive sense of game play to the battlefield."},{"t":"Taiko: Drum Master","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Namco","u":"Namco Hometek, Namco","g":"Rhythm","r":"October 26, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taiko:_Drum_Master","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co5ejn.jpg","s":"Taiko Drum Master is an entry in Namco's Taiko No Tatsujin rhythm game series and the first to have a Western release. As in other rhythm games, the goal is to interact with a special controller according to scrolling onscreen prompts timed to music. This game comes bundled with the TaTaCon drum controller, a miniature version of a Japanese taiko drum with sensors in the middle and on the sides.\n\nIn-game actions are indicated by scrolling circle icons. Red circles indicate hitting the center of the drum, while blue circles require the player to hit the edge. On big circles, the player can hit both center or edge sensors for bonus points. Finally, yellow lines and balloons require the player to perform drum rolls.\n\nThe game comes with a varied set of tunes: from covered pop hits like Material Girl and ABC to music from other Namco games such as Katamari Damacy and Dragon Spirit and even television theme songs. In addition, there are also several mini-games included on the disc that use the TaTaCon for more esoteric purposes, such as watermelon eating and wolf-stacking."},{"t":"Tak 2: The Staff of Dreams","p":["GameCube","PlayStation 2","Xbox","Game Boy Advance"],"r":"October 14"},{"t":"Take Command","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Take_Command_(video_game)"},{"t":"Tales of Rebirth","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Namco Tales Studio","u":"Namco, Namco Bandai Games","g":"Action role-playing game","r":"December 16, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tales_of_Rebirth","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2ywc.jpg","s":"Tales of Rebirth is set in a world where humans (called Huma) and beast people (Gajuma) coexist in relative peace. The world's magical power is called Force, which manifests in various people as control over an element or aspect of the physical laws. In ancient times, after a war sparked when Huma attempted to enslave Gajuma, both races joined forces to found the kingdom of Karegia. An unspecified time before the events of the game, Geyorkias, the ruler of a spirit race called the Sacred Beasts, sought to destroy the Huma as their dark emotions were fueling a primordial destructive force known as Yuris: the other Sacred Beasts put a stop to Geyorkias' plan by sealing him away, then acting to nullify Yuris' threat. The story opens with the death of Karegia's king, Ladras Lindblum, poisoned by the royal adviser Zilva Madigan: during his final moments, he releases his power into the world, causing many humans to become possessed by Force, including Veigue, Annie and Tytree. As the king has failed to name a successor, Karegia enters an interregnum at his death."},{"t":"Tales of Symphonia","p":["GameCube"],"r":"July 13","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tales_of_Symphonia"},{"t":"Target: Terror","p":["Arcade"],"d":"Raw Thrills, Leviathan Games","u":"Raw Thrills, Taito, Konami Digital Entertainment","g":"Light gun shooter","r":"May 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Target:_Terror","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co5txv.jpg","s":"Terror puts you in the place of an elite anti-terrorist agent who is charged with protecting the U.S. from all terrorist activities. With a full scale assault spanning the entire U.S., this is your chance to show terrorists who is in charge. Eliminate the seemingly endless waves of enemies with an assortment of high-tech weapons you have in your arsenal."},{"t":"Taxi Rider","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Tamsoft","u":"D3 Publisher, 505 GameStreet","g":"Racing","r":"March 8, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taxi_Rider","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co80l4.jpg","s":"Taxi Rider is a game about driving a taxi and getting customers to their destination in time, similar to the arcade concept of SEGA's Crazy Taxi series. The player is employed by a local taxi firm set in the fictional Nijiiro, as well as the adjoining areas such as the residential Dream Hills, the Coast Amusement Center and Dragon Peak."},{"t":"Tech Deck Dude: Bare Knuckle Grind","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tech_Deck_Dude:_Bare_Knuckle_Grind"},{"t":"Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles 2: Battle Nexus","p":["Windows","GameCube","PlayStation 2","Xbox","Game Boy Advance"],"r":"October 19"},{"t":"Ten Pin Alley 2","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"d":"Pronto Games, Other Ocean Interactive","u":"XS Games","g":"Sports","r":"April 26, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ten_Pin_Alley_2","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co6qr0.jpg","s":"Bowling game that offers two gameplay options: you can either practice with up to three other players on the same system, or head into a tournament layout for competition against three other computer opponents. Players have the choice of eight different competitors and four different alleys. Ten Pin Alley 2's gameplay is a four click affair: first, mark the spot on the lane you want to stand. Then, watch the aim arrow bounce back and forth on the alley. Hit the button again, and set the power of the throw. The fourth button click sets how much or little a hook you want to throw. Released on a 32 megabit Game Boy Advance cartridge, the game was based on the cell phone game of the same name."},{"t":"Tenchu: Fatal Shadows","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"K2, FromSoftware","u":"FromSoftware, Sega","g":"Action-adventure, stealth","r":"July 22, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tenchu:_Fatal_Shadows","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1p2d.jpg","s":"Two black-clad ninjas, Ayame and Rin, silently stalk enemies and strike with brutal Stealh kills in revenge for the massacre of Rin's village. With lethal blades and their own specialized attacks, the fierce assassins draw ever closer to discovering who ordered this heinous crime."},{"t":"Tenchu: Wrath of Heaven","p":["Xbox"],"r":"March 10"},{"t":"Terminator 3: The Redemption","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"September 2"},{"t":"Test Drive: Eve of Destruction","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"Monster Games","u":"Atari, Inc.","g":"Racing, vehicular combat","r":"August 24, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Test_Drive:_Eve_of_Destruction","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2ezv.jpg","s":"Test Drive: Eve of Destruction blends the best elements of racing and demolition and is packed with 25 different events, including Demo Derby, where the last car standing wins; Gauntlet, where the player climbs behind the wheel of a hearse and tries to finish a set number of laps while the rest of the field attempts to stop them; Trailer Race, a new brand of racing event, where players compete while towing various types of trailers and must finish the race with something resembling a trailer still attached. Additionally, Test Drive: Eve of Destruction offers players a selection of more than 30 custom vehicles, a dynamic soundtrack and a split-screen multiplayer mode for up to four players."},{"t":"Texas Hold 'Em Poker","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"d":"Skyworks Technologies","u":"Majesco","g":"Card game","r":"November 1, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Texas_Hold_'Em_Poker_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/zuunc5ruqhly3hngy7hc.jpg","s":"This game follows the rules and nuances of the community card game Texas hold 'em."},{"t":"The Adventures of Jimmy Neutron Boy Genius: Attack of the Twonkies","p":["GameCube","PlayStation 2","Game Boy Advance"],"r":"September 13"},{"t":"The Bard's Tale","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"October 26","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Bard%27s_Tale_(2004_video_game)"},{"t":"The Chronicles of Riddick: Escape from Butcher Bay","p":["Xbox","Windows"],"u":"Vivendi Universal Games","r":"June 1, 2004"},{"t":"The Chronicles of Riddick: Escape from Butcher Bay – Developer's Cut","p":["Windows"],"u":"Vivendi Universal Games","r":"December 3, 2004"},{"t":"The Dreamhold","p":["Linux","macOS","Windows"],"g":"Adventure","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Dreamhold","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/szn1xfkua6kjmy3pszjg.jpg","s":"Fantasy Interactive Fiction created by Andrew Plotkin, as both a game and an introduction to the genre."},{"t":"The Dukes of Hazzard: Return of the General Lee","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"Ratbag Games","u":"Ubisoft","g":"Racing","r":"September 28, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Dukes_of_Hazzard:_Return_of_the_General_Lee","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/coat94.jpg","s":"The Dukes of Hazzard: Return of the General Lee is a mission based racing (or driving) game released on the PlayStation 2 and Xbox consoles. The game is based on the popular Dukes of Hazzard television show. It is the fourth game based on this show, and the only one to be made on a sixth generation console. Two Dukes games were released for the PlayStation and one was created for the Atari 2600 but was never officially released."},{"t":"The Elder Scrolls Travels: Shadowkey","p":["N-Gage"],"d":"Vir2L Studios, TKO Software","u":"Bethesda Softworks","g":"Role-playing (RPG)","r":"November 9, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Elder_Scrolls_Travels:_Shadowkey","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3als.jpg","s":"The Elder Scrolls Travels: Shadowkey was the third game in the Elder Scrolls Travels series.\nYou must save your village from marauders who are but pawns in the struggle to capture Shadowmage Skelos Undriel -- a piece in a darker and more sinister game. . You'll fight many foes in your search for the power of the Shadowkeys and the Star Teeth, and your journey will lead you to the Crypt of the Heart where you'll face the ultimate test."},{"t":"The Fairly OddParents: Shadow Showdown","p":["Windows","GameCube","PlayStation 2","Game Boy Advance"],"r":"September 8"},{"t":"The Fall: Last Days of Gaia","p":["Windows"],"d":"Silver Style Entertainment","u":"Deep Silver","g":"Post-apocalyptic Tactical RPG","r":"November 15, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Fall:_Last_Days_of_Gaia","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co5x7q.jpg","s":"The Fall is highly influenced by the Fallout series (thus the name) and the Mad Max movies. The game lets you and your team of up to six fight in a post-apocalyptic environment using tons of weapons and vehicles."},{"t":"The Guy Game","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox","Windows"],"d":"Topheavy Studios","u":"Gathering","g":"Party","r":"August 31, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Guy_Game","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3m7i.jpg","s":"The Guy Game is an adult video game for the PlayStation 2, Xbox and PC platforms published in 2004 by Gathering of Developers and developed by now-defunct Top Heavy Studios (it was the team's only game). Presented in a trivia gameshow style supporting up to four players, it consists of about 1,000 questions spread out over 20 episodes. Much of the game involves watching live-action video footage of young women in bikinis, and as the player succeeds in the game the women eventually expose their breasts. The game garnered much controversy and was the subject of a lawsuit after one of the filmed participants, who had exposed herself on camera, was discovered to be 17 years old at the time of filming."},{"t":"The Incredibles","p":["Windows"],"r":"October 29","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Incredibles_(video_game)"},{"t":"The Incredibles: When Danger Calls","p":["Windows"],"r":"November 3"},{"t":"The King of Fighters Neowave","p":["Arcade"],"d":"SNK Playmore","u":"Sammy Corporation, SNK Playmore, Ignition Entertainment","g":"Fighting","r":"July 30, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_King_of_Fighters_Neowave","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co9xas.jpg","s":"KOF Neowave features 12 three-man teams made up of some of the greatest characters from SNK's 11-year history, including the Women Fighters Team (Mai, King and Yuri) and the Fatal Fury Team (Terry, Joe, and Andy). NEOWAVE features three modes of play - Super Cancel, Guard Break, and Max2. A new \"Heat Mode\" lets players power up their attacks in exchange for a gradual loss of health. A total of 43 characters including 7 Bonus characters. 12 of the most dangerous fighting teams ever assembled. Pick your team and fight it out in the original 3-on-3 battle format. Beautifully rendered background graphics. Activate \"Heat Mode\" to power-up your attacks. Revives the evacuation rolling maneuver and thrust attacks. Over-the-top Super Special Moves. 3 modes of play: Super Cancel, Guard Break and Max2. Link a Special Move with a Super Attack in the Super Cancel Mode to cause extreme damage."},{"t":"The Land Before Time: Prehistoric Adventures","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Land_Before_Time:_Prehistoric_Adventures"},{"t":"The Legend of Heroes: Trails in the Sky","p":["Windows"],"d":"Nihon Falcom","u":"Nihon Falcom, Xseed Games, Ghostlight","g":"Role-playing","r":"June 24, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Legend_of_Heroes:_Trails_in_the_Sky","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co7ybm.jpg","s":"The Legend of Heroes: Trails in the Sky is the first installment in the main Trails series, serving as the beginning to the Liberl arc and the series as a whole. The game follows protagonists Estelle Bright and her adopted brother Joshua, who journey through the country of Liberl to train to become senior Bracers, members of a non-government multinational organization that acts to keep the peace and protect civilians.\n\nNihon Falcom comes a series of RPGs telling a legend of adventure, political intrigue, and mystery, with a tale of growing up at the core. With a mix of turn-based and strategy combat, battles will cause unique builds and plans to handle many different situations and allow for different play styles. Wonderfully detailed characters abound, even to the smallest NPC, and the player will find themself taking the world in at every turn. Trails in the Sky sets a new standard for making an enjoyable and immersive RPG."},{"t":"The Legend of Mir 3","p":["Windows"],"d":"WeMade Entertainment","u":"WeMade Entertainment, Shanda, Softworld, Eye Entertainment","g":"Massively multiplayer online role-playing game","r":"October 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Legend_of_Mir_3"},{"t":"The Legend of Zelda","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"February 14","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Legend_of_Zelda_(video_game)"},{"t":"The Legend of Zelda: Four Swords Adventures","p":["GameCube"],"r":"June 7"},{"t":"The Legend of Zelda: The Minish Cap","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"u":"Nintendo","r":"November 4, 2004"},{"t":"The Lord of the Rings: The Battle for Middle-earth","p":["Windows"],"r":"December 6"},{"t":"The Lord of the Rings: The Third Age","p":["GameCube","PlayStation 2","Xbox","Game Boy Advance"],"r":"November 2"},{"t":"The Moment of Silence","p":["Windows"],"d":"House of Tales","u":"Digital Jesters, The Adventure Company","g":"Adventure game","r":"October 1, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Moment_of_Silence","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co43zb.jpg","s":"The Moment of Silence is a classic point-and-click 3rd person adventure game set in New York City in 2044. Players step into the role of Peter Wright, an advertising executive currently heading up the Government's 'Freedom of Speech' campaign."},{"t":"The Mysterious Murasame Castle","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"August 10","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Mysterious_Murasame_Castle"},{"t":"The Nightmare of Druaga","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Arika","u":"Arika, Namco Hometek","g":"Role-playing","r":"July 29, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Nightmare_of_Druaga"},{"t":"The Nightmare of Druaga: Fushigino Dungeon","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"October 27"},{"t":"The Polar Express","p":["Game Boy Advance","GameCube","Windows","PlayStation 2"],"d":"Blue Tongue Entertainment, Tantalus Media","u":"THQ","g":"Action-adventure","r":"November 2, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Polar_Express_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1p2t.jpg","s":"An adventure game based on the CGI-animated Robert Zemeckis movie starring Tom Hanks and based on the children's book by Chris Van Allsburg. When a doubting young boy takes an extraordinary train ride to the North Pole, he embarks on a journey of self-discovery that shows him that the wonder of life never fades for those who believe. Climb aboard the Polar Express and meet memorable characters from the film as you race across train tops, ride runaway rail cars, and sort through mountains of presents. Explore massive 3D environments including the North Pole and The Polar Express. Interact with recognizable characters from the movie, including Hero Girl, Know-it-All, Lonely Boy, Hero Boy, the Hobo, Smokey & Steamer and the Elves. Play mini-games, solve puzzles, and search for lost presents."},{"t":"The Political Machine","p":["Windows"],"d":"Stardock","u":"Ubisoft","g":"Government simulation","r":"August 10, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Political_Machine"},{"t":"The Rumble Fish","p":["Arcade"],"d":"Dimps","u":"Sammy, Sega","g":"2D Versus fighting","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Rumble_Fish","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co497m.jpg","s":"The Rumble Fish is a fighting game created by Dimps for the Atomiswave arcade platform. Its most distinguishing quality is its graphics engine, which animates the characters' limbs separately."},{"t":"The Settlers: Heritage of Kings","p":["Windows"],"d":"Blue Byte","u":"Ubisoft","g":"Real-time strategy","r":"November 25, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Settlers:_Heritage_of_Kings","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co220s.jpg","s":"The Settlers: Heritage of Kings is a 2005 real-time strategy game. It is the fifth installment of The Settlers series.\nThe game tells the story of a young prince, Dario, who must regain control of his dead father's throne from the evil Mordred.\nHeritage of Kings breaks from the typical pattern that previous Settlers games had established; while the basic real-time strategy concept of resource micromanagement remains the same, a lot of the gameplay features have changed from those of The Settlers IV, and slightly resemble many of the gameplay aspects of Cossacks: European Wars. Heritage of Kings is also the first Settlers game in 3D."},{"t":"The Sims 2","p":["Windows"],"u":"Electronic Arts","r":"September 14, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Sims_2"},{"t":"The SpongeBob SquarePants Movie","p":["Windows","GameCube","PlayStation 2","Xbox","Game Boy Advance"],"r":"October 27","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_SpongeBob_SquarePants_Movie_(video_game)"},{"t":"The Suffering","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"g":"Action, Adventure, Indie","r":"March 8","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Suffering_(video_game)","i":"images/steam-1726550.jpg","s":"This game is a psychological horror in which the main character wakes up in an unfamiliar house and must pass all the levels by solving puzzles."},{"t":"The Urbz: Sims in the City","p":["Game Boy Advance","GameCube","Nintendo DS","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"Maxis","u":"Electronic Arts","g":"Life simulation","r":"November 5, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Urbz:_Sims_in_the_City","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1zo9.jpg","s":"The Sims have moved to the City where there's always action and where reputation means everything. In the Urbz: Sims in the City, you can go to work at such locations as the Sushi Bar, Chop Shop, or Bootleg Fireworks, Inc. Success at work brings promotions, access to new power socials, and gear to influence your new lifestyle. Flaunt your attitude by styling your Urbz, and then cross the velvet ropes of an uptown night club, or explore the subway to earn new skills and items."},{"t":"The X-Files: Resist or Serve","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Black Ops Entertainment","u":"Vivendi Universal Games","g":"Survival horror","r":"March 16, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_X-Files:_Resist_or_Serve","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co49ky.jpg","s":"The game follows FBI Special Agents Fox Mulder (voiced by David Duchovny) and Dana Scully (voiced by Gillian Anderson) as they travel to a small town in the Rocky Mountains to dig into the source of some strange and unexplained murders. Sightings of ghostly apparitions, zombies and hints of alien presence lead them on a chase for an \"inhuman\" killer.\n\nDuring the course of the story, Mulder and Scully follow leads to a remote location in Russia and then discover, and search, a mysterious half-buried alien space ship. Players can play as Mulder or Scully as they attempt to prevent alien colonization of Earth."},{"t":"Thief: Deadly Shadows","p":["Windows","Xbox"],"g":"Action","r":"May 25","l":"https://store.steampowered.com/app/6980","i":"images/steam-6980.jpg","s":"You are Garrett, the master thief. Rarely seen and never caught, Garrett is the best that ever was. Able to sneak past any guard, pick any lock, and break into the most ingeniously secured residences. Garrett steals from the wealthy and gives to himself, making his living in the dark and foreboding City."},{"t":"This Is Football 2004","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"London Studio","u":"Sony Computer Entertainment, 989 Sports","g":"Sports","r":"March 26, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/This_Is_Football_2004","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3wzi.jpg","s":"If there's one thing you can't fault This Is Football 2004 on, it's scope. While other PlayStation 2 football titles are happy to concentrate on national and international teams, here the beautiful game is taken right down to grass roots, allowing you (if you wish) to seize control of a local team.\n\nYou do that as part of the best feature in the game: the career mode. Here, you really can go from the very bottom to the very top, and it adds a challenging long term goal to the proceedings. It's just one example of where the game differs from the opposition, and there are plenty more. For instance, you can also try and blatantly blag a penalty by diving in the area. You can get penalised for handball. You can even take it online and test your skills. In short, there's plenty going on."},{"t":"This Is Football 2005","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"London Studio","u":"Sony Computer Entertainment","g":"Sports","r":"October 1, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/This_Is_Football_2005","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/dcilwdyqvdndcpkwkjlt.jpg","s":"Building upon the roots of the franchise, This Is Football 205 provides gamers with a familiar yet enhanced gameplay experience, complete with even more features, players, teams and stadiums.\n\nThe game's global soccer experience is highlighted by more than 935 international and club teams from around the globe, along with 19,000 FIFPro licensed players from 32 different leagues, eight international tournaments and 28 unique stadiums. Utilizing the EyeToy USB camera, gamers can take snapshots of themselves and convert the high-resolution images of a gamer's head into a full 3D model so that they can personally battle against the world's best."},{"t":"Thunderbirds","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"d":"Saffire","u":"Vivendi Universal Games","g":"Action, puzzle","r":"August 10, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thunderbirds_(2004_video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co9tx5.jpg","s":"Based on the live action film released in 2004 (which in turn was based on the 1960s series starring marionettes), Thunderbirds stars Alan, Tin-Tin, and Fermat, three children whose guardians are part of the International Rescue team. The player takes control of all three children as they go through training and are then forced to travel around the world to save members of International Rescue from an evil villain known as The Hood.\n\nThe game takes place in locales such as the International Rescue island, Africa, and even outer space. Each of the three characters has his or her own unique abilities that the player must use to solve puzzles and advance through a level. Alan has strength and jumping ability, Tin-Tin has telekinetic powers that are used to move objects, and Fermat can hack computers and roll through holes. While the majority of the gameplay is primarily composed of solving puzzles from an overhead view, there are also flight action sequences where the player can fly one of the many vehicles known as the Thunderbirds."},{"t":"Ticket to Ride","p":["Steam","Windows","macOS","Xbox","PlayStation"],"d":"Next Level Games, Marmalade Game Studio, Days of Wonder, Asmodee","u":"Valve Corporation, Discord, Epic Games, Microsoft Game Studios","g":"Turn-based strategy","r":"November 15, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ticket_to_Ride_(video_game)"},{"t":"Tiger Woods PGA Tour 2005","p":["Windows","GameCube","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"u":"EA Sports","r":"September 20, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tiger_Woods_PGA_Tour_2005"},{"t":"To Heart 2","p":["PlayStation 2"],"g":"Adventure, Visual Novel","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/To_Heart_2","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co660i.jpg","s":"Following her graduation from middle school, Konomi Yuzuhara enters the same high school as Takāki Kono, her childhood friend. As the new school year begins, they meet their childhood friend Tamaki Kosaka, as well as many new accquaintances. Unbeknownst to the group, their encounters with each other will soon lead to many memorable adventures."},{"t":"TOCA Race Driver 2","p":["Windows","Xbox","PlayStation 2"],"r":"April 13","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TOCA_Race_Driver_2"},{"t":"Tokyo Majin Gakuen Gehōchō: Keppūroku","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Marvelous Entertainment","u":"Marvelous Entertainment","g":"Role-playing video game","r":"August 12, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tokyo_Majin_Gakuen_Geh%C5%8Dch%C5%8D:_Kepp%C5%ABroku"},{"t":"Tom Clancy's Ghost Recon 2","p":["Xbox","PlayStation 2"],"d":"Red Storm Entertainment","u":"Ubisoft","g":"Tactical shooter","r":"November 16, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tom_Clancy's_Ghost_Recon_2","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1yhn.jpg","s":"Set in the near future, Tom Clancy's Ghost Recon 2 puts the player in the shoes of a highly trained operative who works as a part of the infamous military unit from the U.S. Special Forces only known as \"Ghosts\".\n\nThe game is set in North Korea, where an evil general is diverting all the humanitarian aid to boost his forces and gain more political power in the process and it's up to Ghosts to eliminate this threat.\n\nThere is a single player campaign mode, where the player as part of the Ghosts, must take on the evil general in 11 different and quite long missions. There is also a multiplayer modes in both on and offline. The main campaign can be played through with a friend, or you can fight other players in multiple game modes spanning from a simple deathmatch to team based modes.\n\nNew to this part of the series is the possibility to use a third person viewpoint, but the classic \"From the eyes\"-view is also available."},{"t":"Tom Clancy's Ghost Recon: Jungle Storm","p":["PlayStation 2","N-Gage"],"d":"Red Storm Entertainment","u":"Ubisoft","g":"Tactical shooter","r":"March 11, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tom_Clancy's_Ghost_Recon:_Jungle_Storm","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1zse.jpg","s":"Tom Clancy's Ghost Recon: Jungle Storm is an expansion of Tom Clancy's Ghost Recon released on the PlayStation 2. It contains the content of Tom Clancy's Ghost Recon: Island Thunder along with eight new single-player missions set in Colombia and additional multiplayer maps."},{"t":"Tom Clancy's Rainbow Six 3: Athena Sword","p":["Windows"],"r":"March 9","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tom_Clancy%27s_Rainbow_Six_3#Athena_Sword"},{"t":"Tom Clancy's Splinter Cell: Pandora Tomorrow","p":["Xbox","Windows","GameCube","PlayStation 2"],"u":"Ubisoft","g":"Action","r":"March 23, 2004","l":"https://store.steampowered.com/app/3929740","i":"images/steam-3929740.jpg","s":"Infiltrate secure locations across the globe in this stealth-action thriller. Uncover a global conspiracy and stop a deadly bio-terror attack in the second game of the award-winning Splinter Cell series."},{"t":"Tony Hawk's Underground 2","p":["Windows","GameCube","PlayStation 2","Xbox","Game Boy Advance"],"r":"October 4","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tony_Hawk%27s_Underground_2"},{"t":"Top Gun: Combat Zones","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"December 1"},{"t":"Torn","p":["Browser"],"d":"Torn LTD","u":"Torn LTD","g":"MMORPG","r":"November 15, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Torn_(2004_video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co8ygh.jpg","s":"\"Torn is a text-based online RPG set in Torn City, a dark, murky underworld where only the sharpest survive. In Torn City you can be anyone and do anything. Build your character to infinite strengths and play it your way.\n\nTorn City is a massively multiplayer game with thousands of active players around the world. Join them, attack them, befriend them, marry them, trade with them, compete with them. Whatever you do - Do it now!\""},{"t":"Transformers","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Atari Melbourne House","u":"Atari","g":"Third-person shooter","r":"May 7, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Transformers_(2004_video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1p3j.jpg","s":"Battle the Decepticons through eight levels as one of three playable Autobots: Optimus Prime, Red Alert, and Hot Shot. Players can transform between robot and vehicle form during the action and collect dozens of Mini-Cons that can be equipped to upgrade their abilities."},{"t":"Transformers: Armada","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Transformers:_Armada"},{"t":"Travian","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Travian"},{"t":"Tribes: Vengeance","p":["Windows"],"r":"October 5"},{"t":"Trigger Man","p":["PlayStation 2","GameCube","Xbox"],"d":"WNT Games","u":"Crave Entertainment, Play-It","g":"Third-person shooter","r":"September 28, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trigger_Man_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co6ufg.jpg","s":"Trigger Man puts you in the shoes of the Underworld's toughest Mob enforcer. To survive all you'll have are your wits, muscle and street-smarts.\nEight challenging missions in which to destroy the operations and soldiers of the rival families. Hunt out your opponents in realistic locations including deserted loading docks, fine restaurants and a casino."},{"t":"Trivial Pursuit: Unhinged","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox","Windows"],"d":"Artech Studios","u":"Atari Interactive","g":"Digital tabletop, quiz","r":"March 26, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trivial_Pursuit:_Unhinged","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/q8ttwxn5olsdxajtz31y.jpg","s":"A popular trivia game is about to become a wild free-for-all. With incredible new game features, this all-new version of the Trivial Pursuit game rewards the clever, the speedy, and the sneaky, while still highlighting everybody's trivia talents. Trivia fans can bet against others, steal wedges and even crush rivals' game pieces (along with their hopes of winning). Add in some impressive Hollywood types hosting each category, and loads of multimedia clips, and you've got a Trivial Pursuit party where everybody is in on the action. For those who crave free-for-all play, the traditional game, or even a quick trivia fix, there are plenty of modes: the Unhinged version, the original classic, and a fast new minigame."},{"t":"Trizeal","p":["Arcade"],"d":"Triangle Service","u":"Taito, Triangle Service, Datam Polystar, BBMF","g":"Scrolling shooter","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trizeal","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3gb6.jpg","s":"A sci-fi vertical-scrolling shooter directly ported from its arcade incarnation.\n\nUsing polygonal graphics, but retaining a completely 2D gameplay, Trizeal puts you in command of two tiny starfighter as you attempt to clear several stages filled with enemy ships and creatures gunning for you.\n\nYour ship is able to morph into three distinct configurations, each with their own speed and armor as well as unique weapon system (basic machine gun, homing missiles and laser), by picking up power-ups you can upgrade each form and increase its abilities and the point of the game is to keep your ship balanced enough to survive in all situations."},{"t":"Tron 2.0","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"October 20","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tron_2.0"},{"t":"TwinBee","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"May 21","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TwinBee"},{"t":"TwinBee Dungeon","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TwinBee_Dungeon"},{"t":"Two Thrones","p":["Windows"],"d":"Paradox Interactive","u":"Strategy First, PAN Vision, Koch Media","g":"Real-time strategy, Grand strategy","r":"January 21, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Two_Thrones","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2rrl.jpg","s":"Two Thrones: From Jean D'Arc to Richard III is a turn-based strategy game that takes place in the years between 1337 and 1490, focusing on the conflicts between England and France. Though based on the Europa Universalis engine, Two Thrones is much smaller in scope and tighter in focus."},{"t":"Ty the Tasmanian Tiger 2: Bush Rescue","p":["Game Boy Advance","GameCube","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"Krome Studios, Halfbrick Studios","u":"EA Games, Krome Studios","g":"Platform","r":"October 12, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ty_the_Tasmanian_Tiger_2:_Bush_Rescue","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2rrm.jpg","s":"STREWTH! It's time to go back Down Under with this fully remastered version of TY the Tasmanian Tiger 2: Bush Rescue. Rang, bite, smash and glide your way around the Australian Outback and stop the evil machinations of the diabolical BOSS CASS in this open world adventure."},{"t":"UEFA Euro 2004","p":["Windows","Xbox","PlayStation 2"],"d":"EA Canada","u":"EA Sports","g":"Sports, Football","r":"May 4, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/UEFA_Euro_2004_(video_game)"},{"t":"UFC: Sudden Impact","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Opus","u":"Global Star, Marvelous Entertainment","g":"Versus fighting, Sports","r":"April 20, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/UFC:_Sudden_Impact","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co5yeg.jpg"},{"t":"Ultimate Card Games","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"d":"Cosmigo","u":"Telegames","g":"Cards","r":"May 25, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ultimate_Card_Games","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/txa5n4igii1nkj0o4sxn.jpg","s":"Ultimate Card Games is a Board game, developed and published by Telegames, Inc., which was released in 2011."},{"t":"Ultra Bust-a-Move","p":["Xbox"],"d":"Dreams Co., Ltd.","u":"Taito, Majesco, 505 GameStreet","g":"Puzzle","r":"November 4, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ultra_Bust-a-Move","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co8sq3.jpg","s":"Puzzle Bobble (Japanese: パズルボブル Hepburn: Pazuru Boburu?), also known as Bust-a-Move in North America, is a 1994 tile-matching arcade puzzle video game for one or two players created by Taito Corporation. It is based on Taito's popular 1986 arcade game Bubble Bobble, featuring characters and themes from that game. Its characteristically cute Japanese animation and music, along with its play mechanics and level designs, made it successful as an arcade title and spawned several sequels and ports to home gaming systems."},{"t":"Ultraman Fighting Evolution 3","p":["PlayStation 2"],"g":"Fighting","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ultraman_Fighting_Evolution_3","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co8yqo.jpg","s":"Ultraman Fighting Evolution 3 (ウルトラマン Fightingファイティング Evolutionエボリューション 3スリー Urutoraman Faitingu Eboryūshon Surī) also called \"Ultraman FE3\" is a Fighting game developed and published by Banpresto. it is the 3rd in the Ultraman Fighting Evolution series. The direction is provided by Yuji Machi, who acted as Ultraman Tiga's voice actor as well."},{"t":"Under the Skin","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"October 14","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Under_the_Skin_(video_game)"},{"t":"Underworld: The Eternal War","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Lucky Chicken Games","u":"Play-It","g":"Action, top-down shooter","r":"January 16, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Underworld:_The_Eternal_War","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4vel.jpg","s":"Underworld: The Eternal War is based on the movie of the same name. The storyline revolves around the eternal war between the vampires and werewolves, and as the player, you can choose the side you're teaming with. You can either choose the movie's heroine Selene, or can be the \"bad guy\" Raze, who is a werewolf.\n\nIt's an all out slugfest as you take on to the battlefields where you must accomplish missions, were they about protecting someone, kill someone, get an item from somewhere, or just kill everyone. The action is the name of the game here and there are lots of it. Using different weapons, you smack the opposition to kingdom come. Many, many times. After that, it's more smacking. And then some."},{"t":"Unreal II: The Awakening","p":["Xbox"],"r":"February 10"},{"t":"Unreal Tournament 2004","p":["Windows"],"u":"Atari","r":"March 16, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unreal_Tournament_2004"},{"t":"Vampire: The Masquerade – Bloodlines","p":["Windows"],"r":"November 16"},{"t":"Van Helsing","p":["Game Boy Advance","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"Saffire","u":"Vivendi Universal Games","g":"Action-adventure, hack and slash","r":"May 7, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Van_Helsing_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1onp.jpg","s":"Van Helsing is a third-person shooter for the PlayStation 2, Xbox, Game Boy Advance and Mobile phone, which is based on the 2004 action/horror film of the same name by Stephen Sommers. Starting off with the killing of Mr. Hyde in Paris, one must use the character of Van Helsing to hunt down Dracula in Transylvania. The character of Carl is completely missing from the video game but to reasonable accuracy, the characters of Anna Valerious, Velkan Valerious, Igor, Dracula and his three brides are portrayed as in the movie."},{"t":"Vendetta Online","p":["Windows","macOS","Linux"],"d":"Guild Software","u":"Strategy First, Guild Software","g":"Massively multiplayer online role-playing, space trading and combat simulator","r":"November 4, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vendetta_Online","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2fb5.jpg","s":"Vendetta Online is a 3D space combat MMORPG for Windows, Mac, Linux, Android and iOS, as well as the Oculus Rift. This MMO permits thousands of players to interact as the pilots of spaceships in a vast universe. Users may build their characters in any direction they desire, becoming rich captains of industry, military heroes, or outlaws. A fast-paced, realtime \"twitch\" style combat model gives intense action, coupled with the backdrop of RPG gameplay in a massive online galaxy. Three major player factions form a delicate balance of power, with several NPC sub-factions creating situations of economic struggle, political intrigue and conflict. The completely persistent universe and detailed storyline add to the depth of immersion, resulting in a unique online experience."},{"t":"Vib-Ripple","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"NanaOn-Sha","u":"Sony Computer Entertainment","g":"Action","r":"May 27, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vib-Ripple","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co5pi0.jpg","s":"Vib Ripple is the sequel to Vib Ribbon, and the third in the Vib Ribbon series. While Vib Ribbon was based around the tone of music, and Mojib Ribbon was based around lyrics, Vib Ripple is themed around drums and percussion.\n\nPlayers once again control the vector rabbit Vibri as they play. This time, they must move her around a gigantic picture (think of the picture as a giant trampoline), and use the any of the face buttons to make her jump. If you time the jumps to the beat of the music, Vibri will jump higher, and jumping on certain parts of the picture will reveal 'Peta Characters' - 2D representations of objects, such as bunny rabbits, onions, and presents. The goal of each level is to reveal the Peta Characters shown in the crown at the bottom left of the screen (of course, you can uncover more if you're game).\n\nIn later levels, blobby enemies known as 'Boonchies' turn up and begin to slowly zero in on Vibri. She must dodge these enemies in addition to bouncing in time to the beat as she uncovers Peta Characters.\n\nVib Ripple, like Vib Ribbon and Mojib Ribbon, allows players to extend their potential playtime. You can create new levels by hooking up certain USB cameras and mobile phones, and uploading photos to your PS2. However, as with the previous games, the preset levels seem to work the best."},{"t":"Victorious Boxers 2: Fighting Spirit","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"New Corporation","u":"Entertainment Software Publishing, Empire Interactive","g":"Sports, Fighting game","r":"December 22, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Victorious_Boxers_2:_Fighting_Spirit","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/coa4s6.jpg","s":"The follow-up to Victorious Boxers features a new \"coach\" fighter-creation mode and a whole training gym's worth of new moves and boxers."},{"t":"Vietcong: Fist Alpha","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"January 28"},{"t":"Viewtiful Joe","p":["PlayStation 2"],"u":"Capcom","r":"August 24, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Viewtiful_Joe_(video_game)"},{"t":"Viewtiful Joe 2","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"December 8","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Viewtiful_Joe_2"},{"t":"W Wish","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/W_Wish"},{"t":"Wade Hixton's Counter Punch","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"March 15","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wade_Hixton%27s_Counter_Punch"},{"t":"War in the Pacific","p":["Windows"],"d":"2 by 3 Games","u":"Matrix Games","g":"Computer wargame","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/War_in_the_Pacific_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/tyhdu3vw2j4teexeaihk.jpg","s":"War in the Pacific: The Struggle Against Japan 1941-1945 is a classic strategy game, based on the award winning Uncommon Valor game engine. The scale is 60 miles per hex and losses are individual vehicles, aircraft, guns and squads. Since half the planet Earth is covered by the titanic Pacific struggle, the game is massive in scope, covering thousands of ships tens of thousands of aircraft."},{"t":"War Times","p":["Windows"],"d":"Legend Studios","g":"Real-time strategy","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/War_Times","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/eavyc8vqxkkasn2rpwi0.jpg","s":"War Times - During the years of World War II, each nation adopted unique strategies for defense. Now you can try these strategies in a series of campaigns based on historical battles and events of the war. Follow the actions of the European war, as seen by Germany, Great Britain, the USA or the USSR. Powerful multiplayer and cooperative gameplay -- you can even share Allied units with other players"},{"t":"Warhammer 40,000: Dawn of War","p":["Windows"],"r":"September 20"},{"t":"WarioWare: Twisted!","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"u":"Nintendo","r":"October 14, 2004"},{"t":"Warlords Battlecry III","p":["Windows"],"d":"Infinite Interactive","u":"Enlight Software","g":"Real-time strategy","r":"May 19, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Warlords_Battlecry_III","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1rhb.jpg","s":"Warlords Battlecry III further expands the Battlecry tradition of featuring persistent RPG-like fantasy heroes with its retinue of loyal followers fighting massive battles in the Warlords' world of Etheria. It is a true sequel to Warlords Battlecry I & II, featuring many familiar races and troop-types, while also adding some new ones into the mix.\n\nWarlords Battlecry III continue to perfect its automated feature system, greatly reducing gameplay micromanagement and quickly proving to be the holy grail of RTS games among gamers of the genre.\n\nWhile being a strong RTS outright, there are also numerous activities for players to engage in between battles, such as obtaining titles and awards, trading and purchasing items & retinue members, and even an upgradeable castle to reflect your importance and influence in the world of Etheria.\n\nExtra features included in Warlords Battlecry III are specifically geared to please the legions of previous Battlecry players, including the removal of hero and unit caps, the addition of new special abilities for high-level heroes and the creation of an intuitive hero system. All of these features, coupled with new races and hero classes, new spells and items, and new building and dragons meld to form a Real-Time Strategy game that once again raises the benchmark for other games in the genre. Warlords Battlecry III is poised to receive even greater accolades than the previous award-winning titles in the Warlords Battlecry series."},{"t":"Wars and Warriors: Joan of Arc","p":["Windows"],"d":"Enlight","u":"Enlight","g":"Action, Real-Time Strategy","r":"February 10, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wars_and_Warriors:_Joan_of_Arc","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co5tu1.jpg","s":"The year is 1337. During this, the darkest of ages, the bubonic plague was rampant. Kingdoms rose and fell with every swift blow of the sword. The Old Continent was in a state of great upheaval, as English kings hastily attempted time and again to uphold their claim to the French throne, shaking this fragile kingdom to its very foundation. The hundred years' war had been unleashed.\n\nRelive the most intense battle scenarios of medieval Europe in this third-person 3D epic saga. Brandish your sword as you slay enemies amidst adrenaline-pumping action while you lead your troops to victory. Acquire new weaponry while you advance through eight massively gut-wrenching battle scenarios, each packed to the hilt with thousands of enemy troops to slay. Gain experience to obtain and unleash ever-more powerful combo attacks to devastate your foes. Slowly transform yourself from a single warrior into a forceful military leader as you develop and master the art of chivalry and tactical warfare. Become the greatest and most inspirational of French leaders by demonstrating your leadership abilities while commanding your legions of troops to victory. Tap into your arsenal of war machines as you relentlessly tear away at enemy forces.\n\nPlay as Joan of Arc: Live out the most exciting years in the life of Joan of Arc, the ultimate female warrior, in the ultimate epic battles! As you progress through her campaigns, other great military medieval leaders will join your cause and bring their own unique fighting abilities and characteristics into the fray.\n\nFight Epic Battles: Orchestrate your troops through eight massive maps featuring formidable strongholds, lavishly detailed cities and myriad landscapes, from rolling hills to thick forests and flowing rivers. Experience firsthand the sheer intensity and savage brutality of medieval castle sieges brought to life in amazing lifelike 3D.\n\nEngage in Adrenaline-pumping Action: Slash and slay enemies from a thrilling third-person perspective view. Wield the sword to your advantage by executing unique combo attacks with perfect timing to devastate the enemy.\n\nAcquire New Weapons: Train yourself to master new fighting techniques to unleash your full fighting capabilities, then acquire an increasingly devastating arsenal of weaponry to overwhelm your foes.\n\nMaster Long-Lost Skills: Demonstrate your chivalrous aptitude by mastering your timing and precision among dozens of unique attack combos. Train yourself to become the complete warrior.\n\nStrategically Command Entire Armies: Valiantly marshal your troops through the thick of gut-wrenching battles and demonstrate your leadership abilities as generalissimo to your troops, country, and king.\n\nEmploy Fearsome War Machines: Use to your advantage the devastating war machines at hand, such as catapult, trebuchet and battering ram to tear down castle walls, vanquish enemy fortifications, and instill fear in the eyes of your enemies."},{"t":"Way of the Samurai 2","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"May 21","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Way_of_the_Samurai_2"},{"t":"Wik and the Fable of Souls","p":["Windows"],"d":"Reflexive Entertainment","u":"Reflexive Entertainment","g":"Platform game","r":"September 14, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wik_and_the_Fable_of_Souls"},{"t":"Wings of Power","p":["Windows"],"d":"Shockwave Productions","u":"Tri Synergy","g":"Flight simulation","r":"September 13, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wings_of_Power"},{"t":"Wings of Power: WWII Heavy Bombers and Jets","p":["Windows"],"u":"Tri Synergy","r":"September 13, 2004"},{"t":"Wings of War","p":["Windows","Xbox"],"d":"Silver Wish Games","u":"Gathering","g":"Combat flight simulator","r":"July 30, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wings_of_War_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/coat9n.jpg","s":"Wings of War is a Flight Simulator developed by Silver Wish Games and published by Gathering of Developers. The game was a standard wartime flight simulator with the underused setting of World War I. Players assume the role of a Royal Air Force pilot fighting the Luftstreitkräfte in several missions. Despite its setting, the game still features an arcade style to it: the planes never stalled and the planes could be equipped with air-to-air rockets."},{"t":"Wings over Vietnam","p":["Windows"],"d":"Third Wire","u":"Destineer, Bold Games","g":"Combat flight simulator","r":"November 8, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wings_over_Vietnam"},{"t":"World Championship Poker","p":["PlayStation 2","Game Boy Advance","Xbox"],"d":"Coresoft, Point of View","u":"Crave Entertainment, Play It, Oxygen Games, 505 Games","g":"Cards","r":"November 3, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_Championship_Poker","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4z9e.jpg","s":"World Championship Poker offers the most challenging, most realistic poker game play around. Compete against top players for a seat at the Grand Championship Table -- call their bluffs, know when to hold 'em and when to fold 'em, and try to make it to the final showdown!"},{"t":"World Championship Rugby","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"Swordfish Studios","u":"Acclaim Entertainment","g":"Rugby union","r":"April 8, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_Championship_Rugby","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/ttxgl2j6pbadiwoo4h2p.jpg","s":"World Championship Rugby is a computer and video game developed after the 2003 Rugby World Cup. It was developed by Swordfish Studios and published by Acclaim. \n \nAs well as all the teams and games from the 2003 Rugby World Cup, the game includes a number of other tournaments, such as Six Nations, Tri Nations, custom leagues and cups, classic matches and tour games. There is also a feature to beat the all- stars with every team in the game and a survival game. The only licensed teams in the game are England and Wales, however, included is a name editor that allows the fake player names to be changed."},{"t":"World Championship Snooker 2004","p":["PlayStation 2","Windows","Xbox"],"d":"Blade Interactive","u":"Codemasters","g":"Sports","r":"June 25, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_Championship_Snooker_2004_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4eol.jpg","s":"World Championship Snooker 2004 is a sports video game developed by Blade Interactive and published by Codemasters. The game features Career, Quick Play and Trickshot modes. It also includes eight-ball, nine-ball, and blackball pool."},{"t":"World of Warcraft","p":["Windows"],"u":"Blizzard Entertainment","r":"November 23, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_of_Warcraft"},{"t":"Worms Forts: Under Siege","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"Team17","u":"Sega","g":"Artillery, strategy","r":"November 19, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Worms_Forts:_Under_Siege","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1xmc.jpg","s":"Worms Forts: Under Siege is a turn based strategy game by Team 17 which worms must destroy the enemy team or their stronghold"},{"t":"Worms Golf","p":["Mobile phone"],"d":"Rockpool Games","u":"THQ","g":"Sports","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Worms_Golf"},{"t":"Wrath Unleashed","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"February 10","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wrath_Unleashed"},{"t":"WRC 4","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Evolution Studios","u":"SCEE, Spike","g":"Racing","r":"October 22, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/WRC_4","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co9y8n.jpg","s":"WRC4 is the fourth installment to the officially licenced FIA World Rally Championship series. It features all the cars, tracks and drivers from the real world 2004 season."},{"t":"Wrecking Crew","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"May 21","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wrecking_Crew_(video_game)"},{"t":"WWE Day of Reckoning","p":["GameCube"],"r":"August 30","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/WWE_Day_of_Reckoning"},{"t":"WWE SmackDown! vs. Raw","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Yuke's","u":"THQ, Yuke's","g":"Sports","r":"November 2, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/WWE_SmackDown!_vs._Raw","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/coarq1.jpg","s":"WWE SmackDown! vs. Raw brings two of wrestling's most popular game series together on the PS2. The game re-creates WWE programming with voice-overs and commentary throughout the season mode. During matches, you can learn a host of new gameplay moves, such as stare-downs, chop battles, and submission reversals. You can also try out situational challenges or create your own championship. Play as your favorite wrestler, including legends and Divas, and prove to the world that you have what it takes to be the WWE champion."},{"t":"WWE Survivor Series","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"d":"Natsume Co., Ltd.","u":"THQ","g":"Professional wrestling","r":"October 21, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/WWE_Survivor_Series_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co9yur.jpg","s":"Get in the ring with the WWE's top superstars in WWE Survivor Series for the Game Boy Advance. Fight up through the ranks and challenge for the belts to become the champion in the all-new single-player mode. Turn the tables on the battle with the new reversal system and momentum shifts. WWE superstars feature their true-to-life attributes in strength, speed and submission skills -- the only difference between you and the champion is a three count. WWE Survivor Series features all-new gameplay mechanics including submission, reversal and momentum systems as players battle for the belts and defend the title in the new single-player mode or link up with friends to battle in eight match types, including Cage, Tag Team, Fatal 4 Way and more."},{"t":"WWF Panda Junior","p":["Windows"],"g":"Educational, adventure","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/WWF_Panda_Junior","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1hd8.jpg","s":"Play as Alex or Emma as you discover the African continent in this educational WWF-endorsed game, the first in the Safari Adventure series - dedicated to an audience from 6 to 9 years old. Guided by the little WWF Panda and a forest ranger, you journey around and meet lots of different animals. Unfortunately, baddies such as the hunter Mr Mank and tourist Mr Rashburn will try to stop you from progressing."},{"t":"X-Men Legends","p":["GameCube","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"Raven Software","u":"Activision","g":"Action role-playing","r":"September 21, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/X-Men_Legends","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1pez.jpg","s":"X-Men enter the realm of role-playing games with an intense story, superhero action, and multiplayer modes. The story in X-Men Legends begins when the X-Men learn that Magneto has devised a plan to give mutants the power to reign supreme over humans. To save the human race from imprisonment, you compose a four-person team from a roster of X-Men characters, including Storm, Gambit, and Wolverine."},{"t":"Xenosaga Episode II","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Monolith Soft","u":"Namco, Sony Computer Entertainment","g":"Role-playing","r":"June 24, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Xenosaga_Episode_II"},{"t":"Xenosaga: Pied Piper","p":["Mobile phone"],"d":"Monolith Soft, Namco, Tom Create","u":"Namco","g":"Role-playing","r":"July 14, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Xenosaga:_Pied_Piper","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2ppo.jpg","s":"Xenosaga: Pied Piper is a role-playing video game co-developed by Monolith Soft, Namco Mobile, and Tom Create. The game was published by Namco in 2004 for mobile devices.\n\nThe game was only released in Japan, originally in 2004 as 6 Vodafone apps, starting on July 14th and fully released on October 13th. They were available as 3 chapter purchases, each split into 2 parts released within weeks of each other.\nThe game was made available for i-mode devices on July 6th 2006, through Namco's monthly subscription service."},{"t":"Xevious","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"February 14","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Xevious"},{"t":"XII Stag","p":["Arcade","PlayStation 2"],"d":"Triangle Service, Dreams","u":"Taito, 505 Game Street","g":"Shoot 'em up","r":"April 2, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/XII_Stag"},{"t":"Xpand Rally","p":["Windows"],"d":"Techland","u":"TopWare Interactive","g":"Racing","r":"September 24, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Xpand_Rally","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3l9f.jpg","s":"Xpand Rally is a breathtaking game that gives you the true to life experience of driving powerful rally cars amidst photorealistic sceneries. Realistic weather effects, rolling hills, and animated scenery all add to game's visual perfection. Xpand Rally also features highly detailed models of modern rally cars and handling physics developed with the help of rally sport professionals which further enhance the realism of driving experience."},{"t":"XS Junior League Soccer","p":["PlayStation"],"d":"Wahoo Studios","u":"XS Games","g":"Sports","r":"September 29, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/XS_Junior_League_Soccer","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/ahpwejixe66utmsey0kj.jpg","s":"XS Jr. League Soccer is designed to provide a fun, pick-up-and-play adaptation of the world's most popular sport, with colorful graphics and accessible gameplay for the whole family to enjoy.\n\nSelect Your Team: 20 individual players. Everybody can really play. Players have different skill levels. 8000 different 5-a-side combos. Schoolyard Tournaments: Put a strong team together; play an entire round robin tournament in one day. 4 Real World Fields: The School Yard, Sandpit, Car Park, Southside."},{"t":"Yourself!Fitness","p":["Xbox","Windows"],"d":"Respondesign, Ubisoft","u":"Respondesign, Ubisoft","g":"Exergaming","r":"October 8, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yourself!Fitness","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/cobocl.jpg","s":"Yourself!Fitness brings the expertise of a certified personal trainer and nutritionist to your home. Maya, your virtual personal trainer, helps you to choose health and fitness goals and then works with you to achieve them. The game enables you to choose from over 500 unique exercises and to create a customized meal plan with over 4500 recipes. The game is capable of integrating popular fitness equipment into your workout options."},{"t":"Yu Yu Hakusho: Dark Tournament","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Digital Fiction","u":"Atari","g":"Fighting","r":"September 28, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yu_Yu_Hakusho:_Dark_Tournament"},{"t":"Yu Yu Hakusho: Tournament Tactics","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"November 18"},{"t":"Yu-Gi-Oh! Destiny Board Traveler","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"October 26","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yu-Gi-Oh!_Destiny_Board_Traveler"},{"t":"Yu-Gi-Oh! Power of Chaos: Joey the Passion","p":["Windows"],"r":"July 2"},{"t":"Yu-Gi-Oh! The Dawn of Destiny","p":["Xbox"],"d":"Konami Computer Entertainment Japan","u":"Konami","g":"Digital collectible card game","r":"March 23, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yu-Gi-Oh!_The_Dawn_of_Destiny","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co5txz.jpg","s":"Yu-Gi-Oh! The Dawn of Destiny is a strategy video game with over 1,000 Yu-Gi-Oh! cards that integrates the trading card gameplay and rules with 3D monster battles. Players engage in strategic duels against AI opponents, exploring various game modes including Link Duel and Triple Duel modes, which offer fresh challenges and test players' skills against multiple opponents simultaneously."},{"t":"Yu-Gi-Oh! World Championship Tournament 2004","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"February 10","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yu-Gi-Oh!_World_Championship_Tournament_2004"},{"t":"Yume Nikki","p":["Windows"],"d":"Kikiyama","u":"Kikiyama, Playism","g":"Adventure, walking simulator, art game","r":"June 26, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yume_Nikki","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co81f2.jpg","s":"Yume Nikki is a 32-Bit freeware game created by Kikiyama, a Japanese solo game designer. The game was made using RPGMaker 2003. The game is regarded as one of the most original applications of RPGMaker 2003, and the start of a possible new genre of games.\n\n\"Yume Nikki\" means \"Dream Diary\" in Japanese, and the game follows a young girl named Madotsuki as she dreams. The goal is to seek out and acquire all 24 'Effects'.\n\nThe game otherwise has no plot, and nearly the entire game is left up to speculation."},{"t":"Zatch Bell! Mamodo Fury","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Mechanic Arms","u":"Bandai, Namco Bandai Games","g":"Fighting","r":"December 2, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zatch_Bell!_Mamodo_Fury","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co730o.jpg","s":"Zatch Bell! Mamodo Fury is a fighting game released by Bandai in 2004. In 2006 the game was released in North America by Namco Bandai Games, and a GameCube port was released exclusively there."},{"t":"Zelda II: The Adventure of Link","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"August 10"},{"t":"Zoids Infinity","p":["Arcade"],"d":"Taito","u":"Taito","g":"Rail shooter","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zoids_Infinity"},{"t":"Zoids Vs. III","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zoids_Vs._III"},{"t":"Zoo Empire","p":["Windows"],"d":"Enlight Software","u":"Enlight Software","g":"Construction and management simulation","r":"August 4, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zoo_Empire","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/cod0n2.jpg","s":"It's a zoo out there, and you're in charge! Go wild with your imagination running the most exotic, fun and exciting zoo ever. Tend to your animals' health, happiness and nutrition by hiring employees, and adopt new animals as you unlock the numerous features hidden within the game. Attend to visitors by providing facilities for them to eat, drink and buy souvenirs from as they revel in your zoo.\n\nSporting flexible gameplay, choose from either the sandbox mode where you establish the rules of the game, or accept the challenge of graduating from rookie zookeeper to wildlife whiz in the challenging career mode!\n\nKeep your animals, employees and visitors happy, keep the money rolling in, and path by path, animal by animal, exhibit by exhibit, build your very own Zoo Empire!"},{"t":"Zoo Tycoon 2","p":["Windows"],"d":"Blue Fang Games, Rapan","u":"Microsoft Game Studios","g":"Business simulation","r":"November 9, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zoo_Tycoon_2","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co8z9n.jpg","s":"Zoo Tycoon 2 is the sequel to Zoo Tycoon. The sequel updates the graphics, but keeps much of the original gameplay the same.\n\nYou start with an open field and must build it up into a zoo. Create exhibits and populate them with animals. Build amenities and concession stands to keep visitors happy in between exhibits. Happy visitors will donate more money to your zoo so you can make it better. However, you have much more freedom in exhibit creation. You don't even need fences; a moat or ditch will suffice, as this technique is popular at real high profile zoos. There are also more animals and attractions to place in your zoo, and animal habitats look as realistic as the cartoony graphics style will allow."},{"t":"Zoo Vet","p":["Windows"],"d":"Legacy Games","u":"Legacy Games","g":"Simulation","r":"December 1, 2004","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zoo_Vet","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/cobglz.jpg","s":"Lions, tigers and bears... oh, my! In this game you'll get up close and personal with wild animals, because you are one of their doctors! Assume the role of a zoo veterinarian where you can pet, talk to and treat all types of animals in need of help. Every type of animal imaginable is a guest at this world-class zoo and you'll have the opportunity to meet dozens of them in Zoo Vet.\n\nThere are several difficulty modes to choose from. You'll receive help along the way from zookeepers and other veterinarians on staff. Look up facts and play animal trivia to learn more about all of the animals. Earn up to 1,000 per case. The number of points determines what trophies and awards you win. If you do well enough, you will unlock more challenging cases and the praise of your co-workers. Win the game by getting a permanent job at the zoo.\n\nTravel to each of the animal habitats to perform examinations and evaluate the problems. Use 40 medically-accurate tools - even perform surgeries when needed! Go back to your office to relax, play bonus mini-games or to do research.\n\nThe game features a simple point-and-click interface, rendered 3D graphics and voices by real actors and actresses. Zoo Vet is a family-oriented game for all ages."}];
